      "correctText": "parallel lines",
      "topic": "Comparison Skills",
      "explanation": "Parallel lines have equal slopes. Worked example: y=2x+3 and y=2x-5 are parallel — both slope 2, never intersect. NY G-GPE.5 in geometry connects to Algebra 1 slope work. The system formed by two parallel lines has no solution (consistent with the 'no solution' system case). Regents items often ask for the equation of a line parallel to a given one through a specified point — use the given slope and point-slope form.",
