      "correctText": "perpendicular lines",
      "topic": "Comparison Skills",
      "explanation": "Perpendicular slopes multiply to -1. Worked example: y=2x+1 and y=(-1/2)x+4 are perpendicular because 2 * (-1/2) = -1. NY G-GPE.5 introduces this in algebra context. To find a perpendicular line through a point, flip the slope and change its sign, then use point-slope form. Regents items frequently test this — a common wrong answer uses only the reciprocal without changing sign or only the sign without reciprocal.",
