      "correctText": "box plot",
      "topic": "Data Displays",
      "explanation": "Box plots show spread and skewness. Worked example: data 1, 3, 5, 7, 8, 10, 12, 15, 18, 20 has min=1, Q1=5, median=9, Q3=15, max=20 — box from 5 to 15 with median line at 9. NY S-ID.1-2 covers box plots. IQR = Q3-Q1 = 10 shows middle 50% range. Regents items compare two box plots side-by-side to discuss center, spread, and skew.",
