      "correctText": "two-way table",
      "topic": "Data Displays",
      "explanation": "Two-way tables organize categorical data. Worked example: 50 students surveyed on coffee/tea by gender — table cells show counts in each combination. Marginal frequencies are row/column totals; conditional frequencies are row or column percentages. NY S-ID.5 covers two-way tables. Regents items ask 'What percent of females prefer tea?' — divide the cell value by the female row total.",
