      "correctText": "dot plot",
      "topic": "Data Displays",
      "explanation": "Dot plots show small data sets directly. Worked example: ages 5, 5, 6, 6, 6, 7, 8, 8 plot as a stack of two dots above 5, three above 6, one above 7, two above 8. NY S-ID.1 covers dot plots. Easy to read mode (highest stack), shape (symmetric or skewed), and outliers (isolated dots). Regents items use dot plots for small data sets, often asking for measures of center or to compare distributions.",
