      "choices": [
        "x-intercept",
        "growth factor",
        "decay factor",
        "initial value"
      ],
      "correctText": "decay factor",
      "topic": "Exponential Structure",
      "explanation": "Decay factor is the base below 1. Worked example: 8% annual decline has factor 0.92; halving per period has factor 0.5. NY F-LE.5 covers this. From a factor, recover the rate: factor 0.93 means 7% decay (r=0.07). Regents items use this for depreciation (cars, equipment), radioactive decay, and medicine clearance. Each period multiplies by the factor, producing exponential decline that approaches zero but never reaches it.",
      "domain": "Review",
