      "correctText": "growth factor",
      "topic": "Exponential Structure",
      "explanation": "Growth factor is the base above 1. Worked example: a 7% annual growth has factor 1.07; a doubling per year has factor 2. NY F-LE.5 covers this. From a factor, recover the rate: factor 1.12 means 12% growth (r=0.12). Regents items use compound growth in interest, populations, and biological models. The factor multiplies each period, producing exponential growth that beats any linear function eventually.",
      "domain": "Review",
