      "prompt": "The set of all output values a function can produce, dependent on the domain and the function rule.",
      "choices": [
        "independent variable",
        "perpendicular lines",
        "domain",
        "range"
      ],
      "correctText": "range",
      "topic": "Graph Features",
      "explanation": "Range is the output set. Worked example: f(x)=x^2 with domain all reals has range y is greater-than-or-equal 0 because squares are non-negative. NY F-IF.5 covers range interpretation. For linear functions over a restricted domain like 0 less-than-or-equal x less-than-or-equal 10, plug in the endpoints to find range bounds (e.g., y=2x+1 gives range 1 less-than-or-equal y less-than-or-equal 21). Regents items expect range stated with the correct inequality symbols and endpoint inclusion.",
