      "explanation": "Compound inequalities with AND produce intersections (overlap), and with OR produce unions. Worked example: -2 less-than-or-equal x<5 means x is between -2 and 5, including -2 but excluding 5. NY A-REI.3 includes compound forms. Regents items often display number-line graphs; the student must write the matching compound inequality. The OR form like x<-1 OR x>4 produces two separate rays — never collapse it into a single conjoined statement.",
