      "correctText": "constant ratio",
      "topic": "Linear Comparison",
      "explanation": "Constant ratio is the multiplicative step. Worked example: for 2, 6, 18, 54, the constant ratio is 3 because each term is three times the previous. NY F-LE.1 covers identification. Verify by checking multiple consecutive ratios. Regents items test geometric vs arithmetic distinction — if ratios are constant (and differences are not), the sequence is geometric with that ratio.",
