      "correctText": "verbal model",
      "topic": "Multiple Representations",
      "explanation": "Verbal models bridge English and algebra. Worked example: 'A car starts at 50 mph and slows by 2 mph each second' translates to v(t)=50-2t. NY A-CED.1-2 covers this translation. Regents items provide a paragraph context and ask students to (a) write an equation, (b) compute a specific value, (c) interpret a parameter, and (d) state appropriate domain. Identify rate words (per, each), initial value words (starts, begins), and units.",
      "domain": "Review",
