      "explanation": "Projectile motion uses standard physics quadratic. Worked example: a ball launched from 5 ft with initial velocity 64 ft/s — h(t) = -16t^2+64t+5. Vertex t = -64/(2*-16) = 2 s, max height h(2) = -64+128+5 = 69 ft. NY F-IF.4 and A-CED.2 cover this. Regents items routinely use this model. The -16 coefficient comes from half the acceleration of gravity. Set h(t)=0 to find when the object lands.",
