      "correctText": "population",
      "topic": "Regents Claims",
      "explanation": "Population is the target group. Worked example: all registered voters in New York is a population; a 1000-voter poll is a sample from it. NY S-IC.1 covers this distinction. Inference moves from sample (computed statistics) to population (unknown parameters). Regents items state a question (e.g., 'What percent of all 11th graders study at least 2 hours?') and assess whether a sample is appropriate to answer it.",
