      "correctText": "sign error",
      "topic": "Regents Error Analysis",
      "explanation": "Sign errors are the most common Algebra 1 mistake. Worked example: -2(x-3) should distribute to -2x+6, not -2x-6 (flipping the inside negative). NY A-SSE.2 and A-REI.1 require careful sign tracking. Regents items often include traps where students miss the sign change — always rewrite subtraction as adding a negative if confusion arises. Check work by substituting a value back into the original.",
