      "explanation": "Rounding instructions are mandatory. Worked example: if the answer is 3.4567 and the instruction is 'to the nearest hundredth', report 3.46. Rounding to a different precision loses the precision point. NY embeds rounding into problems requiring real-world answers (money to the nearest cent, distances to the nearest tenth of a mile). Regents items lose points for both wrong rounding AND for forgetting to round. Read the question's last sentence carefully for the precision.",
