      "prompt": "A straight-line plot of a function on the coordinate plane, with constant slope and one y-intercept.",
      "choices": [
        "rounding instruction",
        "function notation",
        "linear graph",
        "table of values"
      ],
      "correctText": "linear graph",
      "topic": "Representations",
      "explanation": "Linear graphs are non-vertical straight lines. Worked example: graph y=(1/2)x-3 by plotting (0,-3), moving right 2 and up 1 to (2,-2), and drawing the line. NY F-IF.7 requires graphing linear functions. Regents items show a graph and ask for the equation, or vice versa. Confirm linearity by checking that the slope is constant between any pair of marked points — if not, the graph is not linear.",
