      "prompt": "A two-column listing of paired inputs and outputs, used to identify the constant difference that indicates a linear function.",
      "choices": [
        "table of values",
        "linear graph",
        "initial value",
        "verbal model"
      ],
      "correctText": "table of values",
      "topic": "Representations",
      "explanation": "Tables reveal linearity through constant first differences in y when x changes by 1. Worked example: x=1,2,3,4 yields y=5,8,11,14 — differences 3,3,3, so the function is linear with slope 3 and y-intercept 2 (extrapolate back to x=0). NY F-IF.7 and F-LE.1 use tables to identify function type. Regents items present a table and ask students to write the equation; compute slope from any two points then back-solve for b.",
