      "correctText": "scientific notation",
      "topic": "Scientific Notation",
      "explanation": "Scientific notation compresses extreme values. Worked example: 3,400,000 = 3.4 * 10^6 and 0.0000072 = 7.2 * 10^-6. NY 8.EE.3-4 requires writing and operating with scientific notation. The mantissa a must satisfy 1 is less-than-or-equal |a| < 10 (so 34 * 10^5 is not in scientific notation; rewrite as 3.4 * 10^6). Regents items test conversion both directions and arithmetic operations with scientific notation.",
      "domain": "Review",
