      "correctText": "standard notation",
      "topic": "Scientific Notation",
      "explanation": "Standard notation spells out the value. Worked example: 4.5 * 10^4 in standard notation is 45,000. 6.2 * 10^-3 is 0.0062. NY 8.EE.4 includes conversion. Move the decimal point n places right for positive exponent, left for negative. Regents items provide scientific notation and ask for the standard form, or vice versa — count zeros carefully. Common error: confusing direction for negative exponents (decimal moves left, value gets smaller).",
