      "correctText": "order of magnitude",
      "topic": "Scientific Notation",
      "explanation": "Order of magnitude compares scale. Worked example: 4.2 * 10^7 (ten million) is three orders of magnitude larger than 5.1 * 10^4 (fifty thousand) because 10^7 / 10^4 = 10^3 = 1000 times bigger. NY 8.EE.3 covers this comparison. Regents items present two scientific-notation values and ask 'How many times larger is X than Y?' — subtract exponents to get the order-of-magnitude difference.",
