      "prompt": "The verification step of substituting both x and y values back into both original equations to confirm the proposed solution.",
      "choices": [
        "checking ordered pair",
        "substitution method",
        "matrix display",
        "graph interpretation"
      ],
      "correctText": "checking ordered pair",
      "topic": "Solving Methods",
      "explanation": "Checking confirms accuracy. Worked example: claimed solution (3, 2) for 2x+y=8 and x-y=1; check: 2(3)+2=8 (true) and 3-2=1 (true), confirmed. NY A-REI.6 expects verification. Regents 2-point items often award one point for correct answer and one for the check. A common error: checking only one equation — both must be verified because the ordered pair must satisfy the entire system simultaneously.",
      "domain": "Review",
