      "explanation": "Always substitute to verify. Worked example: for 2x+5=13 check x=4 by computing 2(4)+5=13 (true). NY A-REI.1 makes checking part of justification. Regents Part II (2-point) items award one point for the correct value and one for showing the check or full algebraic work. Forgetting to check loses points on rational and radical equations where extraneous answers (values that satisfy the derived form but not the original) are introduced.",
