      "correctText": "square root method",
      "topic": "Turning Points",
      "explanation": "Square root method works on isolated squared terms. Worked example: (x-3)^2 = 16 — take square root: x-3 = plus or minus 4, so x = 3 plus or minus 4 = 7 or -1. NY A-REI.4 includes this method. Don't forget the plus or minus — both roots must be reported. Regents items often present equations already in the form (x-h)^2=k or convert into this form via completing the square.",
