      "correctText": "model limitation",
      "topic": "Constructed Response",
      "explanation": "Model limitations are explicit statements about where the model fails (S-ID.6 application). Required on constructed-response items asking for interpretation. Examples: extrapolation risk ('valid only within the observed time range'), unrealistic assumptions ('assumes constant growth rate'), domain restrictions ('only for positive time'), and physical constraints ('population cannot exceed carrying capacity'). On the Algebra 2 Regents, recognizing limitations is rewarded with full credit; ignoring them loses credit. Example: a linear model of weight loss may predict negative weight if extrapolated; a sinusoidal tide model assumes perfect periodicity but real tides vary. Always mention at least one limitation when asked to evaluate a model.",
