      "explanation": "A percentile is the value below which a given percentage of data falls (S-ID.4). The kth percentile is the value Pk such that k% of data is ≤Pk. The 25th, 50th, and 75th percentiles are the quartiles Q1, Q2, Q3. Q2 is the median. Example: a score in the 90th percentile is higher than 90% of scores. For a normal distribution: invNorm(0.90, μ, σ) gives the 90th percentile. Used in standardized test reporting (SAT/ACT percentile ranks), growth charts, salary distributions. On the Algebra 2 Regents, percentile computations use calculator's invNorm and connect to z-scores via percentile = P(Z<z).",
