      "correctText": "branch of graph",
      "topic": "Function Behavior",
      "explanation": "A branch is a connected piece of a discontinuous graph (F-IF.7d). The function y=1/x has two branches: one in quadrant I (x>0, y>0) and one in quadrant III (x<0, y<0), separated by the asymptotes x=0 and y=0. Rational functions in general have multiple branches separated by vertical asymptotes. For y=1/(x-2)+3, branches are in regions x<2 and x>2, separated by vertical asymptote x=2 and approaching horizontal asymptote y=3. On the Algebra 2 Regents, branch behavior is examined in graphing items and in describing function behavior on different intervals of the domain.",
