      "explanation": "The base b in exponential y=a·bˣ is the growth factor: y is multiplied by b each time x increases by 1 (F-IF.8b). b>1: growth (b=1.05 = 5% growth rate). 0<b<1: decay (b=0.85 = 15% decay rate per period). b is computed as the constant ratio between consecutive y-values: b=y(x+1)/y(x). On the Algebra 2 Regents, students interpret b in context: in P(t)=5000(1.03)ᵗ for population growth, b=1.03 corresponds to 3% annual growth rate. In V(t)=25000(0.88)ᵗ for car depreciation, b=0.88 corresponds to 12% annual depreciation. Growth rate r relates to b by r=b-1 (positive for growth, negative for decay).",
