      "correctText": "square root function",
      "topic": "Parent Functions",
      "explanation": "The square-root parent function f(x)=√x is the inverse of y=x² restricted to x≥0 (F-IF.7b). Domain is x≥0; range is y≥0. The graph begins at (0,0) and increases without bound but with decreasing steepness. Transformations: y=√(x-2)+1 starts at (2,1). To solve √(x+3)=x-3 on the Regents, square both sides giving x+3=(x-3)²=x²-6x+9, leading to x²-7x+6=0, (x-1)(x-6)=0; check both: x=1 fails (√4≠1-3), x=6 works. Always test for extraneous solutions when squaring. The square-root function is one of the named parent functions in F-IF.7.",
