      "explanation": "The quadratic parent function f(x)=x² is the foundational parabola (F-IF.7a). Vertex (0,0), axis of symmetry x=0, opens upward, range y≥0. All quadratics y=a(x-h)²+k are stretches, reflections, and shifts of this parent. Key features include zeros (x=0 with multiplicity 2), even symmetry (f(-x)=f(x)), and constant second differences. On the Algebra 2 Regents, the quadratic appears as a stepping stone to higher polynomials and in modeling projectile motion. Quadratic-formula items expect students to compute the discriminant b²-4ac to count real roots: positive→two real, zero→one repeated, negative→two complex conjugates.",
