      "correctText": "end behavior",
      "topic": "Polynomial Features",
      "explanation": "End behavior describes f(x) as x→±∞ (F-IF.7c). The rules: (1) even degree, positive leading coefficient: f(x)→+∞ as x→±∞ (both ends up, like x²); (2) even degree, negative leading coefficient: both ends down (like -x²); (3) odd degree, positive leading coefficient: left end down, right end up (like x³); (4) odd degree, negative leading coefficient: left up, right down (like -x³). On the Algebra 2 Regents, end behavior is a frequent multiple choice topic; students should ignore the lower-degree terms and focus on the leading term's sign and exponent parity. Notation: f(x)→∞ as x→∞.",
