      "explanation": "The constant term is a₀ in standard form, the value of the polynomial when x=0, so it equals the y-intercept (A-APR.1, F-IF.7c). For f(x)=2x³-x+5, the constant is 5 and the y-intercept is (0,5). The constant term is also the product of all roots times (-1)^n divided by the leading coefficient (from Vieta's formulas). On the Algebra 2 Regents, students locate the y-intercept quickly by reading the constant term, useful when comparing transformations or interpreting models. In factored form f(x)=a(x-r₁)(x-r₂)...(x-r_n), the constant equals a·(-r₁)(-r₂)...(-r_n)=a·(-1)^n·∏r_i.",
