      "correctText": "index of summation",
      "topic": "Power + Change",
      "explanation": "The index of summation is the variable (commonly k, i, or j) that ranges over the integers from the lower to upper limit in sigma notation (A-SSE.4). Σ(k=1 to 5) k² evaluates k² for k=1,2,3,4,5: 1+4+9+16+25=55. The index is a 'dummy variable'—renaming doesn't change the sum: Σ(j=1 to 5) j²=Σ(k=1 to 5) k². Adjust the index for shifts: Σ(k=1 to n) aₖ₊₂ = Σ(j=3 to n+2) aⱼ. On the Algebra 2 Regents, sigma notation problems test recognition of the index, substitution into the summand, and the relationship between sigma form and explicit addition.",
