      "correctText": "multiplication rule",
      "topic": "Probability Rules",
      "explanation": "The multiplication rule: P(A∩B)=P(A)·P(B|A), where P(B|A) is the conditional probability of B given A (S-CP.8). For independent events, P(B|A)=P(B), so P(A∩B)=P(A)·P(B). Example: drawing two cards without replacement, P(2 aces)=P(first ace)·P(second ace | first ace)=4/52·3/51=12/2652=1/221. With replacement, both draws are independent: 4/52·4/52=1/169. On the Algebra 2 Regents, the multiplication rule is tested in sequential or simultaneous events; distinguishing with vs without replacement determines whether to use P(B) or P(B|A). Tree diagrams visualize multi-step problems.",
