      "topic": "Regents Model Defense",
      "explanation": "Rounded answer defense justifies the rounding choice based on context (N-Q.3). Examples: round up for time-to-reach (need at least this much time); round down for capacity (cannot exceed limit); round to nearest cent for money; round to integer for counts of objects. Example: if a population reaches 10,000 at t=17.67 years, round up to 18 years for 'the smallest integer year at which population exceeds 10,000.' On the cumulative Algebra 2 Regents review, students explicitly justify rounding decisions: 'I rounded up to 5 buses because 4 buses cannot transport all students.' Always include units. Default Regents rounding is to the precision specified in the question (nearest tenth, hundredth, etc.).",
