      "correctText": "regression equation",
      "topic": "Technology Output",
      "explanation": "A regression equation is the best-fit function for given data, computed via calculator commands like LinReg, QuadReg, ExpReg, LnReg, SinReg (S-ID.6). Procedure: enter x-values in L1, y-values in L2, choose appropriate regression. Calculator returns coefficients and statistics (r, r²). Example: LinReg on data returns y=2.3x+5.1 with r=0.95 (strong positive correlation). The regression equation lets students make predictions: predict y when x=10 by substituting. On the Algebra 2 Regents, students choose the correct regression type based on data shape, perform the regression, interpret coefficients in context, and use the equation for prediction. Choosing the wrong regression type produces a poor fit; check r² to compare.",
