      "correctText": "residual plot",
      "topic": "Technology Output",
      "explanation": "A residual plot graphs residuals (observed − predicted) against x-values (S-ID.6b). Random scatter: model is appropriate. Pattern (curve, fan shape, trend): model is inadequate—wrong type or missing transformation. Examples: U-shape in residuals → linear model is missing a quadratic component. Fan shape (widening spread) → non-constant variance (heteroscedasticity). Linear trend in residuals → wrong type entirely. On the Algebra 2 Regents, residual plots distinguish good fits from inadequate ones: high r² with patterned residuals signals a structural issue. Construct a residual plot by computing predicted values from the regression and subtracting from observed.",
