      "correctText": "calculator window",
      "topic": "Technology Output",
      "explanation": "The calculator window defines what's visible on the screen (F-IF.4 connection). Set with WINDOW or ZOOM commands. ZoomStandard sets [-10,10]×[-10,10]; ZoomFit shows full range of data; ZBox lets you draw a custom box; ZoomStat shows the data range plus margin. Wrong window settings can hide features: a parabola with vertex at (50, 100) won't appear in the standard window. On the Algebra 2 Regents, students set appropriate windows to visualize functions and data: include all important features (intercepts, vertex, asymptotes, data range). Use Xscl and Yscl to set tick mark intervals. Always state your window when sketching from calculator graphs.",
