      "explanation": "A unit-circle value is an exact trig value computed from unit-circle coordinates (F-TF.2). Memorize key values: sin(0)=0, sin(π/6)=1/2, sin(π/4)=√2/2, sin(π/3)=√3/2, sin(π/2)=1. cos(0)=1, cos(π/6)=√3/2, cos(π/4)=√2/2, cos(π/3)=1/2, cos(π/2)=0. tan: 0, √3/3, 1, √3, undefined. For angles in other quadrants, find the reference angle, look up the value, then apply quadrant sign (CAST or ASTC mnemonic). Example: sin(5π/6) has reference π/6 and is in Q2 (sin positive), so sin(5π/6)=1/2. cos(7π/4) reference π/4, Q4 (cos positive), so √2/2. On the cumulative Algebra 2 Regents review, unit-circle values appear constantly without calculator.",
