      "correctText": "sequence formula",
      "topic": "Trig and Sequences",
      "explanation": "A sequence formula gives the nth term either explicitly (as a function of n) or recursively (in terms of previous terms) (F-BF.2, F-IF.3). Arithmetic explicit: aₙ=a₁+(n-1)d. Geometric explicit: aₙ=a₁·r^(n-1). Recursive arithmetic: aₙ=aₙ₋₁+d with a₁ given. Recursive geometric: aₙ=r·aₙ₋₁ with a₁ given. Example: arithmetic 5, 8, 11, 14, ...: explicit aₙ=5+(n-1)·3=3n+2; recursive aₙ=aₙ₋₁+3, a₁=5. To translate from explicit to recursive: compute d or r from a₂-a₁ or a₂/a₁. On the cumulative Algebra 2 Regents review, students convert between forms and evaluate specific terms.",
