      "explanation": "The cosine function maps angle θ to the x-coordinate of its unit circle point (F-TF.2). Range [-1,1], period 2π, even function: cos(-θ)=cos(θ). Key values: cos(0)=1, cos(π/6)=√3/2, cos(π/4)=√2/2, cos(π/3)=1/2, cos(π/2)=0, cos(π)=-1, cos(3π/2)=0. The graph y=cos(θ) starts at maximum (0,1), drops to 0 at π/2, minimum -1 at π, back to 0 at 3π/2, max again at 2π. Cosine is a phase-shifted sine: cos(θ)=sin(θ+π/2). On the Algebra 2 Regents, cosine appears in unit-circle evaluation, sinusoidal modeling, and the Pythagorean identity sin²+cos²=1.",
