      "explanation": "The tangent function is tan(θ)=sin(θ)/cos(θ) (F-TF.2). Range all reals, period π, odd. Vertical asymptotes where cos(θ)=0: θ=π/2, 3π/2, etc. (odd multiples of π/2). Key values: tan(0)=0, tan(π/6)=√3/3, tan(π/4)=1, tan(π/3)=√3. tan(π/2) undefined. The graph y=tan(θ) repeats every π, with branches between consecutive asymptotes. tan(θ)>0 in Q1 and Q3 (where sin and cos have same sign); tan(θ)<0 in Q2 and Q4. On the Algebra 2 Regents, tangent appears in unit circle evaluation, in identities, and in modeling situations where the rate sin/cos has meaning (e.g., slope of a line at angle θ to the x-axis).",
