      "topic": "Apoptosis + Checkpoints",
      "explanation": "Intrinsic (mitochondrial) apoptosis is governed by Bcl-2 family proteins: pro-apoptotic (Bax, Bak — effectors that oligomerize and permeabilize the outer mitochondrial membrane; BH3-only proteins like Bid, Bim, Puma — sensors) vs. anti-apoptotic (Bcl-2, Bcl-xL, Mcl-1 — sequester pro-apoptotic). When the balance tips pro-apoptotic, MOMP (mitochondrial outer membrane permeabilization) releases cytochrome c → apoptosome (Apaf-1 + procaspase-9) → caspase-9 → caspase-3 → apoptosis. Bcl-2 was discovered as a t(14;18) translocation in follicular lymphoma (Korsmeyer 1985), the first oncogene that promoted survival rather than proliferation. Venetoclax (Bcl-2 inhibitor) treats CLL. AP Bio Unit 4 expects students to predict apoptosis outcomes from Bax/Bcl-2 ratios.",
