      "topic": "Apoptosis + Checkpoints",
      "explanation": "Metaphase: sister-chromatid pairs align at the metaphase plate (cell equator), each kinetochore attached to spindle microtubules from opposite poles (bipolar attachment). Mitosis sequence: prophase (chromosome condensation, NE breakdown begins) → prometaphase (NE breakdown, MT capture by kinetochores) → metaphase (alignment) → anaphase (sister separation) → telophase (NE reforms, decondensation) → cytokinesis (cleavage furrow). Spindle assembly checkpoint (SAC, Mad2/BubR1) blocks anaphase entry until all kinetochores are properly attached — error here causes aneuploidy and is a cancer driver (Boveri 1914 first hypothesized). AP Bio Unit 4 demands phase identification on micrographs.",
