      "explanation": "Apoptosis (Greek: 'falling away') is regulated, non-inflammatory cell death. Hallmarks: chromatin condensation, DNA fragmentation (180-bp ladder by CAD), cell shrinkage, blebbing, apoptotic bodies cleared by macrophages. Executed by caspases (cysteine-aspartate proteases): initiators (caspase-8 extrinsic, caspase-9 intrinsic) activate executioners (caspase-3, -6, -7) that cleave hundreds of substrates. Pathways: extrinsic (death receptors FAS, TNFR + ligand → caspase-8) and intrinsic (mitochondrial — Bax/Bak permeabilize outer membrane, cytochrome c release → apoptosome → caspase-9). Discovered through C. elegans developmental cell death (Brenner, Horvitz, Sulston 2002 Nobel). AP Bio Unit 4 expects this as a tumor-suppressing mechanism.",
