      "explanation": "P53 (TP53 gene) is mutated in >50% of human cancers — the most-mutated tumor suppressor. Discovered 1979 by Lane, Crawford, Levine. In response to DNA damage (ATM/ATR phosphorylation), oncogene activation, or hypoxia, p53 protein is stabilized (Mdm2 degradation halts) and transcribes target genes: p21 (cell-cycle arrest), GADD45 (DNA repair), PUMA + Bax (apoptosis). Germline TP53 mutations cause Li-Fraumeni syndrome (multiple cancers, often early-onset). HPV E6 protein degrades p53 — mechanism of HPV-driven cervical cancer. AP Bio Unit 4 + 6 FRQs ask students to predict cell behavior when p53 is lost: failure to arrest with damage → mutation accumulation → cancer.",
