      "correctText": "Altruism",
      "topic": "Behavior + Climate Impact",
      "explanation": "Altruism: behavior that REDUCES the actor's reproductive fitness while INCREASING another's. Hamilton's rule (1964): altruism evolves when rB > C, where r = coefficient of relatedness, B = benefit to recipient, C = cost to actor. Kin selection explains most cases: helping siblings (r=0.5), nieces/nephews (r=0.25). Inclusive fitness includes direct (own offspring) + indirect (kin offspring helped) reproduction. Examples: vampire bat food sharing (with non-kin too — reciprocal altruism, Trivers 1971); meerkat sentinels (r ≈ 0.32 in family groups); naked mole rat eusociality (extremely high relatedness through inbreeding). Reciprocal altruism (delayed payback) and group selection are also proposed mechanisms. AP Bio Unit 8 + 7 expects evolutionary explanations of cooperation.",
