      "explanation": "AP CSP Big Idea 3.17 distinguishes 'reasonable' (polynomial time — runs in n, n², n³ steps for input size n) from 'unreasonable' (exponential — 2^n grows so fast that n=100 takes longer than the age of the universe). Pioneer Alan Cobham (1965) and Jack Edmonds (1965) defined 'tractable' as polynomial time. The famous P vs NP problem (Stephen Cook 1971, Leonid Levin 1973) asks if every efficiently checkable problem is also efficiently solvable. Clay Mathematics offers $1M for a solution. Exam questions compare algorithm efficiency and ask which is reasonable.",
