      "explanation": "Boolean values (named for George Boole's 1854 'Laws of Thought') are true/false used in conditionals. AP CSP CED Big Idea 3.8 covers Boolean expressions and operators (AND, OR, NOT). Compound expressions: (age >= 13 AND age < 20) tests teenager. De Morgan's laws (Augustus De Morgan, 1847) let you transform NOT(A AND B) into (NOT A) OR (NOT B). Exam questions test whether students can evaluate compound Booleans for given variable values, or simplify them using De Morgan. Short-circuit evaluation (AND stops on first false; OR stops on first true) appears as an efficiency optimization.",
