      "explanation": "Lists in AP CSP are 1-indexed — list[1] is the first element, list[LENGTH(list)] is the last. (Most languages use 0-indexing, but the AP reference sheet uses 1.) The Create Performance Task rubric requires use of a list — without one, students automatically lose 1 of 6 points. Reference-sheet operations: APPEND, INSERT, REMOVE, FOR EACH item IN list. Pioneer John McCarthy's LISP (1958) made lists a first-class data type. Exam questions test trace: 'after APPEND(L, 7), what is L?' or 'what does L[3] return after these operations?'.",
      "domain": "Review",
      "gradeBand": "Multi",
      "subjectArea": "Review",
      "standardRefs": [],
      "sourceAuthority": "mr-macs-jeopardy",
      "assessmentSourceId": "jeopardy-ap-computer-science-principles",
