      "correctText": "MLA",
      "topic": "Citation Practices",
      "explanation": "MLA (Modern Language Association) is the citation style standard for English studies - the style most AP English students learn for research papers, though the synthesis FRQ does not require full MLA formatting. AP English Language Unit 8 references MLA primarily for context: the synthesis FRQ uses in-text attribution by source letter or author name rather than full MLA in-text citations with page numbers, but students should know MLA conventions for other writing. The 2021 MLA Handbook (9th edition) is the current standard. Strong AP students transfer MLA's commitment to attribution and source integrity even when the FRQ format does not demand the full apparatus.",
