      "correctText": "Works cited",
      "topic": "Citation Practices",
      "explanation": "Works cited is the alphabetical list of sources at the end of an MLA-formatted essay - a feature not required by the AP synthesis FRQ (Q1) but central to research writing. AP English Language Unit 8 teaches Works Cited primarily for transfer to research writing in other courses: the FRQ format substitutes the provided source packet for the Works Cited list. Strong students recognize that the source packet performs the same function: making sources locatable and verifiable. The MLA Handbook (9th ed., 2021) sets current Works Cited standards. Students applying MLA outside the FRQ should know container framework, hanging indent, alphabetical order, and full publication information.",
