      "correctText": "Flow",
      "topic": "Coherence",
      "explanation": "Flow is the perceived smoothness of movement between ideas - the cumulative effect of strong transitions, parallel structure, and varied sentence rhythm. AP English Language Unit 3 teaches flow as one quality among many that distinguishes sophisticated prose: jagged transitions, repetitive sentence structure, and disjointed paragraph order all impede flow. The AP argument FRQ rubric awards sophistication (Row C, 1 point, College Board CED 2024) partly on the basis of prose that 'employs a style that is consistently vivid and persuasive' - a category covering flow. King's prose flows because his transitions are logical and his anaphora establishes rhythm.",
