      "correctText": "Jargon",
      "topic": "Diction",
      "explanation": "Jargon is the specialized vocabulary of a field or profession - terms that are precise within the disciplinary community but opaque to outsiders. AP English Language Unit 4 teaches jargon as double-edged: it builds credibility with expert audiences (ethos through demonstrated insider knowledge) but excludes general readers and can be deployed to mystify (Orwell's complaint in 'Politics and the English Language,' 1946). Carson's 'Silent Spring' (1962) integrates chemical jargon ('chlorinated hydrocarbons,' 'cholinesterase inhibition') with general-audience prose, building expert ethos without losing accessibility. The AP rhetorical analysis FRQ rewards students who note when jargon serves or undermines author purpose.",
