      "explanation": "Six points is the total possible score on each FRQ - the AP English Language exam scoring scale established in 2019 (replacing the older 9-point rubric). AP English Language frames the 6-point rubric as standardizing scoring across the three FRQs: Row A (thesis) earns 0 or 1 point, Row B (evidence and commentary) earns 0-4 points, Row C (sophistication) earns 0 or 1 point. Total: 0-6 points per essay, 0-18 across the three FRQs (College Board CED 2024). Students must learn the rubric structure cold because earning each row's points requires meeting different specific criteria. The 6-point rubric replaced the 9-point holistic scale to make scoring more transparent.",
