      "correctText": "Argumentative essay",
      "topic": "Genre",
      "explanation": "An argumentative essay defends a thesis through evidence, reasoning, and anticipation of counterarguments - the genre tested directly by FRQ 3 (argument) on the AP English Language exam. AP Lang Unit 1 introduces argumentative essay so students can model their own writing on canonical examples: Orwell's 'Politics and the English Language' (1946) on diction and political honesty; Sandel's 'Justice: What's the Right Thing to Do?' (2009) on moral philosophy. The argumentative essay must take a clear position, structure body paragraphs with claim/evidence/warrant logic, and earn sophistication points by acknowledging complexity rather than retreating into both-sidesism.",
