      "explanation": "An editorial is a persuasive piece appearing in a newspaper, magazine, or online outlet that argues a position on a public issue - typically unsigned (representing the publication) or attributed to a named editor. AP English Language Unit 1 teaches editorial as a key genre because editorial rhetoric is heavily tested on the synthesis FRQ (Q1), which often draws sources from editorial pages. Editorials follow conventions: claim of policy, condensed evidence, anticipated objections, urgent call to action. Students must distinguish editorials from news reporting on the AP synthesis FRQ source set - failing to flag bias when citing an editorial costs evidence/commentary points.",
