      "correctText": "Pathos",
      "topic": "Persuasive Strategies",
      "explanation": "Pathos is persuasion via emotional appeal - the Aristotelian artistic proof grounded in imagery, anecdote, charged diction, and identification with shared values. AP English Language Unit 7 teaches pathos as essential to argument because pure logos rarely moves audiences to action: the analytical proof must be felt to land. King's 'I Have a Dream' (1963) deploys pathos through imagery of 'little black boys and black girls joining hands'; Sojourner Truth's 1851 speech mobilizes pathos through counted lost children. The AP argument FRQ (Q3) rubric (Row C, sophistication, 1 point) rewards essays where pathos serves the argument rather than substitutes for it - earned pathos integrated with logos and ethos.",
