      "correctText": "Logos",
      "topic": "Persuasive Strategies",
      "explanation": "Logos is persuasion via logical appeal - the Aristotelian artistic proof grounded in evidence, valid reasoning, and clear inference, central to AP English Language Unit 7 argumentation. Logos persuades through statistics, syllogism, expert testimony, empirical evidence, and reasoning chains. Carson's 'Silent Spring' (1962) builds logos through chemical evidence; Sandel's 'Justice' (2009) builds logos through philosophical reasoning. The AP argument FRQ (Q3) rubric (Row B, up to 4 points) rewards logos-driven evidence and commentary specifically, distinguishing reasoning from mere assertion. Pure logos without ethos or pathos rarely persuades real audiences; Aristotle's 'Rhetoric' (4th c. BCE) emphasized that the three appeals work together.",
