      "correctText": "Kairos",
      "topic": "Persuasive Strategies",
      "explanation": "Kairos is persuasion via right timing - the classical Greek concept of the opportune moment, added to Aristotle's three artistic proofs as a fourth dimension in modern rhetoric. AP English Language Unit 7 teaches kairos as essential to argumentative success: the same case made at the wrong moment fails. King's 'I Have a Dream' (1963) chose the Lincoln Memorial centenary of the Emancipation Proclamation; JFK's Inaugural (1961) seized the Cold War threshold. The AP argument FRQ (Q3) rubric (Row C, sophistication) rewards essays that situate their claims kairotically - engaging the cultural moment rather than treating the prompt's question as abstract or timeless.",
