      "id": "ap-english-language-and-composition-pe-025",
      "prompt": "PASSAGE E: \"Critics dismiss the neighborhood garden as a hobby for those who can afford the time. They miss the point. The garden produces tomatoes, yes; but it also produces the small, ordinary trust between neighbors who have learned each other's names while waiting for the rain. Of the two harvests, the second is harder to grow and easier to lose.\" — The writer's central claim is best summarized as —",
