      "explanation": "In-text citation in the AP synthesis FRQ (Q1) means identifying which source a student is using within the essay's prose - typically by Source A, Source B, or by author name in parentheses. AP English Language Unit 8 teaches that the synthesis FRQ does not require full MLA formal citation but does require attribution clear enough for the reader to identify which source the student is citing. The AP synthesis rubric (Row B) penalizes evidence used without attribution - the reader cannot credit unattributed claims as drawn from sources. Strong essays integrate citation smoothly: 'As Source A notes...' or '(Source A)' parenthetically.",
