      "correctText": "Three sources",
      "topic": "Synthesis Skills",
      "explanation": "Three sources is the minimum number students must incorporate in the AP synthesis FRQ (Q1) to earn evidence points - specifically, the Row B rubric requires at least three of the provided sources used in support of the student's thesis. AP English Language Unit 8 teaches that students should engage more sources when possible (the packet typically contains six or seven), but three is the floor for evidence credit. The College Board CED 2024 explicitly directs students to 'incorporate at least three of the provided sources' as the procedural baseline. Strong essays integrate sources rather than parading them, treating each as evidence for the controlling argument.",
