      "correctText": "Synthesis thesis",
      "topic": "Synthesis Skills",
      "explanation": "A synthesis thesis is an original argument using sources rather than merely summarizing them - the controlling claim of the AP synthesis FRQ (Q1) response. AP English Language Unit 8 teaches that the synthesis thesis must take a defensible position responsive to the prompt and use the source packet as evidence and conversation. The AP synthesis FRQ rubric (Row A, 1 point, College Board CED 2024) requires a defensible thesis; pure summary of sources or restatement of the prompt earns zero. Strong synthesis theses are specific (not 'this is complex'), defensible (not absolutist), and clearly the student's own argument supported by but not reducible to the sources.",
