      "correctText": "Multiple media",
      "topic": "Synthesis Skills",
      "explanation": "Multiple media in the AP synthesis FRQ (Q1) source packet refers to the variety of source types students encounter - editorials, charts, photographs, op-eds, primary sources, scholarly excerpts, data visualizations. AP English Language Unit 8 teaches that visual sources (charts, images, cartoons) require the same rhetorical analysis as textual ones: identifying purpose, audience, evidence, and bias. The AP synthesis FRQ rubric (Row B) rewards students who integrate visual and textual sources alongside each other rather than skipping visual sources or treating them superficially. Pollan, Carson, and other modern essayists routinely braid statistics, charts, and prose to mirror the multi-media synthesis FRQ challenge.",
