      "correctText": "Critical reading",
      "topic": "Synthesis Strategy",
      "explanation": "Critical reading is the practice of acknowledging source bias, evaluating evidence, and questioning assumptions within the AP synthesis FRQ (Q1) source packet. AP English Language Unit 8 teaches critical reading as essential to credible synthesis: students who treat all sources as equally authoritative miss the rhetorical work of source evaluation. The AP synthesis FRQ rubric (Row B, evidence and commentary) rewards critical engagement with source bias - acknowledging that an editorial pushes a position, that a corporate-sponsored study has interests, that a primary source comes from a particular vantage. Critical reading builds student ethos by demonstrating she can be trusted with the evidence.",
