      "correctText": "Original synthesis",
      "topic": "Synthesis Strategy",
      "explanation": "Original synthesis is the central goal of the AP synthesis FRQ (Q1): building an argument from the sources that is the student's own, not reducible to any single source's position. AP English Language Unit 8 teaches that original synthesis requires the student to take a stance the source packet supports but does not state - using sources as evidence and conversation partners rather than authorities to defer to. The AP synthesis FRQ rubric (Row A, 1 point, College Board CED 2024) requires a defensible thesis; Row C (1 point) rewards sophistication including 'engaging effectively with broader context.' Original synthesis is what distinguishes 5- and 6-point essays from mere source compilation.",
