      "correctText": "Source selection",
      "topic": "Synthesis Strategy",
      "explanation": "Source selection is the strategic choice of which sources from the AP synthesis FRQ (Q1) packet to use in the essay - typically three to five of the six or seven provided. AP English Language Unit 8 teaches that the choice matters: not all sources serve the student's argument equally well, and weaker essays often cite all sources cursorily while stronger essays develop fewer sources thoroughly. The AP synthesis FRQ rubric (Row B, evidence and commentary) rewards depth of integration over breadth of citation, so students should select sources they can engage analytically rather than parading the full packet. The College Board CED 2024 emphasizes 'judicious use' of the source packet.",
