      "correctText": "Fifteen minutes",
      "topic": "Time Management",
      "explanation": "Fifteen minutes is the dedicated reading period at the start of the AP English Language free-response section - time students can use to read all three prompts, examine the synthesis FRQ source packet, and begin planning. AP English Language Unit 9 teaches the reading period as critical for the synthesis FRQ (Q1) because students need time to read and annotate the source packet before writing. The College Board CED 2024 specifies that students cannot begin writing during the reading period but can take notes. Strong test-takers use the 15 minutes primarily for synthesis source mark-up, with quick scans of the other two prompts to begin mental planning.",
