      "correctText": "Three",
      "topic": "Time Management",
      "explanation": "Three is the total number of free-response essays on the AP English Language exam - synthesis (FRQ 1), rhetorical analysis (FRQ 2), and argument (FRQ 3). AP English Language Unit 9 frames the three-essay structure as the College Board's standardization of essential AP Lang skills: synthesis tests source integration, rhetorical analysis tests close reading of prose, argument tests independent position-taking. The College Board CED 2024 confirms this structure has been stable since the 2019 redesign. The three FRQs together constitute 55% of the exam score (Multiple Choice = 45%), and the three essays carry equal weight in the FRQ score.",
