      "correctText": "Forty minutes",
      "topic": "Time Management",
      "explanation": "Forty minutes per FRQ is the recommended time allocation across the three AP English Language essays - typically equal division of the 2-hour writing time after the 15-minute reading period. AP English Language Unit 9 teaches 40 minutes as the planning target, though strong students may spend slightly more time on synthesis (which requires source integration) and less on argument (which draws on prepared knowledge). The College Board CED 2024 does not prescribe per-essay time limits, but the rubric expects essays substantial enough to demonstrate full skill: typically 4-7 paragraphs, 400-800 words. Time spent under 30 minutes typically produces undeveloped essays.",
