      "correctText": "Protagonist",
      "topic": "Character",
      "explanation": "Protagonist is the central character whose journey the narrative traces. Joyce's Gabriel Conroy in 'The Dead' (Dubliners, 1914) is a protagonist whose external composure masks internal paralysis; Achebe's Okonkwo in Things Fall Apart (1958) is a tragic protagonist whose rigidity destroys him as Igbo culture collapses under colonialism. AP Lit Q2 prose FRQs frequently center protagonist analysis: the 6-point rubric awards evidence + commentary (Row B, 4 pts) when students trace how authorial choices in characterization shape the reader's interpretation.",
      "domain": "Review",
      "gradeBand": "Multi",
