      "correctText": "Flat character",
      "topic": "Character",
      "explanation": "Flat characters are constructed around a single dominant trait. Forster, Aspects of the Novel (1927): they 'never need re-introducing.' Mrs. Bennet in Austen's Pride and Prejudice (1813) is flat — her obsession with marrying daughters never deepens. AP Lit Q2 prose-analysis FRQs use flat characters as foils: the 6-point rubric (Row B, 4 pts) rewards students who explain how a flat character's simplicity sharpens contrast with a round protagonist's complexity, deepening thematic meaning rather than merely categorizing types.",
