      "explanation": "Character revelation is the gradual disclosure of character traits, motives, and depths through action, dialogue, and narration. Faulkner's 'A Rose for Emily' (1930) reveals Emily Grierson through fragmented chronology, withholding the climactic discovery until the final paragraph. AP Lit Q2 prose-analysis FRQs (6-point rubric, Row B, 4 pts) reward students who trace specific revelations and explain how their placement, withholding, and final disclosure generate thematic meaning. Sophistication (Row C, 1 pt) emerges through interpretive layering.",
