      "prompt": "Original prose passage composed for this practice exam:\\n\\n\" +\n  \"The lighthouse stood at the edge of the cliff like a forgotten sentinel, its lamp long since extinguished, its keeper \" +\n  \"long since gone. Eleanor climbed the spiral staircase that her grandfather had climbed every evening for forty-three years, \" +\n  \"and at each turn she felt the granite walls pressing in upon her as though the tower itself were a memory she could not \" +\n  \"escape. At the top she found what she had always found: the lens, the brass fittings tarnished but intact, the small leather \" +\n  \"logbook her grandfather had left open on the last day of his service. She did not read the final entry. She had read it \" +\n  \"once, the summer she turned fifteen, and the words had sat inside her ever since like a stone dropped into a deep well -- \" +\n  \"still falling, still unanswered. Outside, the sea performed its old indifferent argument with the rocks. Eleanor closed \" +\n  \"the logbook, set it carefully back upon the desk, and descended.\n\nEleanor's decision not to read the final entry most strongly characterizes her as:",
