      "correctText": "Rising action",
      "topic": "Plot Structure",
      "explanation": "Rising action escalates tension toward the climax through complications and conflict. Freytag's Pyramid (1863) systematizes this for five-act drama; Shakespeare's Macbeth (1606) embodies it as Macbeth murders Duncan, suspects Banquo, and consults the witches. On the AP Lit Q1 poetry-analysis and Q2 prose-analysis FRQs, the 6-point rubric (Row B, 4 points for evidence/commentary) rewards students who explain how escalating choices create meaning rather than cataloguing plot beats. Cause-and-effect tracing distinguishes a 3+ essay from a summary.",
