      "topic": "Plot Structure",
      "explanation": "Plot is the structured sequence of events in a narrative. Aristotle's Poetics (335 BCE) defined plot (mythos) as the soul of tragedy, demanding a beginning, middle, and end bound by causality rather than mere chronology. Gustav Freytag's Pyramid (1863) refined this into exposition, rising action, climax, falling action, denouement. On the AP Lit Q2 prose-analysis FRQ, examiners reward students who trace how plot construction generates meaning rather than merely summarizing events; the 6-point rubric awards thesis (1), evidence and commentary (4), and sophistication (1).",
