      "correctText": "Total marked over recaptured marked",
      "topic": "Sampling Populations",
      "explanation": "The Lincoln-Petersen estimator is N = M*C/R where M = total individuals marked and released, C = total in recapture sample, R = marked individuals in recapture sample. The ratio M/N (proportion of population marked) equals R/C (proportion marked in recapture) — basic probability. Lincoln (1930 waterfowl), Petersen (1896 plaice fish). Assumes the marked individuals fully mix back into the population, no births or deaths during the study, and equal catchability. Violations bias estimates downward (if marked animals are easier to recapture, R is too high, N too low). AP Environmental Science FRQs (CED Unit 3.3) require N calculation and identification of assumption violations from scenarios.",
