      "topic": "Sampling Populations",
      "explanation": "Mark-recapture (Lincoln-Petersen method) estimates mobile-animal populations: capture, mark, and release a sample (M); after mixing, capture a second sample (C); count marked individuals in second sample (R). Total population N = (M x C)/R. Frederick Lincoln applied it to waterfowl in 1930; C.G.J. Petersen had earlier applied it to fish in 1896. Assumes closed population, equal catchability, no mark loss. AP Environmental Science FRQs (CED Unit 3.3) frequently provide M, C, R data and require N calculation. Example: 100 fish marked, 80 recaptured, 20 marked among recaptures gives N = (100 x 80)/20 = 400 fish.",
