      "correctText": "Ne va pas!",
      "topic": "L'Impératif",
      "explanation": "Ne va pas! is the AP French Language negative tu command of aller. All negative commands keep the ne...pas structure: Ne parle pas, Ne mange pas, Ne fais pas, Ne pars pas. With pronouns, negative commands place pronouns before the verb (regular position): Ne le mange pas! Ne te lève pas! Compare with affirmative commands where pronouns attach to the verb with hyphen: Mange-le! Lève-toi! AP Conventions scoring rewards correct pronoun placement in both affirmative and negative commands. The rule: affirmative = verb + hyphen + pronoun; negative = ne + pronoun + verb + pas.",
