      "topic": "L'Impératif",
      "explanation": "The third-person imperative in French uses AP French Language subjunctive: Que vive la France! (Long live France!) Qu'il parte! (Let him leave!) Qu'ils viennent! (Let them come!) The construction Que + subjunctive expresses commands or wishes for third persons. Formal contexts use it: Que Dieu vous bénisse (May God bless you). Compare with vous/tu/nous direct imperatives (where Que is not used). Other fixed subjunctive expressions: Soit (so be it), Vive le roi (long live the king), Ainsi soit-il (so be it / amen). AP Language Use scoring at 5 rewards these subtle subjunctive uses, especially in formal writing.",
