      "explanation": "Le foyer multigénérationnel (or la famille élargie) is more common in immigrant and Maghrebi Francophone communities than in mainstream metropolitan France. AP French Language interpretive sources discuss how Algerian, Tunisian, Marocain immigrants in France maintain extended-family households against majority French norms of independence. Vocabulary: cohabiter, prendre soin de, les aînés (elders), la transmission intergénérationnelle. Useful expressions: vivre sous le même toit, partager le quotidien. Subjunctive triggers: Il est important que la famille reste unie. AP cultural comparison essays scoring 5 examine how multigenerational living preserves cultural heritage.",
