      "explanation": "La famille is a foundational AP French Language theme. In Francophone cultures, la famille extends beyond the nuclear unit (parents et enfants) to include grands-parents, oncles, tantes, cousins, and parfois parrains et marraines. AP interpretive readings frequently contrast la famille traditionnelle with la famille moderne, exploring divorce, familles monoparentales, and unions civiles. On the exam, expect text and audio sources comparing family structures across France, Québec, Belgique, Sénégal, and the Maghreb. Cultural comparison essays often ask students to compare la famille in their own community with one in the Francophone world.",
