      "correctText": "Marie Curie",
      "topic": "La Technologie",
      "explanation": "Marie Curie (1867-1934) is the AP French Language paradigmatic woman scientist. Born in Warsaw, she moved to Paris to study at the Sorbonne. With husband Pierre, she discovered polonium and radium. She won the Nobel Prize in Physics (1903) and Chemistry (1911), the only person to win Nobels in two different sciences. She died from radiation exposure. Her daughter Irène Joliot-Curie also won a Nobel. Vocabulary: la radioactivité, la chimie, la physique, le prix Nobel, la pionnière. AP cultural comparison essays scoring 5 examine how Marie Curie broke gender barriers in science and connect to contemporary women in STEM.",
