      "prompt": "The French mood for talking about hypothetical situations (would).",
      "choices": [
        "le foyer multigénérationnel",
        "le conditionnel passé",
        "imparfait",
        "le conditionnel"
      ],
      "correctText": "le conditionnel",
      "topic": "Le Conditionnel",
      "explanation": "Le conditionnel is the AP French Language tense for would. Form: infinitive + imperfect endings (-ais, -ais, -ait, -ions, -iez, -aient). Examples: Je parlerais, Tu finirais, Nous viendrions. Same irregular stems as future: tendr-, viendr-, ferr-, dirr-, pourr-, savr-, voudr-, courr-, mourr-, irr-, aurr-, serr-. Uses: hypothetical (Si j'avais le temps, je voyagerais), polite requests (Pourriez-vous m'aider?), expressing wishes (J'aimerais), softened opinion (On pourrait dire que). AP Language Use scoring rewards correct conditional use, especially paired with imperfect in si clauses.",
