      "explanation": "Lui (singular) and leur (plural) are AP French Language indirect object pronouns. They replace à + person constructions. Examples: Je parle à Marie → Je lui parle. J'ai téléphoné aux étudiants → Je leur ai téléphoné. Lui and leur are the same regardless of gender, unlike le/la. Placement follows the same rules as direct object pronouns. AP Language Use scoring rewards consistency: students must correctly identify which verbs take direct vs. indirect objects (téléphoner à, parler à, donner à, écrire à take indirect; voir, aimer, regarder take direct). When both pronouns appear: me/te/se/nous/vous come first, then le/la/les, then lui/leur.",
