      "topic": "Travail et Carrière",
      "explanation": "Les syndicats are a foundational AP French Language Republican institution. Major French unions: CGT (Confédération générale du travail), CFDT (more reformist), FO (Force ouvrière), Solidaires. Despite low membership rates (~8%), French unions have outsized influence through their ability to mobilize strikes (la grève) and pressure governments. Major waves: 1968 general strike, 1995 anti-pension reform, 2018 yellow vests (gilets jaunes), 2019-23 pension reform protests under Macron. Vocabulary: la grève, la manifestation, la négociation collective, les acquis sociaux. AP cultural comparison essays scoring 5 contrast French unions with the U.S. labor movement.",
