      "topic": "Culture",
      "explanation": "By Caesar's day a legion had 10 cohorts (cohortes); each cohort had 6 centuries (centuriae); each century was nominally 80 fighting men (the term 'centuria' is older, when it held closer to 100). Each century was led by a centurio; the primus pilus was the senior centurion of the first cohort and the legion's most senior centurion.",
