      "correctText": "The two consuls",
      "topic": "Culture",
      "explanation": "Two consuls, elected annually, held supreme civilian and military authority (imperium). Each could veto the other (a built-in check). Censors (every 5 years) oversaw the census and morals; praetors handled justice; tribunes of the plebs protected plebeian interests (10 of them, with veto power, but no imperium). Caesar was consul in 59 BCE before his Gallic command.",
