      "correctText": "Accusative plural — direct object of the verb",
      "topic": "Grammar/Syntax",
      "explanation": "'Rosas' is the accusative plural of 'rosa' (1st declension). 'Pulchras' is the matching feminine accusative plural of 'pulcher, -chra, -chrum.' Adjectives must agree with their nouns in gender, number, and case. They are the direct object of 'dat' ('she gives').",
