      "topic": "Grammar/Syntax",
      "explanation": "In Latin indirect statement, the subject of the reported clause is in the accusative ('hostes') and the verb is an infinitive ('venire,' present active infinitive). 'Caesar says that X is happening' — the present infinitive expresses an action contemporaneous with the main verb.",
