      "correctText": "Normal goods",
      "topic": "Demand",
      "explanation": "A normal good is one for which demand increases as consumer income rises (positive income elasticity of demand, YED > 0). Most goods are normal — as incomes rise, people buy more restaurant meals, vacations, and new cars. Contrast with inferior goods (YED < 0), for which demand falls when income rises. Luxury goods are a subset of normal goods with YED > 1.",
