      "correctText": "Demand curve shift",
      "topic": "Demand",
      "explanation": "A shift in the demand curve means the entire schedule changes: at every price, consumers now demand a different quantity. Rightward shifts (demand increase) follow from: higher income (for normal goods), higher prices of substitutes, lower prices of complements, favorable taste changes, higher expected future prices, or more buyers. Leftward shifts reflect the opposites. Do not confuse a demand shift with a price-driven movement along the curve.",
