      "explanation": "Consumer surplus (CS) is the difference between the maximum a buyer is willing to pay (their reservation price) and the actual market price paid, summed across all buyers. On a supply-demand graph, CS is the triangular area above the equilibrium price and below the demand curve. Taxes, price ceilings, and monopoly pricing reduce CS; subsidies increase it. Together with producer surplus, CS measures total market welfare.",
