      "correctText": "Efficiency versus equity",
      "topic": "Supply Basics",
      "explanation": "Efficiency seeks to maximize total output and minimize waste (produce on the PPC, allocate where P = MC); equity focuses on the fairness of distribution. Policies improving equity (progressive taxes, subsidies to low-income groups) often reduce efficiency by distorting incentives, and vice versa. AP Micro FRQs may ask you to evaluate a policy on both dimensions.",
