      "correctText": "Supply curve shift",
      "topic": "Surplus + Taxes",
      "explanation": "A shift in supply means the entire supply schedule changes — sellers offer a different quantity at every price. Rightward shifts (supply increase): lower input costs, better technology, more sellers, subsidies, or favorable price expectations. Leftward shifts (supply decrease): higher input costs, taxes, fewer sellers. AP FRQ trap: a price change moves you along the supply curve; only a non-price determinant shifts the curve.",
      "domain": "Review",
