      "correctText": "Marginal social benefit",
      "topic": "Taxes + Subsidies",
      "explanation": "Marginal social benefit (MSB) = MPB (private benefit) + MEB (marginal external benefit). For activities with positive externalities (education, vaccination), MSB > MPB. The MSB curve is the 'true' demand curve from society's perspective. Efficient output: where MSB = MSC. Market output (where MPB = MPC) is less than efficient Q* when MSB > MPB. A Pigouvian subsidy equal to MEB per unit makes private demand (MPB + subsidy) coincide with MSB.",
