      "explanation": "Position x(t) is recovered from velocity by antidifferentiation: x(t) = x_0 + integral from 0 to t of v(t')dt'. This is the calculus inverse of v = dx/dt and a defining AP Physics C Mech competency absent from algebra-based courses. On a v-t graph, the signed area under the curve from 0 to t equals the displacement x(t) - x_0. The 2019 AP Phys C Mech FRQ #1 provided a piecewise v(t) graph and required students to compute displacement by summing areas (triangles and rectangles), invoking the Fundamental Theorem of Calculus. Science Practice 2 (mathematical routines) and Practice 3 (graphical analysis) are co-tested here.",
