      "explanation": "Plasticity is the brain's ability to reorganize its structure and function in response to experience, learning, or injury. It peaks in childhood (critical periods) but continues throughout life. London taxi drivers show enlarged hippocampi from years of spatial navigation. After stroke or brain injury, adjacent regions can sometimes take over lost functions — the basis for neurorehabilitation therapy.",
