      "correctText": "Dispositional attribution",
      "topic": "Classic Studies",
      "explanation": "Dispositional (internal) attribution explains behavior by citing the person's character, personality, attitudes, or abilities — 'she failed because she's lazy.' It contrasts with situational attribution. The fundamental attribution error is the systematic bias toward dispositional explanations when observing others. AP FRQs often present a scenario and ask students to distinguish between dispositional and situational attributions in the context of a real social psychology study.",
