      "correctText": "Big Five",
      "topic": "Classic Studies",
      "explanation": "The Big Five (OCEAN: Openness, Conscientiousness, Extraversion, Agreeableness, Neuroticism) is the dominant trait model in personality psychology, derived through factor analysis of personality descriptors. Unlike Freud's theory, it's empirically grounded and cross-culturally replicated. High conscientiousness predicts academic and occupational success; high neuroticism predicts psychological distress. Traits are stable across the lifespan but personalities tend to mellow (less neuroticism, more agreeableness) with age.",
