      "prompt": "Learning by associating two stimuli.",
      "choices": [
        "Classical conditioning",
        "Freud",
        "Extinction",
        "Reinforcement"
      ],
      "correctText": "Classical conditioning",
      "topic": "Classical Conditioning",
      "explanation": "Classical conditioning, discovered by Ivan Pavlov, is a form of associative learning in which a neutral stimulus (CS) acquires the power to elicit a response after being repeatedly paired with a stimulus that naturally triggers that response (US). Key processes include acquisition, extinction, spontaneous recovery, generalization, and discrimination. Watson applied these principles to humans in the infamous 'Little Albert' experiment, conditioning fear of a white rat.",
