      "prompt": "Active system for briefly holding and manipulating information.",
      "choices": [
        "Median",
        "Validity",
        "Availability heuristic",
        "Working memory"
      ],
      "correctText": "Working memory",
      "topic": "Cognition",
      "explanation": "Working memory (Baddeley's model) is the active cognitive system that temporarily holds and manipulates information, comprising a phonological loop (verbal), visuospatial sketchpad (spatial/visual), episodic buffer (integration), and central executive (attention). Its limited capacity (~4 chunks, per Cowan) explains why phone numbers, directions, and multi-step problems overload us. It's essential for reading comprehension, math problem-solving, and any task requiring holding information while processing.",
