      "prompt": "Using expectations, context, and prior knowledge to interpret sensory input.",
      "choices": [
        "Top-down processing",
        "Validity",
        "Biopsychosocial approach",
        "Working memory"
      ],
      "correctText": "Top-down processing",
      "topic": "Cognition",
      "explanation": "Top-down processing uses prior knowledge, context, and expectations to shape perception — the brain actively constructs meaning rather than passively receiving sensory input. Reading words in context (you can raed tihs scntence because context guides your parsing), hearing your name across a noisy room, or misidentifying a dark shape as a familiar dog illustrate top-down effects. It interacts continuously with bottom-up sensory data, explaining why perception is faster but also error-prone.",
