      "correctText": "Descriptive statistics",
      "topic": "Descriptive Statistics",
      "explanation": "Descriptive statistics organize and summarize raw data through measures of central tendency (mean, median, mode) and spread (range, standard deviation). They describe what is in a dataset without making inferences beyond it. A histogram, frequency table, or box plot are all forms of descriptive statistical presentation. They're the essential first step before applying inferential tests.",
