      "prompt": "Learning by watching and imitating others.",
      "choices": [
        "Secure attachment",
        "Extinction",
        "Observational learning",
        "Object permanence"
      ],
      "correctText": "Observational learning",
      "topic": "Development + Learning",
      "explanation": "Observational learning (Bandura) is acquiring behavior, attitudes, or emotional reactions by watching others — without direct reinforcement of the learner. Bandura's Bobo doll experiments showed children imitated filmed aggressive models even without personal reward. Required processes: attention to the model, retention of behavior, motor reproduction ability, and motivation. This contrasts with classical conditioning (no stimulus pairing needed) and operant conditioning (no personal consequence needed).",
