      "prompt": "Learning shaped by reinforcement and punishment.",
      "choices": [
        "Operant conditioning",
        "Observational learning",
        "Secure attachment",
        "Endocrine system"
      ],
      "correctText": "Operant conditioning",
      "topic": "Development + Learning",
      "explanation": "Operant conditioning (Skinner) shapes voluntary behavior through reinforcement (consequences that increase behavior) and punishment (consequences that decrease behavior). Positive adds a stimulus; negative removes one. Schedules of reinforcement control how quickly behavior is acquired and extinguished: continuous reinforcement builds behavior fastest; variable-ratio (slot machine) produces highest response rates and most resistance to extinction — which is why intermittent reward is so addictive.",
