      "correctText": "Placebo effect",
      "topic": "Experimental Control",
      "explanation": "The placebo effect occurs when participants show measurable improvement after receiving an inert treatment simply because they believe it will work. It reveals the power of expectation on physiology and behavior. To control for it, researchers use placebos and blind procedures — participants in the control group receive a sugar pill, for instance, so psychological expectation is equivalent across groups.",
