      "correctText": "Replication",
      "topic": "Experimental Control",
      "explanation": "Replication is the repetition of a study to check whether its findings appear reliably across different samples, researchers, and settings. Science's credibility depends on it — a single experiment's result may be a fluke, but convergent replications build confidence. The psychology 'replication crisis' (post-2010) revealed that many classic findings failed to reproduce, prompting reforms in study design and data transparency.",
