      "correctText": "Defense mechanisms",
      "topic": "Groups + Influence",
      "explanation": "Defense mechanisms are unconscious psychological strategies used by the ego to manage anxiety from id impulses or superego demands. Freud identified repression (banishing thoughts to unconscious) as foundational; Anna Freud elaborated others: rationalization (logical-sounding justifications), projection (attributing own feelings to others), displacement (redirecting impulses to a safer target), and reaction formation (behaving opposite to unconscious urge). AP FRQs test recognition and application of specific mechanisms.",
