      "correctText": "Representativeness heuristic",
      "topic": "Memory Errors",
      "explanation": "The representativeness heuristic involves judging the probability that something belongs to a category by how much it resembles the typical member (prototype). Tversky and Kahneman's Linda problem illustrates it: people rate 'Linda is a feminist bank teller' as more probable than 'Linda is a bank teller' — logically impossible, because a conjunction can't exceed a single event. This heuristic leads to ignoring base rates and causes clinical overdiagnosis when a patient resembles a textbook case.",
