      "topic": "Memory Errors",
      "explanation": "The misinformation effect occurs when exposure to misleading post-event information alters memory of the original event, as demonstrated by Loftus's research. Participants who heard leading questions after a filmed car accident 'remembered' details that never occurred (broken glass when none existed). This undermines confidence in eyewitness testimony and has led to reforms in how police conduct lineups and witness interviews to avoid contaminating memory.",
