      "explanation": "Working memory (Baddeley's model) is an active cognitive workspace that temporarily holds and manipulates information while it's being used, encompassing the phonological loop (verbal), visuospatial sketchpad (visual/spatial), and episodic buffer, all coordinated by the central executive. Its capacity is limited (~4 chunks, per Cowan's revised estimate) and duration is brief (~20 seconds without rehearsal). It's critical for comprehension, reasoning, and learning.",
