      "explanation": "Storage is the retention of encoded information over time in a neural network, maintained through synaptic changes (long-term potentiation). Atkinson and Shiffrin's three-box (multi-store) model distinguishes sensory memory (fractions of a second), short-term/working memory (seconds, ~7±2 chunks), and long-term memory (potentially permanent). Consolidation — the stabilization of new memories during sleep — is a critical subprocess of storage.",
