      "correctText": "Spacing effect",
      "topic": "Memory Strategies",
      "explanation": "The spacing effect is the well-documented finding that spreading study sessions over time produces better long-term retention than massed practice (cramming) of the same total duration. Ebbinghaus first documented it in 1885. Spaced repetition apps (like Anki) exploit this by re-presenting material just before it's forgotten. AP students often over-rely on cramming, which produces inflated short-term performance but poor retention a week later.",
