      "explanation": "The testing effect (also retrieval practice effect) is the finding that actively retrieving information from memory — even via low-stakes quizzes — strengthens that memory trace more than additional study does. Roediger and Karpicke's research showed that students who practiced retrieval scored ~50% better on final tests than those who restudied. This is why doing practice problems, using flashcards, and taking practice AP exams works better than rereading.",
