      "correctText": "Medical model",
      "topic": "Mood + Psychosis",
      "explanation": "The medical model treats psychological disorders as diseases with biological causes that can be diagnosed by symptoms and treated with medication or somatic therapy. It drives DSM classification and pharmaceutical interventions. Critics argue it pathologizes normal human variation and neglects social/psychological causes. The biopsychosocial model, increasingly favored, integrates biological vulnerability with psychological stressors and social context — explaining why two people with identical genetics can have very different mental health outcomes.",
