      "explanation": "Acquisition is the initial phase of learning when a conditioned response or behavior is established through pairing or reinforcement. In classical conditioning, it occurs when a CS is repeatedly paired with a US until the CS alone elicits a CR. In operant conditioning, it's when reinforced behaviors increase in frequency. Acquisition is faster when the CS-US interval is short (ideally 0.5 seconds for most conditioning) and the association is consistent.",
