      "explanation": "The conditioned response (CR) is the learned behavior elicited by the conditioned stimulus after repeated CS-US pairings. In Pavlov's experiments, salivation to the bell was the CR. It typically resembles but is slightly weaker than the unconditioned response (UR). A key AP distinction: the CR and UR may look identical (both are salivation in Pavlov's case) but are fundamentally different — one is learned, one is innate. Context matters for identification.",
