      "choices": [
        "Random assignment",
        "Case study",
        "Correlation",
        "Inattentional blindness"
      ],
      "correctText": "Case study",
      "topic": "Research Methods",
      "explanation": "A case study is an in-depth investigation of one individual, group, or event, providing rich, detailed data — particularly valuable for rare conditions that can't be studied experimentally. Phineas Gage (personality after brain injury), H.M. (anterograde amnesia after hippocampal removal), and Genie (language deprivation) are landmark AP case studies. The main weakness is low external validity: one exceptional case may not generalize to typical people.",
      "domain": "Review",
