      "prompt": "Entire group a researcher wants to study.",
      "choices": [
        "Psychoanalysis",
        "Informed consent",
        "Population",
        "Random sample"
      ],
      "correctText": "Population",
      "topic": "Sampling + Ethics",
      "explanation": "The population is the complete group about whom researchers want to draw conclusions — it could be all American adults, all 6-year-olds, or all patients with PTSD. Because studying an entire population is usually impossible, researchers draw samples. The quality of those generalizations depends on how representative the sample is; a biased sample produces misleading inferences about the population.",
      "domain": "Review",
      "gradeBand": "Multi",
