      "prompt": "Statistics used to judge whether results are likely meaningful beyond the sample.",
      "choices": [
        "Sample",
        "Inferential statistics",
        "Secure attachment",
        "Random sample"
      ],
      "correctText": "Inferential statistics",
      "topic": "Sampling + Ethics",
      "explanation": "Inferential statistics are used to draw conclusions about a population from a sample, including determining whether observed differences likely reflect true effects or random chance. The p-value (typically p <.05) is the probability of getting results at least as extreme if the null hypothesis were true. AP exam items test whether students understand that statistical significance does not equal practical importance or large effect size.",
