      "prompt": "Overestimating internal traits and underestimating situations when explaining others' behavior.",
      "choices": [
        "Fundamental attribution error",
        "Mean",
        "Big Five",
        "DSM-5-TR"
      ],
      "correctText": "Fundamental attribution error",
      "topic": "Social + Mental Health",
      "explanation": "The fundamental attribution error (FAE) is the systematic tendency to overestimate dispositional (personality) factors and underestimate situational ones when explaining others' behavior. Jones and Harris showed people attributed essay positions to writers' true beliefs even when told positions were assigned. The actor-observer asymmetry extends this: we attribute others' behavior to personality but our own to circumstances. Milgram's obedience research is the classic demonstration that situations powerfully override dispositions.",
