      "prompt": "Personality model using openness, conscientiousness, extraversion, agreeableness, and neuroticism.",
      "choices": [
        "Big Five",
        "Humanistic psychology",
        "Cognitive dissonance",
        "Fundamental attribution error"
      ],
      "correctText": "Big Five",
      "topic": "Social + Mental Health",
      "explanation": "The Big Five personality model (OCEAN: Openness, Conscientiousness, Extraversion, Agreeableness, Neuroticism) is the most empirically supported trait taxonomy, derived through factor analysis and replicated across cultures. High conscientiousness predicts academic and occupational success; high neuroticism predicts anxiety, depression, and relationship problems. Traits remain relatively stable across adulthood but personality generally becomes more conscientious and agreeable and less neurotic with age.",
