      "prompt": "Treatment approach focused on changing maladaptive thoughts and behaviors.",
      "choices": [
        "Cognitive dissonance",
        "Big Five",
        "Chunking",
        "Cognitive-behavioral therapy"
      ],
      "correctText": "Cognitive-behavioral therapy",
      "topic": "Social + Mental Health",
      "explanation": "CBT (Aaron Beck, Albert Ellis) targets the reciprocal relationship between maladaptive thoughts, feelings, and behaviors — identifying cognitive distortions (all-or-nothing thinking, catastrophizing, personalization) and challenging them through Socratic questioning and behavioral experiments. It is the most extensively researched psychotherapy and is evidence-based for depression, anxiety disorders, OCD, PTSD, eating disorders, and more. A typical course is 12-20 structured sessions, making it more time-limited than psychoanalysis.",
