      "choices": [
        "Hypothesis",
        "Availability heuristic",
        "Algorithm",
        "Prototype"
      ],
      "correctText": "Algorithm",
      "topic": "Thinking + Biases",
      "explanation": "An algorithm is a guaranteed problem-solving procedure that systematically considers all possibilities, always yielding the correct answer if one exists. For example, finding a word in a dictionary by checking every entry alphabetically is an algorithm. Unlike heuristics, algorithms guarantee accuracy but are slow and exhausting for complex problems. AP exam items often contrast algorithms (thorough, slow) with heuristics (fast, fallible) to test understanding of problem-solving tradeoffs.",
      "domain": "Review",
