      "explanation": "Salvador Dalí (1904-1989) is a high-frequency AP Spanish Language artista español. His surrealist masterpiece La persistencia de la memoria (1931) features los relojes derretidos (melting clocks). Dalí lived through la Guerra Civil and exile in the U.S. before returning to Cataluña. Vocabulary: el surrealismo, el subconsciente, los sueños, la realidad transformada, la imagen onírica. Other key Spanish surrealists: Joan Miró, Luis Buñuel (filmmaker). AP cultural comparison essays scoring 5 link Dalí's surrealism to political turmoil of 1930s Europe and to surrealist movements in Latin America (e.g., Remedios Varo, Leonora Carrington).",
