      "explanation": "El cuadro (or la pintura) is core AP Spanish Language vocabulary for visual arts sources. Related: el lienzo (canvas), el óleo (oil paint), la acuarela (watercolor), el dibujo (drawing), el bosquejo (sketch). Verbs: pintar, dibujar, retratar (to portray), representar. AP interpretive sources include cuadros by Velázquez, Goya, Picasso, Dalí, Miró, Frida Kahlo, Diego Rivera, and Botero, each tied to a specific país de origen. Useful expressions: el cuadro representa, el artista pintó, la obra refleja. AP cultural comparison essays scoring 5 analyze a cuadro hispano alongside a comparable work from the student's community.",
