      "correctText": "El Bosco",
      "topic": "Arte Hispano",
      "explanation": "El Bosco (Hieronymus Bosch, c.1450-1516) is a recurring AP Spanish Language Golden Age master (although Dutch, his works hang in el Prado in Madrid and influenced Spanish art). El jardín de las delicias (The Garden of Earthly Delights, c.1490-1510) is a triptych depicting Paradise, sin, and Hell. Vocabulary: el tríptico, la moral cristiana, la fantasía, el pecado, el infierno. AP interpretive sources connect el Bosco to Spanish religious iconography in colonial Latin America (e.g., Cuzco school, Capilla Sixtina paintings). AP cultural comparison essays scoring 5 explore how religious art served pedagogical purposes in the Hispanic world.",
