      "correctText": "Guillermo del Toro",
      "topic": "Gender and LGBTQ+",
      "explanation": "Guillermo del Toro (born 1964) is a major AP Spanish Language héroe cultural in cine. His films (El laberinto del fauno / Pan's Labyrinth 2006, La forma del agua / The Shape of Water 2017 Oscar Best Picture, Pinocho 2022) blend fantasía with critique of fascism and marginal voices. Vocabulary: el cine, la película, el director, el guion (screenplay), el premio (award), el Óscar. Other Hispanic film auteurs on the exam: Alfonso Cuarón (Roma), Alejandro González Iñárritu (Birdman), Pedro Almodóvar (Spain). Cultural comparison essays scoring 5 examine how Hispanic directors reshape global cinema.",
