      "correctText": "la comunidad LGBTQ",
      "topic": "Gender and LGBTQ+",
      "explanation": "La comunidad LGBTQ (sometimes LGBTI+ in Spanish-speaking countries) describes lesbianas, gais, bisexuales, transgénero, queer, and intersex people. AP Spanish Language interpretive sources discuss the legalización del matrimonio igualitario in Spain (2005), Argentina (2010), México (state by state), and Colombia. Vocabulary: salir del armario (to come out), la orientación sexual, la identidad de género, el orgullo gay, la discriminación, los derechos. AP cultural comparison essays scoring 5 contrast LGBTQ rights timelines and current debates in Hispanic countries vs. the United States.",
