      "explanation": "La herencia indígena is essential AP Spanish Language cultural content. Modern Spanish-speaking populations often acknowledge raíces indígenas: maya in Guatemala/Yucatán, quechua/aymara in Peru/Bolivia/Ecuador, mapuche in Chile, náhuatl in México. Vocabulary: los pueblos originarios (original peoples), las lenguas indígenas, la cosmovisión (worldview), la mestizaje (mixing). AP interpretive readings examine government policies, language preservation, and indigenous-led movements. Cultural comparison essays scoring 5 connect herencia indígena to similar movements in your own community (e.g., Native American identity, Hawaiian sovereignty).",
