      "explanation": "Los padrinos (godparents) and the broader system of compadrazgo are key Hispanic cultural concepts on the AP exam. Padrinos serve at baptism (el bautizo), confirmation, and at weddings; they form a lifelong bond with both the child (el ahijado / la ahijada) and the parents (compadres). This kinship-by-choice system is especially strong in México, Centroamérica, and the Andes. Expect interpretive readings about quinceañeras or bodas to use padrinos, madrina, and compadrazgo. AP free-response prompts may ask you to compare padrinos to mentor relationships in your own culture.",
