      "explanation": "Criar means to raise or rear children, while educar means to formally instruct or school them. The noun la crianza refers to the entire process of child-rearing. AP Spanish Language sources often debate styles of crianza: estricta vs. permisiva, tradicional vs. moderna. Expect interpersonal speaking prompts asking your opinion about cómo deben los padres criar a sus hijos. Useful collocations: criar con valores, crianza positiva, hijos bien criados. Tense note: criar is a regular -ar verb; the preterite of criar means raised (one-time action), the imperfect means used to raise (ongoing past).",
