      "explanation": "La familia is a foundational AP Spanish Language theme. In many Hispanic cultures, la familia extends beyond the nuclear unit (padres e hijos) to include abuelos, tíos, primos, and padrinos. AP interpretive readings frequently contrast la familia tradicional with la familia moderna, exploring divorcio, familias monoparentales, and uniones civiles. On the exam, expect text and audio sources comparing family structures across Spain, México, and the Caribbean. Cultural comparison essays (presentational writing) often ask students to compare la familia in their own community with one in the Spanish-speaking world.",
