      "topic": "Literatura Hispana",
      "explanation": "Miguel de Cervantes (1547-1616) is a foundational AP Spanish Language author. Don Quijote de la Mancha (Part I 1605, Part II 1615) is widely considered the first modern novel, blending parody of caballerías (chivalric romances) with deep meditation on idealismo y realismo. Vocabulary: el hidalgo, el caballero andante (knight errant), el escudero (squire), los molinos de viento (windmills), la locura (madness). Famous characters: Don Quijote (Alonso Quijano), Sancho Panza, Dulcinea del Toboso, Rocinante (horse). AP cultural comparison essays scoring 5 examine how Don Quijote shaped global literary tradition.",
