      "explanation": "Pablo Neruda (1904-1973) is a major AP Spanish Language Chilean poeta, winner of the 1971 Premio Nobel de Literatura. Veinte poemas de amor y una canción desesperada (1924) made him famous as a young writer. Canto general (1950) traced Latin American history. He served as a senator and diplomat and died days after Pinochet's golpe de estado in 1973. Vocabulary: la poesía, el verso, la estrofa, la metáfora, el amor, la nostalgia, la política. AP interpretive sources include Neruda's love poems and his political odas. Cultural comparison essays scoring 5 examine how Neruda blended romance and revolution.",
