      "topic": "Literatura Hispana",
      "explanation": "Gabriel García Márquez (1927-2014), nicknamed Gabo, is a central AP Spanish Language author. His novel Cien años de soledad (1967) launched el realismo mágico globally, weaving Macondo's Buendía family through historia y mito. He won the Premio Nobel de Literatura in 1982. Other works: El amor en los tiempos del cólera, Crónica de una muerte anunciada, La hojarasca. Vocabulary: el realismo mágico, la saga familiar, la historia latinoamericana, el sincretismo. AP interpretive sources frequently include Gabo excerpts. Cultural comparison essays scoring 5 connect magical realism to Latin American identity and to U.S. counterparts (Toni Morrison).",
