      "correctText": "Mario Molina",
      "topic": "Medio Ambiente",
      "explanation": "Mario Molina (1943-2020) is a major AP Spanish Language Hispanic scientist. He shared the 1995 Premio Nobel de Química for showing how chlorofluorocarbons (CFCs) destroy the capa de ozono. His research led to the Montreal Protocol (1987), a global treaty phasing out CFCs that proves international environmental cooperation can work. Vocabulary: la capa de ozono, los CFCs, el calentamiento global, el cambio climático, el medio ambiente, la atmósfera. Useful expressions: contribuir a la ciencia, ganar el Nobel, salvar el planeta. Cultural comparison essays scoring 5 connect Molina's work to broader Hispanic contributions to climate science.",
