      "correctText": "el Mercosur",
      "topic": "Medio Ambiente Global",
      "explanation": "El Mercosur (Mercado Común del Sur) is a major AP Spanish Language regional integration project. Founded in 1991 by Argentina, Brazil, Paraguay, and Uruguay; Venezuela and Bolivia are members (Venezuela suspended); Chile, Colombia, Ecuador, Peru, Guyana, Suriname are associate. Mercosur aims to remove trade barriers, coordinate macroeconomic policy, and present a unified front in global negotiations. Vocabulary: la integración regional, el libre comercio, los aranceles (tariffs), la moneda común, la cooperación. Compared to: la Unión Europea (deeper integration), USMCA (NAFTA successor), CAN (Comunidad Andina). Cultural comparison essays scoring 5 examine integration tradeoffs.",
