      "explanation": "Víctor Jara (1932-1973) is a critical AP Spanish Language Chilean folk singer associated with la Nueva Canción Chilena. A supporter of Salvador Allende, he was tortured and killed by Pinochet's forces days after the 11 de septiembre golpe de estado of 1973. His song Te recuerdo Amanda became a Latin American protest anthem. Vocabulary: la Nueva Canción, la canción protesta, la dictadura, el golpe de estado, la memoria histórica, los derechos humanos. Cultural comparison essays scoring 5 link Jara to similar protest singers globally (Bob Dylan, Joan Baez) and to art's role in resisting authoritarianism.",
