      "explanation": "Los Sanfermines (festival of San Fermín, Pamplona, July 6-14) feature the encierro (bull run) and AP Spanish Language interpretive sources analyze them critically. The fiesta combines religious procession (San Fermín is patron saint), bullfighting (la corrida), white-and-red dress code, music, and partying. Vocabulary: el toro, el torero, la corrida, la fiesta patronal, el santo patrón, los riesgos (risks). Useful expressions: lanzar el chupinazo, vestirse de blanco y rojo. Debate: defender la tradición vs. proteger los derechos animales. Cultural comparison essays scoring 5 weigh tradition and contemporary ethics.",
