      "topic": "Ocio y Deportes",
      "explanation": "El béisbol (or la pelota in Cuban Spanish) dominates AP Spanish Language sources about Caribbean sport. The Dominican Republic, Cuba, Puerto Rico, Venezuela, and Panamá produce more MLB players per capita than any country. Stars: Pedro Martínez, David Ortiz, Albert Pujols, Roberto Clemente, José Altuve. Vocabulary: el lanzador (pitcher), el bateador (batter), el jonrón (home run), el equipo, la temporada. Useful expressions: jugar en las Grandes Ligas, firmar un contrato. Cultural comparison essays scoring 5 examine how béisbol connects Caribbean communities to U.S. immigration and economic mobility.",
