      "correctText": "el franquismo",
      "topic": "Paz y Conflicto",
      "explanation": "El franquismo (1939-1975) is a major AP Spanish Language Spanish-history concept. After winning la Guerra Civil (1936-1939), Francisco Franco ruled Spain as caudillo: censorship, repression of regional identities (catalán, vasco, gallego banned), one-party rule, Catholic conservatism. After his 1975 death, Spain transitioned to democracy under King Juan Carlos. Vocabulary: la dictadura, el caudillo, la represión, los exiliados, la transición democrática, la Ley de Memoria Histórica, las fosas comunes (mass graves). Cultural comparison essays scoring 5 examine ongoing debates about Spain's memoria histórica.",
