      "topic": "Paz y Conflicto",
      "explanation": "El zapatismo (EZLN - Ejército Zapatista de Liberación Nacional) launched a major AP Spanish Language indigenous-rights uprising on January 1, 1994 (day NAFTA took effect) in Chiapas, Mexico. Led by the masked Subcomandante Marcos, the movement demands tierra, libertad, justicia for indigenous communities and global anti-neoliberalism. Vocabulary: los pueblos indígenas, la autonomía, los derechos colectivos, los caracoles (Zapatista communities), el neoliberalismo, la globalización. Useful expressions: defender la tierra, exigir justicia. Cultural comparison essays scoring 5 connect zapatismo to indigenous movements across the Americas.",
