      "topic": "Salud y Medicina",
      "explanation": "La medicina tradicional (or la herbolaria) refers to indigenous and folk healing practices using plantas medicinales and ritual. AP Spanish Language interpretive sources discuss how mayan, aymara, and quechua healing traditions persist alongside biomedicine. Vocabulary: el curandero (healer), las hierbas, el remedio casero, la sabiduría ancestral, las plantas medicinales. Useful expressions: tratar con hierbas, recurrir a la medicina ancestral. Cultural comparison essays scoring 5 examine how integrative medicine (la medicina integrativa) bridges traditional and scientific approaches in Hispanic communities and contrast with U.S. holistic medicine trends.",
