      "explanation": "La comedia nueva is the AP Spanish Literature dramatic form Lope de Vega systematized in his Arte nuevo de hacer comedias (1609). Features: 3 acts (instead of classical 5), polymetric verse (different meters for different effects: romance for narration, redondillas for dialogue, sonnets for soliloquy, décimas for lament), mixing of tragic and comic, freedom from Aristotelian unities, popular and aristocratic characters. Fuenteovejuna demonstrates these features. Vocabulary: el verso polimétrico, el acto, la acotación (stage direction), el gracioso (comic servant). AP analysis essays score 5 by examining how Lope's metric choices match scene types and how the form's flexibility enables collective protagonism.",
