      "explanation": "La representación del otro and la alteridad are essential AP Spanish Literature critical concepts. Colonial-era texts (Cortés, Cabeza de Vaca) depict indigenous peoples through European lenses, often blending awe with dehumanization. Modern post-colonial criticism (Edward Said's Orientalism, Walter Mignolo, Mary Louise Pratt's contact zone) interrogates how texts construct el otro. Strategies: physical description, comparison with European categories, attribution of language and culture, silencing of indigenous voice. AP analysis essays score 5 by comparing representation across texts: Cortés's strategic awe at Tenochtitlán vs. Cabeza de Vaca's gradual identification with his hosts vs. Bolívar's homogenizing 'we'.",
