      "explanation": "La novela picaresca is the AP Spanish Literature genre originated by El Lazarillo de Tormes (1554). Features: first-person autobiographical narration by a low-class protagonist (el pícaro), episodic structure following service to a series of masters, satire of social institutions, hunger as constant motivation, moral ambiguity, epistolary frame addressed to a superior. Later picaresque novels: Guzmán de Alfarache (Mateo Alemán), El Buscón (Quevedo), La pícara Justina, Estebanillo González. Theme connections: las relaciones interpersonales (master/servant), la dualidad del ser (apparent innocence vs. cynical strategy), la construcción del género (gender constraints). AP analysis essays score 5 by tracing the form's conventions.",
