      "correctText": "Variability",
      "topic": "Bias and Variability",
      "explanation": "Variability is the spread of an estimator's sampling distribution - typically measured by its standard error (SE). AP Statistics Unit 5 emphasizes that low variability means the estimator is consistent: across many samples, estimates cluster tightly around the parameter. The 2019 FRQ tested variability assessment in choosing between estimators: a lower-variability estimator is more precise, all else equal. Rubric points required citing both unbiasedness AND low variability as criteria for choosing an estimator. Variability decreases with sample size n: typically SE proportional to 1/sqrt(n), so quadrupling n halves SE.",
