      "correctText": "Response bias",
      "topic": "Bias Types",
      "explanation": "Response bias occurs when respondents answer untruthfully or inaccurately - due to social desirability (lying about drug use or income), recall error (mis-remembering past events), or interviewer effects (face-to-face questions about race elicit different responses than anonymous web surveys). AP Statistics Unit 3 emphasizes that response bias is hard to detect and even harder to fix. The 2019 FRQ tested a face-to-face survey about cheating in school - rubric points were awarded for identifying that students likely under-report cheating in person but might respond truthfully in an anonymous online survey, suggesting a methodological fix.",
      "domain": "Review",
      "gradeBand": "Multi",
