      "correctText": "Nonresponse bias",
      "topic": "Bias Types",
      "explanation": "Non-response bias occurs when individuals selected for the sample refuse to respond or cannot be reached, AND the non-responders differ systematically from responders in ways relevant to the survey. AP Statistics Unit 3 emphasizes that non-response is distinct from undercoverage: in non-response, the individuals are in the frame and were selected but did not participate. The 2018 FRQ included a mail survey with 30 percent response rate - students earned full credit for identifying non-response bias and proposing follow-up calls or incentives. Modern surveys with response rates below 10 percent (e.g., political polls) are especially vulnerable.",
