      "correctText": "Binomial distribution",
      "topic": "Binomial Distribution",
      "explanation": "The binomial distribution describes the number of successes X in n independent trials, each with probability p of success. AP Statistics Unit 4 emphasizes that the binomial has 2 parameters (n, p), takes values 0 through n, and has probability mass function P(X = k) = C(n,k) * p^k * (1-p)^(n-k). The 2019 FRQ tested binomial computation: P(at least 3 successes in 10 trials, p = 0.4) - rubric points required either explicit binomial PDF summation or use of 1 - binomcdf with correct bounds. The binomial arises whenever a fixed number of independent yes/no trials are aggregated.",
      "domain": "Review",
      "gradeBand": "Multi",
