      "correctText": "Negative 1 to 1",
      "topic": "Correlation",
      "explanation": "The correlation coefficient r is always bounded -1 <= r <= 1. AP Statistics Unit 2 explains: r = +1 means a perfect positive linear relationship (all points on a line with positive slope); r = -1 means a perfect negative linear relationship; r = 0 means no linear association (but possibly a curved relationship). The bounds follow from r being defined as a covariance divided by the product of standard deviations, which by the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality cannot exceed 1 in magnitude. The 2018 FRQ tested boundary intuition: students were asked to interpret r = -0.97 between hours of TV and exam scores - earning rubric points for citing both strength and the negative direction.",
