      "correctText": "z-score",
      "topic": "Data Analysis",
      "explanation": "A z-score z = (x - mu)/sigma standardizes an observation by expressing its distance from the mean in units of standard deviation. AP Statistics Unit 1 introduces z-scores, which are foundational throughout the course. The 2019 FRQ tested z-score comparison: SAT score 1400 (mu = 1000, sigma = 200) gives z = 2; ACT score 30 (mu = 21, sigma = 4) gives z = 2.25. The ACT score is relatively higher because its z-score is larger. Rubric points required showing both z-scores AND explicit comparison. Z-scores are unitless and enable comparison across distributions.",
