      "correctText": "Ogive",
      "topic": "Distributions",
      "explanation": "An ogive (pronounced 'oh-jive') is a cumulative relative frequency plot - the x-axis shows variable values and the y-axis shows the proportion of observations at or below each x. The curve always rises monotonically from 0 to 1 and resembles a stretched-out 'S' for Normal data. AP Stats Unit 1 uses ogives to read off percentiles directly: to find the median, locate y = 0.5 and read the corresponding x. The 2015 FRQ asked students to identify quartiles and the IQR from an ogive. Ogives also let students compare two distributions: the curve farther to the right indicates higher values.",
