      "prompt": "Interval estimate.",
      "choices": [
        "Mutually exclusive",
        "x-bar",
        "Confidence interval",
        "s over sqrt n"
      ],
      "correctText": "Confidence interval",
      "topic": "Estimating Mean",
      "explanation": "A confidence interval provides an INTERVAL estimate of the population mean, combining the point estimate x-bar with a margin of error: x-bar plus or minus t*-times-(s/sqrt(n)). AP Statistics Unit 7 emphasizes that CIs are the standard interval estimate for means. The 2018 FRQ tested CI interpretation: 'we are 95 percent confident the true mean lies between [low] and [high].' Rubric points required (a) the interval, (b) the confidence level, and (c) the parameter being estimated (population mean) - in context. CIs communicate both the estimate AND the uncertainty in one statement.",
