      "prompt": "Point estimate of population mean.",
      "choices": [
        "Increases power",
        "s over sqrt n",
        "x-bar",
        "Narrower CI"
      ],
      "correctText": "x-bar",
      "topic": "Estimating Mean",
      "explanation": "The point estimate of the population mean mu is the sample mean x-bar. AP Statistics Unit 7 emphasizes that x-bar is the best single estimate of mu - unbiased and (under Normal populations) the most efficient. The 2019 FRQ tested point-estimate identification: for a sample with x-bar = 75.2, the point estimate of mu is 75.2. Rubric points required citing x-bar (not the median or any robust estimator). Combined with the SE = s/sqrt(n), the point estimate forms the center of a confidence interval. Point estimates alone are insufficient for inference - they need a CI or hypothesis test to convey uncertainty.",
