      "correctText": "Response variable",
      "topic": "Experimental Design",
      "explanation": "The response variable in an experiment is the outcome measured to assess treatment effects - the experimental analog of the dependent variable. AP Statistics Unit 3 emphasizes that the response should be: (1) clearly defined, (2) measurable, (3) sensitive to the treatment, and (4) relevant to the research question. The 2018 FRQ tested a weight-loss experiment with response variable 'change in body weight (kg) after 12 weeks' - rubric points required specifying units AND a time frame. Vague responses like 'health improvement' lose points. The choice of response can dramatically affect the experiment's conclusions.",
