      "correctText": "Interpolation",
      "topic": "Extrapolation and Influence",
      "explanation": "Interpolation is using a regression model to predict y for x values WITHIN the observed range. AP Statistics Unit 9 emphasizes interpolation as the reliable use of regression - the model has been validated over this range. The 2018 FRQ tested interpolation vs extrapolation: predicting cricket chirps at temperatures within the observed range (60-90 F) is interpolation; predicting at 100 F is extrapolation. Rubric points required correctly classifying predictions AND explaining the reliability difference. Interpolation is the standard, reliable use of regression; extrapolation always warrants caution.",
