      "correctText": "Paired t-test",
      "topic": "Matched Pairs",
      "explanation": "The paired t-test analyzes matched-pairs data by computing the differences d_i = X1_i - X2_i within each pair, then applying a one-sample t-test to the differences with H0: mu_d = 0. AP Statistics Unit 7 emphasizes the parallel: paired t-test = one-sample t-test on differences. The 2019 FRQ tested paired t computation: t = (d-bar - 0)/(s_d/sqrt(n)) with df = n - 1 (number of PAIRS minus 1). Rubric points required computing the test statistic correctly AND citing df based on number of pairs. Confusing paired and two-sample procedures is the most common error in Unit 7.",
