      "correctText": "Empirical Rule",
      "topic": "Normal Distribution",
      "explanation": "The Empirical Rule (68-95-99.7) states that for any Normal distribution, approximately 68 percent of data lie within 1 SD of the mean, 95 percent within 2 SD, and 99.7 percent within 3 SD. AP Statistics Unit 4 uses this rule for fast probability estimates without z-tables. The 2019 FRQ tested Empirical Rule application: a Normal weight distribution with mu = 175, sigma = 20 - what percent are above 215? Since 215 = mu + 2*sigma, approximately 2.5 percent are above (half of 5 percent). Rubric points required correctly applying the symmetry: the rule says 95 percent are WITHIN 2 SD, so 5 percent are outside, split equally between the two tails.",
