      "correctText": "Mean 0 SD 1",
      "topic": "Normal Distribution",
      "explanation": "The standard Normal distribution N(0, 1) has mean 0 and standard deviation 1. AP Statistics Unit 4 emphasizes that any Normal random variable X with mean mu and SD sigma can be standardized to Z = (X - mu)/sigma, which follows the standard Normal. This transformation lets students use a single table (or calculator function) to compute all Normal probabilities, regardless of mu and sigma. The 2018 FRQ tested standardization: a Normal IQ distribution with mu = 100, sigma = 15 - 'find P(X > 130)' requires Z = (130 - 100)/15 = 2, then P(Z > 2) = 0.0228 from tables. Rubric points awarded for correct standardization step.",
