      "correctText": "Observational study",
      "topic": "Observational Studies",
      "explanation": "An observational study collects data on subjects without manipulating any variable - the researcher observes naturally occurring values of both explanatory and response variables. AP Statistics Unit 3 emphasizes the key limitation: observational studies CANNOT establish causation because confounding variables may explain any observed association. The 2018 FRQ contrasted an observational study (smokers vs non-smokers and lung cancer) with an impossible-to-conduct experiment (random assignment to smoke), awarding points for noting that the observational evidence remains correlational - causation was ultimately established through multiple convergent lines including dose-response and biological mechanism (Doll & Hill 1950s).",
