      "topic": "Sampling Distribution of Difference",
      "explanation": "The standard error of the difference p1-hat minus p2-hat is SE = sqrt(p1*(1-p1)/n1 + p2*(1-p2)/n2). This formula assumes independent samples and uses the fact that the variance of a difference of independent random variables is the sum of their variances. AP Statistics Unit 5 emphasizes this 'sum of variances' formula as the foundation for two-sample inference. The 2019 FRQ tested SE computation in a smoking-rate comparison: SE was used to construct a confidence interval for p1 - p2. Rubric points required correct SE formula AND independence justification. For hypothesis tests (Unit 6), a pooled estimate replaces p1, p2 with a single combined p-hat.",
