      "topic": "Sampling Distribution of p-hat",
      "explanation": "The Large Counts condition requires both np >= 10 AND n(1-p) >= 10 to use the Normal approximation for the sampling distribution of p-hat. AP Statistics Unit 5 emphasizes this as essential before applying any Normal-based inference for proportions in Units 6 and 8. The 2018 FRQ tested this condition: for p = 0.05 and n = 100, np = 5 fails Large Counts, so Normal approximation is invalid. Rubric points required checking BOTH parts of the condition, not just one. When Large Counts fails, exact binomial methods or larger samples are needed. The threshold of 10 is conventional; some texts use 5.",
