      "explanation": "The sampling distribution of p-hat is the probability distribution of the sample proportion p-hat across all possible samples of size n from a population with proportion p. AP Statistics Unit 5 introduces this as the foundation for inference about proportions in Units 6 and 8. By the CLT, p-hat is approximately Normal when the Large Counts condition (np >= 10 and n(1-p) >= 10) holds. The 2019 FRQ tested sampling distribution recognition: for a population proportion p = 0.4 and n = 100, the sampling distribution of p-hat is approximately N(0.4, sqrt(0.4*0.6/100)) = N(0.4, 0.049). Rubric points required citing both the mean AND the SD.",
