      "topic": "Sampling Distribution of p-hat",
      "explanation": "The 10 percent condition (also called the independence condition) requires that the sample size n be no more than 10 percent of the population size N: n <= 0.10*N. AP Statistics Unit 5 introduces this rule to ensure approximate independence when sampling WITHOUT replacement from a finite population. The 2019 FRQ docked points for students who applied Normal inference to a sample of 500 from a population of 1000 - the 10 percent condition fails (50 percent of population), so the simple SD formula overstates variability. Rubric points required citing both Large Counts AND 10 percent conditions before applying Normal approximation in inference for proportions.",
