      "topic": "Standardization",
      "explanation": "The Empirical Rule (68-95-99.7 rule) states that for any Normal distribution, approximately 68 percent of data fall within 1 SD of the mean, 95 percent within 2 SD, and 99.7 percent within 3 SD. Introduced in AP Stats Unit 1, this rule is a fast approximation that avoids the need for z-tables when the question matches integer SD boundaries exactly. The rule fails for non-Normal distributions - students must verify approximate Normality from histograms, dotplots, or Normal probability plots first. The 2017 FRQ asked students to apply the rule to a Normal IQ distribution (mean 100, SD 15) to find the proportion of scores above 130.",
