      "explanation": "A signing statement is a written pronouncement issued by a president when signing a bill into law, sometimes asserting that the administration will not enforce provisions it considers unconstitutional. George W. Bush dramatically expanded their use, issuing over 1,200 signing statements challenging ~1,100 provisions. Critics argue they undermine the rule of law and circumvent the veto process; AP Gov Unit 2 links signing statements to the unitary executive theory and executive branch power relative to Congress.",
