      "correctText": "elevation",
      "topic": "Climate Controls",
      "explanation": "As elevation increases, air pressure drops and air expands, cooling at roughly 6.5 °C per 1,000 m — the environmental lapse rate listed in the ESRT. This is why mountaintops stay cold even in tropical latitudes. Denver, at ~1,600 m, averages about 10 °C cooler than coastal cities at the same latitude. High-altitude climates can differ dramatically from nearby lowlands.",
