      "topic": "Climate Controls",
      "explanation": "Latitude measures how far north or south of the equator a location sits. Near the equator, the sun's rays strike at a high angle year-round, delivering intense insolation. Toward the poles, rays arrive at a low angle and spread over more surface, reducing heating. Latitude is the single strongest predictor of a region's average temperature.",
