      "explanation": "Ocean currents redistribute heat globally. Warm currents (e.g., Gulf Stream) carry tropical water poleward, raising coastal winter temperatures. Cold currents (e.g., California Current) bring upwelled deep water equatorward, cooling and drying adjacent coastlines. Western Europe's mild winters despite high latitude are largely due to the warm North Atlantic Current.",
