      "explanation": "Infiltration is the movement of water from the surface downward into soil and rock pores. Rate depends on soil texture, vegetation cover, moisture content, and slope. When rainfall intensity exceeds the infiltration rate, excess water runs off the surface. Infiltration replenishes groundwater and reduces flood peaks — vegetation promotes infiltration far better than pavement.",
