      "correctText": "evaporation",
      "topic": "Cycle Processes",
      "explanation": "Evaporation is the phase change from liquid water to water vapor at a water's surface. It is driven by solar energy and depends on temperature, surface area, wind speed, and vapor pressure difference between the water and overlying air. Oceans are the largest source of atmospheric water vapor. Higher temperatures accelerate evaporation, intensifying the water cycle.",
