      "correctText": "condensation",
      "topic": "Cycle Processes",
      "explanation": "Condensation is the phase change from water vapor to liquid water. It occurs when air cools below its dew point — the temperature at which air is saturated. Condensation onto dust or sea-salt particles (condensation nuclei) forms cloud droplets. Clouds, fog, and dew all result from condensation. Without nuclei, supersaturated air could not easily form droplets.",
