      "topic": "Cycle Processes",
      "explanation": "Transpiration is the release of water vapor through tiny pores (stomata) in plant leaves. Forests return enormous amounts of water to the atmosphere — a large oak can transpire over 100 liters per day. Combined with evaporation, it is called evapotranspiration (ET). Vegetation type and density strongly influence how much precipitation is recycled locally vs. becoming runoff.",
