      "explanation": "The focus (hypocenter) is the point inside Earth where rock first ruptures and seismic energy is released. Shallow-focus earthquakes (<70 km) occur at all plate boundaries; deep-focus events (>300 km) occur only in subducting slabs. The NYS ESRT provides the P/S-wave travel-time graph; distance to the focus is calculated from P–S arrival-time lag at three seismic stations, then triangulated to locate the event's position.",
