      "explanation": "P-waves (Primary/compressional) are the fastest seismic body waves, arriving first at seismographs and traveling through solids, liquids, and gases. The NYS ESRT travel-time graph plots P-wave arrival versus distance — use it to compute earthquake distance from arrival lag. P-waves pass through both the liquid outer core and solid inner core, so they alone cannot confirm whether the outer core is molten.",
