      "explanation": "Seismic stations record ground motion; the P–S arrival lag at each is converted to distance using the NYS ESRT travel-time graph. Three stations are required for triangulation to locate the epicenter. The global network built after WWII confirmed plate-boundary locations and revealed Wadati- Benioff deep-focus earthquake zones above subducting slabs, supporting Hess's seafloor-spreading model.",
