      "correctText": "isotherm",
      "topic": "Energy Balance Evidence",
      "explanation": "An isotherm is a line on a weather or climate map connecting all points with the same temperature at a given time or averaged over a period. On NYS Regents station-model problems, isotherms reveal temperature gradients (Fourier's ΔT/Δd concept applied to the atmosphere). Closely spaced isotherms indicate a steep temperature gradient — a strong front. Isotherms also curve with ocean currents, showing how advection of joules by water redistributes thermal energy across Earth's surface.",
