      "explanation": "Running water is Earth's dominant erosional agent, responsible for most stream valleys, floodplains, and deltas. The NYS ESRT 'Relationship of Transported Particle Size to Water Velocity' graph shows that faster streams carry larger particles. Hutton and Lyell both argued rivers shape entire continents. The Hudson River valley is a classic NYS example of stream-cut erosional landscape still active today.",
