      "explanation": "Soil saturation occurs when all pore spaces are filled with water, leaving no infiltration capacity. Once saturated, even light rainfall becomes 100% runoff. Saturation commonly follows prolonged rain or rapid snowmelt. Antecedent moisture — how wet the soil was before a storm — is a key predictor of runoff volume and flash-flood risk.",
