      "explanation": "Lag time is the delay between peak rainfall and peak stream discharge on a hydrograph. Short lag times occur in small, steep, urbanized basins where water reaches the channel quickly. Long lag times occur in large, flat, forested basins. Engineers use lag time to design culverts and flood-control structures. Restoring wetlands and reducing impervious cover lengthen lag time.",
