      "explanation": "Trace fossils preserve behavior—footprints, burrows, feeding trails, coprolites—rather than body parts. They record an organism's activity and can reveal locomotion style and sediment conditions even when no body fossil survives. A dinosaur trackway in Triassic mudstone proves the animal was alive there. Regents items distinguish trace from body fossils; both count as fossil evidence of past life on the NYS ESRT Geologic History page.",
