      "explanation": "The Law of Fossil Succession (William Smith, 1815) states that fossil species appear and disappear in the same vertical order worldwide—allowing correlation of rock units across continents without radiometric dates. Each geologic period on the NYS ESRT Geologic History page is characterized by distinctive organisms. Regents items may show two separated outcrops and ask students to use index fossils to determine which layers are the same age.",
