      "explanation": "An index fossil belongs to an organism that lived briefly but spread globally, so its presence identifies a specific time interval. William Smith (1815) pioneered the technique correlating English coal strata. NYS examples: trilobites (Cambrian–Permian), Eurypterids (Silurian state fossil). The ESRT Geologic History page lists characteristic fossils by period; recognizing them is a core Regents skill for dating and correlating rock layers.",
