      "correctText": "astronomical unit",
      "topic": "Reference Table Space Data",
      "explanation": "One astronomical unit (AU) = mean Earth-Sun distance ≈ 1.5 × 10⁸ km. Copernicus (1543) used relative AU distances to scale the solar system without knowing the actual km value. The NYS ESRT Solar System Data table lists each planet's mean distance in AU (Mars ≈ 1.52 AU; Neptune ≈ 30.07 AU). Regents items ask students to read the table, convert, or compare distances and identify which unit applies to intra-solar-system measurements.",
