      "correctText": "light-year",
      "topic": "Reference Table Space Data",
      "explanation": "One light-year ≈ 9.46 × 10¹² km — the distance light travels in one year at 3 × 10⁸ m/s. The NYS ESRT uses light-years for distances beyond the solar system (Proxima Centauri ≈ 4.2 ly; the observable universe ≈ 46 billion ly in radius). The Big Bang occurred ~13.8 billion years ago. Regents items ask which unit — AU or light-year — is appropriate for a given scale, or compare the relative sizes of the solar system versus the galaxy.",
