      "prompt": "Grid of latitude and longitude lines used to locate any point on Earth's surface.",
      "choices": [
        "coordinate system",
        "eccentricity",
        "dynamic equilibrium",
        "occluded front"
      ],
      "correctText": "coordinate system",
      "topic": "Regents Calculations",
      "explanation": "A coordinate system uses intersecting reference lines to locate points. In Earth Science, latitude and longitude form the coordinate system for Earth's surface: latitude measures degrees north or south of the equator (0°–90°); longitude measures degrees east or west of the Prime Meridian (0°–180°). The ESRT includes maps with latitude/longitude grids. Regents questions ask students to locate cities, earthquakes, and plate boundaries using these coordinates.",
