      "explanation": "Cloud cover on a station model is shown by how much of the central circle is filled in. ESRT p. 13 gives the standard key: empty circle = clear (0/8 sky); half-filled = scattered (4/8); completely filled = overcast (8/8). Intermediate fills indicate partly cloudy conditions. Regents questions may show a station model and ask students to describe sky conditions or to match the symbol to a weather description.",
