      "correctText": "dew point",
      "topic": "Station Models",
      "explanation": "Dew point temperature, plotted in the lower left of a station model in °F or °C, is the temperature to which air must cool (at constant pressure and moisture) before water vapor begins to condense. A high dew point signals humid air; below-freezing dew points indicate very dry air. Using the dew point and temperature together with the ESRT Relative Humidity table (p. 12) allows calculation of relative humidity.",
