      "correctText": "watershed",
      "topic": "Stream Systems",
      "explanation": "A watershed (drainage basin) is the land area that drains to a common outlet — a river, lake, or ocean. Every point on Earth belongs to exactly one watershed. Ridges and hills form divides separating basins. Land use within a watershed determines water quality: farms introduce nutrients; cities add impervious surfaces. Watershed management protects downstream drinking-water supplies.",
