      "correctText": "stream velocity",
      "topic": "Stream Systems",
      "explanation": "Stream velocity is the speed of water flow (m/s). It increases with steeper gradient, greater discharge, and smoother channel shape. Fast-moving water erodes and transports sediment; slower water deposits it. The ESRT erosion-transport-deposition diagram shows the critical velocity needed to move particles of different sizes — coarser particles require higher velocities.",
      "domain": "Review",
