      "correctText": "discharge",
      "topic": "Stream Systems",
      "explanation": "Discharge is the volume of water passing a stream cross-section per unit time (Q = A × v, in m³/s). It increases after rainfall and snowmelt, decreasing during dry periods when groundwater baseflow sustains the stream. Hydrographs plot discharge over time: a sharp high peak indicates flashy runoff; a broad low peak reflects a slow groundwater-fed response.",
      "domain": "Review",
