      "correctText": "groundwater model",
      "topic": "Surface Processes",
      "explanation": "The vadose (aeration) zone holds air and some water; below the water table the saturated zone is fully water-filled. The water table rises after rain and mimics surface topography. Confined aquifers are sandwiched between impermeable layers; artesian wells flow under natural pressure. Porosity and permeability control storage and flow. Regents cross-sections ask students to identify zones or explain why a well goes dry.",
