      "topic": "Surface Processes",
      "explanation": "Sediment deposits when transport energy drops. The ESRT 'Transported Particle Size vs. Water Velocity' graph shows gravel settling near the source and clay traveling farthest. Delta layers fine upward; glacial till is unsorted. Vertical grain-size sorting confirms superposition. Regents questions provide a sediment cross-section and ask students to infer current speed, transport direction, or depositional environment.",
