      "correctText": "topographic profile",
      "topic": "Surface Processes",
      "explanation": "A topographic profile is a side-view elevation drawing built by projecting contour values from a map to a graph. Students transfer each contour crossing to the grid, then connect points smoothly. Regents items provide a contour map, a labeled cross-section line, and a blank grid; students plot the profile. Close contour spacing = steep slope; wide spacing = gentle slope. Accurate reading of contour intervals is essential.",
