      "correctText": "watershed analysis",
      "topic": "Surface Processes",
      "explanation": "A watershed is the land area draining to a common outlet; its boundary follows ridge crests on a topographic map. Regents items provide a contour map and ask students to shade the watershed or identify which stream drains a given point. Stream gradient (rise ÷ run, in m/km) is calculated from contour maps and controls erosion rate—steep gradient = fast water = more erosive power.",
