      "topic": "Surface Processes",
      "explanation": "Each erosion agent leaves diagnostic landforms. Glaciers carve U-shaped valleys and leave striations and erratics; rivers cut V-shaped valleys with meanders; waves cut sea cliffs and stacks. ESRT landscape region maps provide regional context. Regents questions show a landform photo or cross-section and ask students to identify the agent from shape, deposit type, or particle sorting.",
