      "correctText": "index contour",
      "topic": "Topographic Maps",
      "explanation": "Every fifth contour line is drawn heavier and labeled with its elevation — this is the index contour. Between two adjacent index contours are four intermediate (unlabeled) lines. To find any point's elevation: locate the nearest labeled index contour, count intermediate lines multiplied by the contour interval. NYS Regents Earth Science maps always include index contours and require students to interpolate elevations from them.",
      "domain": "Review",
