      "explanation": "Depression contours are hachured (tick-marked) lines showing a closed area lower than surrounding terrain — a pit, sinkhole, or crater. Hachure marks point toward the lowest point. On NYS Regents maps, elevation inside a depression contour is lower than the labeled value. Sinkholes formed by carbonation of limestone are the classic NYS context for this feature on Regents lab practicals.",
