      "correctText": "stream competence",
      "topic": "Transport and Sorting",
      "explanation": "Stream competence is the maximum particle size a stream can transport at a given velocity; it increases approximately as the square of velocity. The ESRT particle-size graph lets students read the critical velocity needed to move each grain size. Hutton's principle of uniformitarianism means that ancient conglomerates — coarse-grained sedimentary rocks — record high-energy, fast-moving stream environments from the geologic past.",
