      "explanation": "Deposition rate depends on particle size, shape, density, and current velocity. Heavier, rounder, denser particles settle fastest — read from the ESRT settling-velocity graph. Spherical particles sink faster than flat ones of equal mass due to lower drag. Hutton's uniformitarianism predicts identical physics governed ancient deltas, letting geologists interpret shale lamination thickness as a record of seasonal flood pulses.",
