      "topic": "Global Trade",
      "explanation": "A tariff diagram uses a domestic supply-demand framework with a world price line; the tariff raises the domestic price above world price, causing domestic quantity supplied to rise, domestic quantity demanded to fall, and imports to shrink. The diagram shows four effects: consumer loss (reduced consumer surplus), producer gain (increased producer surplus), government revenue (tariff rectangle), and deadweight loss (two triangles representing inefficiency). The U.S. solar panel tariff imposed in 2018 is visible on such a diagram — higher prices reduced installation demand while boosting domestic production.",
