      "topic": "Incentives",
      "explanation": "Property rights are legally enforced claims over the use, income, and transfer of resources or goods; secure property rights are a prerequisite for functioning markets because they create incentives to invest, maintain, and trade assets. Without clear property rights, the tragedy of the commons leads to overuse — shared fishing grounds get depleted because no individual owns them. Intellectual property rights (patents, copyrights) incentivize innovation by allowing inventors to capture returns.",
