      "correctText": "Budget constraint",
      "topic": "Incentives",
      "explanation": "A budget constraint is the set of all combinations of goods a consumer can purchase given their income and the prices of goods; it appears as a straight line on a quantity graph whose slope equals the negative price ratio (−Px/Py). A rise in income shifts the line outward in parallel; a fall in one good's price rotates the line outward along that axis, expanding choice. Understanding budget constraints helps students see why wage increases enable higher saving rates and why inflation erodes purchasing power.",
