      "topic": "Inflation",
      "explanation": "Inflation is a sustained, economy-wide rise in the general price level, eroding purchasing power; measured by the CPI or PCE deflator, the Fed targets 2% annual inflation as consistent with price stability and maximum employment. Demand-pull inflation (excess AD relative to SRAS) and cost-push inflation (SRAS shifts left from supply shocks) have different policy remedies. Unexpected inflation redistributes wealth from creditors to debtors, creating arbitrary economic winners and losers.",
