      "topic": "Inflation",
      "explanation": "An inflationary gap occurs when actual real GDP exceeds potential output — the AD-SRAS equilibrium lies to the right of the LRAS curve — indicating the economy is operating beyond sustainable capacity, driving inflation upward. During 2021-22, pandemic-era fiscal stimulus and pent-up demand created an inflationary gap as spending exceeded supply, driving CPI inflation to 9.1% by June 2022. Contractionary fiscal policy or monetary tightening (rate hikes) shift AD left to close inflationary gaps.",
