      "explanation": "Taxation is the compulsory collection of money by government from households and businesses to fund public expenditures including defense, education, infrastructure, and transfer payments. Tax revenue sources in the U.S. include individual income taxes (~50% of federal revenue), payroll taxes (~36%), corporate taxes, and excise taxes. The design of tax systems involves trade-offs between efficiency (minimizing deadweight loss) and equity (distributing the burden fairly) — a central debate in fiscal policy.",
