      "topic": "Public Goods + Taxes",
      "explanation": "Progressive taxation is a system where average tax rates rise with taxable income — higher earners pay both a larger absolute amount and a larger share of income in taxes. The U.S. federal income tax uses seven brackets (10% to 37% in 2024); the marginal rate applies only to income within each bracket, not all income. Proponents argue it reduces after-tax income inequality; critics argue high marginal rates reduce incentives to work and invest — making the optimal degree of progressivity a central political economy debate.",
