      "correctText": "Diversification",
      "topic": "Risk",
      "explanation": "Diversification is the investment strategy of spreading assets across multiple securities, asset classes, or markets so that poor performance in one investment is offset by others, reducing overall portfolio risk without necessarily reducing expected return. A portfolio holding only one stock experiences its full volatility; adding stocks from different industries and international markets reduces unsystematic (firm-specific) risk. Index funds provide instant diversification across hundreds of companies, which is why financial advisors recommend them for long-term retirement saving.",
