      "correctText": "Scarcity",
      "topic": "Scarcity",
      "explanation": "Scarcity is the foundational economic problem: because resources (land, labor, capital) are finite while human wants are unlimited, every society must make choices about what to produce, how, and for whom. On a PPF, every interior point represents wasted resources while points on the curve represent full use of scarce resources. Scarcity is why prices exist — they ration limited goods among competing buyers.",
