      "correctText": "Scarcity model",
      "topic": "Scarcity",
      "explanation": "The scarcity model formalizes the core economic problem: unlimited human wants facing limited resources forces every society to develop mechanisms for allocation — prices, planning, or custom. It motivates the study of all economic systems, as each is fundamentally a different answer to the allocation question imposed by scarcity. The PPF is the most common graphical representation of the scarcity model, showing the maximum output frontier given fixed resources.",
