      "correctText": "Trade-off",
      "topic": "Scarcity",
      "explanation": "A trade-off is the sacrifice of one option or goal to pursue another whenever resources are scarce and choices must be made; all points on the PPF represent trade-offs between two goods. Every government budget decision involves trade-offs: more spending on defense means less on education or infrastructure, given fixed tax revenue. The opportunity cost is the precise measure of a trade-off's value — the best alternative surrendered.",
