      "correctText": "Specialization",
      "topic": "Scarcity",
      "explanation": "Specialization occurs when individuals, firms, or countries focus production on the good or service at which they have a comparative advantage, boosting total output beyond what general production allows. Adam Smith's pin-factory example showed that dividing labor into specialized tasks multiplied output; today, global supply chains reflect specialization across nations. It enables trade but also creates interdependence and vulnerability to supply disruptions.",
