      "correctText": "Economic systems",
      "topic": "Scarcity",
      "explanation": "Economic systems are the institutional arrangements — rules, ownership structures, and decision-making processes — that societies use to coordinate production, distribution, and consumption under scarcity. The four main types are traditional, command, market, and mixed; most modern economies are mixed, blending private markets with government oversight. China's economy illustrates the spectrum: state-owned enterprises coexist with private firms, mixing command elements with market incentives.",
