      "correctText": "Supply",
      "topic": "Supply",
      "explanation": "Supply is the full schedule of quantities producers are willing and able to offer for sale at each possible price during a given period, shown as an upward-sloping curve because higher prices create stronger profit incentives (law of supply). A price change causes movement along the supply curve; changes in input costs, technology, number of sellers, expectations, or government policy shift the entire curve. Market supply is the horizontal sum of all individual firm supply curves.",
