      "explanation": "A surplus (excess supply) exists when quantity supplied exceeds quantity demanded at the current price, meaning unsold inventory accumulates; rational sellers respond by lowering prices, moving the market back toward equilibrium. On a supply-demand graph, a surplus appears when a horizontal price line sits above equilibrium — the gap between supply and demand curves measures its size. Price floors set above equilibrium (like certain agricultural price supports) create persistent surpluses.",
