      "correctText": "Trade-offs",
      "topic": "Tradeoffs",
      "explanation": "Trade-offs pervade every level of economic decision-making: households trade leisure for income, governments trade defense spending for social programs, and central banks trade lower inflation for higher unemployment (the Phillips Curve short-run trade-off). The PPF makes national trade-offs visible — a point connecting guns and butter shows exactly how much of one must be sacrificed for the other. Recognizing all trade-offs is the first step toward rational, fully-informed decision-making.",
      "domain": "Review",
