      "explanation": "The circular flow model illustrates how households supply factors of production (labor, land, capital) to firms through factor markets and receive income (wages, rent, profit), while firms supply goods and services to households through product markets. Money flows clockwise (households pay firms for goods; firms pay households for resources); real resources flow counterclockwise. Adding government and foreign sectors creates a four-sector model that tracks injections (G, X, I) and leakages (T, M, S).",
