      "explanation": "An incentive is any factor — a price signal, tax, subsidy, fine, or reward — that raises or lowers the cost or benefit of a particular behavior, thereby influencing rational decision-making. Higher prices incentivize producers to supply more and consumers to buy less (movement along the supply and demand curves). Poorly designed incentives cause unintended consequences: a tax on medical devices once reduced domestic production while imports rose.",
