      "topic": "Unemployment",
      "explanation": "Transfer payments are government payments to individuals — Social Security, Medicare, Medicaid, unemployment insurance, SNAP, TANF — that redistribute income without requiring a current productive contribution; they are the largest component of federal spending (about 60% of the budget). Transfer payments function as automatic stabilizers: unemployment insurance and SNAP automatically expand in recessions, sustaining consumer spending. Transfer payments are excluded from GDP calculations because they do not represent current production.",
