      "correctText": "Stagflation",
      "topic": "Unemployment",
      "explanation": "Stagflation is the rare and painful combination of high inflation and high unemployment (economic stagnation) that defies the traditional short-run Phillips Curve trade-off; it typically results from a severe negative supply shock shifting SRAS left. The 1970s U.S. stagflation — driven by OPEC oil embargoes — saw unemployment and inflation both above 10% simultaneously, creating an Okun's Misery Index peak. Policy responses face a dilemma: fighting inflation tightens policy and worsens unemployment, while stimulus worsens inflation.",
      "domain": "Review",
      "gradeBand": "Multi",
      "subjectArea": "Review",
