      "correctText": "Full-employment output",
      "topic": "Unemployment",
      "explanation": "Full-employment output (potential GDP) is the real GDP the economy produces when unemployment equals the natural rate (~4%) — resources are fully but not excessively employed; it is represented by the LRAS curve. When actual GDP exceeds potential (inflationary gap), wages rise, SRAS shifts left, and the economy self-corrects. The Congressional Budget Office (CBO) estimates U.S. potential GDP annually — the gap between actual and potential GDP guides fiscal stimulus or restraint decisions.",
      "domain": "Review",
      "gradeBand": "Multi",
