      "explanation": "Public debt is the cumulative sum of all past federal budget deficits minus surpluses — the total amount the federal government owes to domestic and foreign creditors (primarily in Treasury bonds). U.S. federal debt exceeded $34 trillion in 2024, representing over 120% of GDP — a level that raises concerns about long-run debt-service costs crowding out other spending. Distinguishing gross debt from debt held by the public (excluding intragovernmental holdings) is important for accurate analysis.",
