      "correctText": "Claim of policy",
      "topic": "Argument Structure",
      "explanation": "A claim of policy advocates a specific action ('Schools should adopt later start times'). Policy claims build on fact claims (problem exists) and value claims (problem is bad) to recommend action. RI.9-10.8 covers argument. Regents Part 3 source-based argument essays often pose policy questions. AP Lang argument essays frequently require policy positions. The structure problem-cause-solution organizes most policy arguments. Strong policy claims address feasibility, not just desirability.",
