      "explanation": "Bias is a source's unstated preference, shaped by funding, political affiliation, or personal investment. A tobacco-industry-funded smoking study has structural bias. RI.9-10.6 covers point of view; RI.9-10.8 evaluates argument. Regents Part 3 source-based argument essays sometimes pair biased and neutral sources. AP Lang argument and synthesis essays reward bias-aware source handling. Bias detection requires examining: who funded this, who published it, what perspective is missing?",
