      "explanation": "Classical argument structure (from Aristotle and Cicero) has five parts: introduction (exordium), narration of facts (narratio), confirmation of claim (confirmatio), refutation of opposition (refutatio), conclusion (peroratio). W.9-10.1 covers argumentative writing. AP Lang argument essays accept classical structure; rhetorical analysis essays often analyze it in source speeches. Regents Part 3 source-based argument essays implicitly use this structure. Mastery of classical structure unlocks both analysis and writing.",
