      "correctText": "Hyperbole",
      "topic": "Figurative Language",
      "explanation": "Hyperbole is intentional exaggeration for emphasis or effect. Stanley's 'I am the king around here!' (Streetcar, scene 8) declares dominance through hyperbole. Williams uses hyperbole for Stanley's territorial assertion and Blanche's romantic delusions ('I want magic!'). RL.9-10.4 covers figurative language. Regents Part 2 multiple-choice tests hyperbole recognition. AP Lit and AP Lang demand analysis of how exaggeration serves character or argument. Distinct from litotes (understatement) and metaphor (substitution).",
