      "explanation": "Litotes (LIE-toh-teez) understates by negating the opposite: 'not bad' for 'good,' 'no small problem' for 'a big problem.' L.9-10.5a covers figurative language. MLK's 'I am not unmindful that some of you have come here out of great trials and tribulations' uses litotes. Regents Part 2 multiple-choice rarely tests litotes; AP Lang rhetorical analysis essays prize identification. Anglo-Saxon literature (Beowulf) heavily uses litotes.",
