      "explanation": "In medias res (Latin: 'in the middle of things') begins narrative in mid-action, then fills in background. The Iliad opens with Achilles's anger already raging. W.9-10.3a requires engaging openings. Regents Part 4 text-analysis response and AP Lang argument writing reward strong openings. The technique creates immediate stakes and pulls readers in. Modern fiction uses it heavily (Beloved opens 'with mid-action and traumatic memory').",
