      "correctText": "Sentence variety",
      "topic": "Narrative Structure",
      "explanation": "Sentence variety (syntactic diversity) mixes sentence lengths and structures: short punchy sentences for emphasis, longer flowing sentences for development, fragments for impact. Monotonous syntax bores readers. W.9-10.5 covers revision; W.9-10.4 covers style. Regents Part 4 text-analysis writing rewards varied syntax. AP Lang and AP Lit narrative writing and analysis prize syntactic range as sophistication.",
