      "correctText": "Volta",
      "topic": "Sonnet Form",
      "explanation": "The volta (Italian for 'turn') marks the shift in argument, emotion, or perspective in a sonnet. In Petrarchan sonnets, the volta typically sits between octave and sestet (line 9). In Shakespearean sonnets, the volta can appear at line 9 or shift to the closing couplet (line 13). RL.9-10.5 covers form-meaning relationships. AP Lit demands precise volta identification and analysis. Regents Part 2 may test volta recognition. The volta is the sonnet's structural hinge.",
