      "explanation": "Peer-reviewed scholarly sources have undergone expert evaluation before publication, providing authority that blog posts lack. RI.9-10.8 evaluates source authority. W.9-10.8 covers gathering credible sources. Regents Part 3 source-based argument essays sometimes mix scholarly and popular sources for student evaluation. AP Lang's synthesis essay (formerly part of the exam) explicitly required source-type evaluation. Not all peer review is equal: predatory journals exist. Scholarly authority is a starting point, not absolute.",
