      "topic": "Source Credibility",
      "explanation": "Unverifiable evidence (vague attribution to 'studies' or 'experts' without naming them) prevents fact-checking. 'Studies show' is a red flag in argument analysis. RI.9-10.8 requires evaluating evidence. Regents Part 3 source-based argument essays may include sources guilty of this weakness. AP Lang rhetorical analysis trains students to flag unverifiable evidence as a rhetorical move. Strong writing names sources specifically; weak writing hides behind anonymous authority.",
