      "topic": "Speech Analysis",
      "explanation": "Epistrophe (Greek: 'turning back') repeats words at the end of successive clauses. Lincoln's Gettysburg Address 'government of the people, by the people, for the people' uses repetition of 'the people.' RI.9-10.6 covers rhetoric. Regents Part 3 source-based argument essays and AP Lang rhetorical analysis essays demand precise device-naming. Combined anaphora and epistrophe is symploke ('When there is need of silence, you speak, and when there is need of speech, you remain silent').",
