      "correctText": "Exigence",
      "topic": "Speech Analysis",
      "explanation": "Exigence (Lloyd Bitzer's term) is the urgent issue or event that calls forth rhetoric. Antony's exigence: Caesar's body lies before a crowd, the conspirators speak first, Rome's future is in the balance. RI.9-10.6 covers context. Regents Part 3 source-based argument essays implicitly require exigence awareness. AP Lang rhetorical analysis essays explicitly score exigence identification as part of rhetorical situation analysis. Exigence shapes purpose and constraints.",
