      "correctText": "Situation",
      "topic": "Speech Analysis",
      "explanation": "The rhetorical situation (Lloyd Bitzer, 1968) includes exigence (urgent issue), audience (those who can act), and constraints (factors limiting what can be said). Antony's funeral oration occurs in a specific situation (Caesar dead, mob present, conspirators armed) shaping what he can say. RI.9-10.6 covers context-driven rhetoric. Regents Part 3 source-based argument essays implicitly require situational awareness. AP Lang rhetorical analysis demands explicit situational analysis.",
