      "explanation": "Periodic (hypotactic) style uses long, subordinated sentences with delayed main clauses, building momentum to a final point. Henry James, Faulkner, and Toni Morrison write in periodic styles. Contrast with paratactic (short, coordinate) style. W.9-10.4 covers style; W.9-10.5 covers revision. Regents Part 4 text-analysis writing benefits from syntactic analysis. AP Lang rhetorical analysis essays reward syntactic precision.",
