      "explanation": "Diction is word choice. Three levels: formal (academic), informal (conversational), colloquial (dialect, slang). Style-conscious writers vary diction strategically. W.9-10.5 covers revision for style; W.9-10.3d requires precise words. RL.9-10.4 covers how word choice shapes meaning. Regents Part 4 text-analysis writing and AP Lang rhetorical analysis essays both heavily score diction awareness.",
