      "topic": "Texts and Authors",
      "explanation": "Shakespeare's Julius Caesar (1599) dramatizes the conspiracy of Brutus and Cassius, the assassination of Caesar, and the civil war that follows. RL.9-10.2 covers theme; RL.9-10.5 covers structure. Antony's funeral oration in 3.2 is canonical rhetoric. Common Core lists Shakespeare among the foundational texts for Grades 9-10. Regents Part 3 source-based argument essays on conspiracy, rhetoric, and power use this play. AP Lit treats it as a teaching text for tragedy.",
