      "correctText": "Authenticity in a fake adult world",
      "topic": "Theme Statements",
      "explanation": "Salinger uses Holden's repeated 'phony' (45+ instances) to develop the theme that adult society demands a kind of fakeness Holden cannot accept. The catcher fantasy (catching children before they fall off the cliff into adulthood) crystallizes the theme. RL.9-10.2 covers theme. Regents Part 3 source-based arguments on adolescent identity use Catcher. AP Lit prizes precise diction-theme analysis. The novel was the most-banned book in 1973-78.",
