      "correctText": "Civilization is a thin veneer",
      "topic": "Theme Statements",
      "explanation": "Golding's Lord of the Flies traces how British schoolboys, removed from adult oversight, descend through stages: rules to face paint to hunting frenzy to Piggy's murder. The theme argues civilization is precariously held. RL.9-10.2 covers theme development. The novel's epigraph (Coral Island, R.M. Ballantyne) sets up Golding's deliberate inversion of Victorian optimism. Regents Part 3 source-based arguments on human nature use LOTF. AP Lit treats it as canonical.",
