      "explanation": "A symbol is a concrete thing that represents an abstract idea. Golding makes the Lord of the Flies (Beelzebub, fly-king, Hebrew for Satan) the pig's head on a stake that 'speaks' to Simon. The symbol externalizes evil as internal to humans. RL.9-10.4 covers symbol. Regents Part 3 source-based arguments on human nature use LOTF. AP Lit demands precise symbol analysis: not just what X means, but how X's transformation across the text develops theme. Common Core lists symbol analysis as central.",
