      "explanation": "Wiesel's Night (1958) traces Eliezer's transformation from devout student to numb survivor: 'Never shall I forget that smoke. Never shall I forget the little faces of the children whose bodies I saw transformed into smoke under a silent sky.' The 'where is God now' moment at the hanging marks his crisis. RI.9-10.6 covers memoir; RL.9-10.2 covers theme. Regents Part 3 source-based arguments on the Holocaust and witness use this text.",
