      "prompt": "Swift's 'A Modest Proposal' to eat Irish babies demonstrates this tone of biting irony.",
      "choices": [
        "Elegiac",
        "Sardonic",
        "Satirical",
        "Exigence"
      ],
      "correctText": "Satirical",
      "topic": "Tone Vocabulary",
      "explanation": "Satirical tone uses irony, exaggeration, and ridicule to expose folly or vice. Swift's 'A Modest Proposal' (1729) deadpan-suggests selling Irish babies for food to wealthy English. Orwell's Animal Farm employs satirical tone in its omniscient narration. RI.9-10.4 covers tone. Regents Part 3 source-based argument essays often include satirical passages. AP Lang rhetorical analysis essays require satire identification and analysis of its rhetorical purpose (often exposing power).",
