      "explanation": "The rhetorical triangle (Aristotle) connects writer/speaker (ethos), audience (pathos), and subject (logos). RI.11-12.6 covers point of view and rhetoric. AP Lang's rhetorical analysis essay is built on this framework. Regents Part 3 source-based argument essays implicitly require triangle awareness. Mapping the triangle answers who is speaking, to whom, about what.",
