      "correctText": "Anaphora",
      "topic": "Argument and Rhetoric",
      "explanation": "Anaphora repeats a word or phrase at the start of successive clauses. King's eight 'I have a dream' repetitions; Lincoln's 'we cannot dedicate...' RI.11-12.6 covers rhetoric. Regents Part 3 source-based argument essays explicitly reward anaphora identification. AP Lang rhetorical analysis essays demand precise device-naming. Distinguish anaphora from epistrophe (ending repetition).",
