      "correctText": "Counterclaim",
      "topic": "Argument and Rhetoric",
      "explanation": "A counterclaim is the opposing position a writer addresses. W.11-12.1b requires developing 'claims and counterclaims fairly and thoroughly.' The Grade 11 'thoroughly' is stricter than 9-10. Regents Part 3 source-based argument essays evaluate counterclaim acknowledgment. AP Lang argument essays heavily reward genuine counterclaim engagement.",
