      "correctText": "Gettysburg Address",
      "topic": "Argument Structure",
      "explanation": "Lincoln's Gettysburg Address (November 19, 1863) is approximately 272 words delivered at the dedication of the Soldiers' National Cemetery. Its concision is itself rhetorical. RI.11-12.9 requires analysis of foundational U.S. documents 'for their themes, purposes, and rhetorical features.' Common Core lists the Gettysburg Address for Grades 11-12. Regents Part 3 source-based argument essays on memory, sacrifice, or democracy use this text. AP Lang treats it as canonical.",
      "domain": "Review",
