      "explanation": "Fitzgerald threads color through Gatsby: Gatsby's hope (green), the wealth and corruption (yellow/gold), Daisy and Jordan's affected innocence (white), the Valley of Ashes (gray), Gatsby's love (red). The color system encodes moral judgments. RL.11-12.4 covers figurative meaning. AP Lit treats Gatsby's color motifs as canonical close-reading material. Regents Part 3 source-based arguments on Gatsby's craft use color symbolism. Fitzgerald's deliberate color planning is documented in his manuscripts.",
