      "correctText": "Inform",
      "topic": "Author's Purpose",
      "explanation": "Informational/expository purpose is to explain or convey knowledge clearly without arguing a position. Science writing, encyclopedia entries, technical manuals, civics explainers, and most news reporting are primarily informational. RI.11-12.6 covers purpose. Regents Part 2 multiple-choice routinely tests purpose categorization. AP Lang requires distinguishing informational from argumentative (taking a position) and from expressive (writer's emotions or experience).",
