      "correctText": "Persuade",
      "topic": "Author's Purpose",
      "explanation": "Author's purpose can be to inform, persuade, entertain, or express. Frederick Douglass's Narrative (1845) is autobiographical and informative, but its primary purpose is persuasive: to abolish slavery by making readers see its evils through Douglass's experience. RI.11-12.6 explicitly examines purpose. Regents Part 2 multiple-choice tests purpose identification. AP Lang rhetorical analysis essays must explain how the writer's choices advance the specific purpose. Common Core lists Douglass for Grades 11-12 informational study.",
