      "correctText": "Cultivate transformation",
      "topic": "Author's Purpose",
      "explanation": "Transcendentalist writers (Emerson, Thoreau, Margaret Fuller) aimed less at persuasion to specific action than at transforming readers' consciousness. Emerson's 'Self-Reliance' demands a different self, not just a different policy. Thoreau's Walden demands different daily life. RI.11-12.6 covers purpose. Regents Part 3 source-based argument essays may pair Transcendentalist texts with policy texts. AP Lang treats Transcendentalists as canonical American rhetoric. Their purpose blends expressive and persuasive: transform yourself.",
