      "correctText": "Express personal experience",
      "topic": "Author's Purpose",
      "explanation": "Expressive purpose centers the writer's personal perspective, feelings, or experience. Thoreau's Walden (1854) and 'Civil Disobedience' blend personal reflection with broader argument. Personal essays by Joan Didion, James Baldwin, and Douglass all combine purposes. RI.11-12.6 covers purpose. Regents Part 3 source-based argument prompts occasionally include literary nonfiction. AP Lang argument and synthesis essays draw on expressive writing as evidence. Expressive writing often combines purposes: expressing experience to inform or persuade.",
