      "prompt": "A writer treating both sides fairly without clear position has this stance.",
      "choices": [
        "Climax",
        "Objective",
        "Critical",
        "Subjective"
      ],
      "correctText": "Objective",
      "topic": "Author's Stance",
      "explanation": "Objective stance presents information without favoring a side. Encyclopedic and most news writing aim for objectivity. RI.11-12.6 covers stance. Regents Part 2 multiple-choice tests stance categorization. AP Lang requires distinguishing objective (neutral) from subjective (personal-view-laden) writing. True objectivity is contested; writers' choices about what to include shape stance even without explicit position. The distinction is foundational for source evaluation.",
