      "prompt": "The triangular relationship of writer, audience, and subject is called the rhetorical this.",
      "choices": [
        "Civil Disobedience",
        "Critical",
        "Triangle",
        "Subjective"
      ],
      "correctText": "Triangle",
      "topic": "Author's Stance",
      "explanation": "The rhetorical triangle (Aristotle) connects writer/speaker (ethos), audience (pathos), and subject (logos). Effective rhetoric balances all three angles. RI.11-12.6 covers point of view and rhetoric. Regents Part 3 source-based argument essays often pose questions about audience or speaker stance. AP Lang's rhetorical analysis essay requires mapping the triangle: who is speaking, to whom, about what, and how the choices serve all three points.",
