      "correctText": "Introductory adverbial phrase",
      "topic": "Comma Rules",
      "explanation": "Introductory adverbial phrases (prepositional, participial, infinitive) preceding the main clause take a comma. 'After the war ended, soldiers returned home.' 'Running through the woods, Rainsford spotted Zaroff.' L.11-12.2 explicitly covers punctuation conventions. Regents Part 4 text-analysis writing and AP Lang rhetorical analysis essays both reward correct introductory comma usage. Failure signals basic error.",
