      "explanation": "Latin root 'spec/spect' (look, see) generates 'inspect' (look into), 'spectator' (one who looks), 'spectacular' (worth looking at), 'speculate' (theorize), 'perspective' (look through), 'suspect' (doubt). L.11-12.4b requires roots and affixes. Regents Part 2 vocabulary tests root recognition. AP Lang and AP Lit assume root literacy. Family also includes 'specimen,' 'specter,' 'aspect.'.",
