      "choices": [
        "Foil",
        "Letter from Birmingham Jail",
        "The Great Gatsby",
        "Parallel structure"
      ],
      "correctText": "The Great Gatsby",
      "topic": "Literary Devices",
      "explanation": "Fitzgerald's The Great Gatsby (1925) is narrated by Nick Carraway and follows Jay Gatsby's pursuit of Daisy Buchanan in Long Island's Jazz Age. Common Core lists Gatsby for Grades 11-12. RL.11-12.2 covers theme; RL.11-12.5 covers structure. Regents Part 3 source-based argument essays on the American Dream use this novel as a centerpiece. AP Lit treats it as canonical for character, theme, and symbol analysis.",
