      "prompt": "Read this passage:\n\n'The hallway was narrow and the bulbs hummed like trapped wasps. Paint peeled in soft strips. Every door was numbered, and every number was wrong: 13B, 13B, 13B, as if the building itself could not remember how to count.'\n\nHow does the setting most directly contribute to the passage?",
