      "id": "ela-11-pe-012",
      "prompt": "Consider this line from Robert Frost's 'Stopping by Woods on a Snowy Evening' (1923, public domain):\n\n'The woods are lovely, dark, and deep, / But I have promises to keep.'\n\nWhich form of irony is most relevant if a fire chief, sprinting late to a five-alarm fire, mutters this line to himself?",
