      "prompt": "Read this passage:\n\n'Of course Mr. Hollings was thrilled to spend another Saturday cleaning the gutters. He whistled a cheerful tune as cold rainwater ran down his sleeves and a squirrel, watching from the maple, judged him silently.'\n\nWhich word best describes the author's tone?",
