      "correctText": "Show don't tell",
      "topic": "Sensory Detail",
      "explanation": "'Show, don't tell' demands writers demonstrate emotion, character, and meaning through action, dialogue, and sensory detail rather than stating directly. W.11-12.3d explicitly requires sensory language. Regents Part 4 text-analysis writing rewards showing. AP Lit narrative scenes reward showing as a sophistication marker. Foundational rule of fiction craft, attributed variously to Henry James and Anton Chekhov.",
