      "topic": "Thesis Construction",
      "explanation": "Arguability distinguishes a thesis from a topic statement. W.11-12.1a requires writers to introduce 'precise, knowledgeable claim(s).' Regents Part 3 source-based argument essays explicitly reward arguable theses. AP Lang's argument essay rubric distinguishes defensible thesis (1 pt) from no thesis (0 pts). Strong theses pass the 'who would disagree?' test. If no reasonable person would disagree, it's not a thesis but a fact or a topic statement.",
