      "prompt": "A weak thesis that just restates the prompt or asserts an obvious fact has this flaw.",
      "choices": [
        "Civil Disobedience",
        "Arguable",
        "Lack of specificity",
        "Knowledgeable"
      ],
      "correctText": "Lack of specificity",
      "topic": "Thesis Construction",
      "explanation": "Vague theses fail because they neither argue nor specify. Strong theses name the text, the specific claim, and often the mechanism. W.11-12.1a explicitly requires 'precise, knowledgeable claim(s).' Regents Part 3 source-based argument essays penalize thesis vagueness. AP Lang's argument essay rubric awards thesis points only for defensible, specific claims. Students should ask: would anyone disagree with my thesis? If not, it's not a thesis. Would my thesis apply to any text in the genre? If yes, it's too general.",
