      "explanation": "Signal phrases introduce quotations with context: 'As Douglass argues...' 'According to Source 2...' 'Emerson, writing in 1841, observes...' W.11-12.1c covers cohesion. Regents Part 3 source-based argument essays explicitly require source attribution; failure drops a score band. AP Lang argument essays favor varied signal phrases. Effective signal phrases include the writer's authority or perspective. Avoid repetitive 'X says' constructions.",
