      "correctText": "Sardonic",
      "topic": "Tone Vocabulary",
      "explanation": "Sardonic tone combines scorn with bitter humor; it mocks while smiling. Twain's later writing, Fitzgerald's narrator at his most cutting, and Vonnegut's prose all use sardonic tone. RI.11-12.4 covers tone. Regents Part 2 multiple-choice tests advanced tone vocabulary. AP Lit and AP Lang demand precise tone names: sardonic, wry, acerbic, jocular. Avoid 'serious' or 'funny' generically. Sardonic is more cynical than satirical, more bitter than wry.",
