      "prompt": "Emerson's confident pronouncements like 'Trust thyself' describe this tone.",
      "choices": [
        "Straw man",
        "Sardonic",
        "Resolute",
        "Assertive"
      ],
      "correctText": "Assertive",
      "topic": "Tone Vocabulary",
      "explanation": "Assertive tone confidently declares positions. Emerson's 'Self-Reliance' (1841) opens with epigrammatic assertions: 'Trust thyself: every heart vibrates to that iron string.' 'A foolish consistency is the hobgoblin of little minds.' The tone embodies the essay's argument: declarative selfhood. RI.11-12.4 covers tone. Regents Part 2 multiple-choice tests advanced tone vocabulary. AP Lang and AP Lit demand precise tone naming. Distinct from defensive, hesitant, or measured tones.",
