      "correctText": "Resolute",
      "topic": "Tone Vocabulary",
      "explanation": "Resolute tone shows firm, unwavering commitment without anger or hesitation. Thoreau's 'Civil Disobedience' (1849) recounts his refusal to pay the poll tax in support of slavery and the Mexican-American War, narrated with calm principle rather than fury. RI.11-12.4 covers tone. Regents Part 2 multiple-choice tests precise tone vocabulary. AP Lang demands students name tone with specificity, not just 'serious' or 'principled.' Distinct from defiant (which is confrontational) and committed (which is more general).",
