      "correctText": "Satirical",
      "topic": "Tone Vocabulary",
      "explanation": "Satirical tone uses irony, exaggeration, and ridicule to expose folly. Mark Twain's Huckleberry Finn satirizes antebellum Southern hypocrisy through Huck's naive narration of brutal events. RI.11-12.4 covers tone; RL.11-12.4 covers literary tone. Regents Part 3 source-based argument essays often include satirical passages. AP Lang rhetorical analysis essays require satire identification and analysis of its purpose (often exposing power). Distinct from sarcastic (more personal, narrower) and ironic (broader category).",
      "domain": "Review",
      "gradeBand": "Multi",
      "subjectArea": "Review",
      "standardRefs": [],
