      "correctText": "Denotation",
      "topic": "Vocabulary in Context",
      "explanation": "Denotation is a word's literal, dictionary definition. Contrasts with connotation (associations). 'House' and 'home' have similar denotations but different connotations. L.11-12.4 covers vocabulary; L.11-12.5b explicitly covers 'denotations.' Regents Part 2 multiple-choice often tests denotation/connotation distinction. AP Lang rhetorical analysis essays must distinguish these for precise word-choice analysis. Foundational vocabulary distinction.",
