      "explanation": "'Show, don't tell' demands writers demonstrate emotion through action, dialogue, and sensory detail rather than stating it directly. W.11-12.3d requires sensory language. Regents Part 4 text-analysis writing rewards showing. AP Lit narrative writing scores showing heavily. Foundational rule of fiction craft attributed variously to Henry James and Anton Chekhov.",
