      "explanation": "Personal essays by Joan Didion (Slouching Towards Bethlehem 1968, The White Album 1979), James Baldwin (Notes of a Native Son 1955), Annie Dillard (Pilgrim at Tinker Creek 1974), and George Orwell ('Shooting an Elephant' 1936) have primarily the purpose to express personal experience and render it meaningful to readers. Distinct from inform (factual conveyance), persuade (changing belief), and entertain (amusement). NYS W.11-12.3 covers narrative writing including personal narrative. AP English Lang FRQ Question 2 (rhetorical analysis) sometimes presents personal essays - rubric rewards students who recognize expressive purpose AND analyze how rhetorical choices (voice, anecdote, reflective commentary) serve it.",
