      "correctText": "Tone",
      "topic": "Author's Purpose",
      "explanation": "SOAPSTone is the standard rhetorical-analysis acronym: Speaker, Occasion, Audience, Purpose, Subject, Tone. Tone completes the heuristic - the speaker's attitude toward the subject and audience, conveyed through diction, syntax, imagery, and figurative choice. SOAPSTone surfaces all six rhetorical situation components for analysis. NYS RI.11-12.6 covers rhetorical analysis. AP English Language and Composition uses SOAPSTone in the curriculum framework; FRQ Question 2 (rhetorical analysis, 6 points) implicitly tests all six elements - rubric rewards essays that analyze multiple SOAPSTone elements in relation to one another, not just identify them serially. Tone is the synthesizing element that integrates the others.",
