      "prompt": "A writer's openly stated position is called this kind of stance.",
      "choices": [
        "Explicit",
        "Elegiac",
        "Subjective",
        "Objective"
      ],
      "correctText": "Explicit",
      "topic": "Author's Stance",
      "explanation": "An explicit stance is the writer's openly stated position - declared in the thesis or in clear topic sentences, with no rhetorical concealment. Distinct from implicit stance (position discernible only through tone, diction, and structural emphasis without direct statement). Explicit stance is the convention for academic argumentative essays and for AP English Lang FRQ Question 3 (argument, 6 points), which rewards essays whose claim is plainly stated. Implicit stance is more common in literary fiction, irony, and satire. NYS W.11-12.1 covers argument writing with explicit claims; RI.11-12.6 covers analyzing author's point of view. AP English Lang FRQ Question 2 (rhetorical analysis, 6 points) rewards students who distinguish explicit from implicit stance and analyze the rhetorical effect of the choice.",
