      "explanation": "FANBOYS is the standard mnemonic for the seven coordinating conjunctions that can join two independent clauses with a comma: For, And, Nor, But, Or, Yet, So. Example: 'It was raining, so we went home.' Distinct from subordinating conjunctions (because, although, while, when, if, since) which create dependent clauses requiring different punctuation. NYS L.11-12.1 covers grammar conventions; L.11-12.2 covers punctuation conventions. AP English Lang FRQ Question 2 (rhetorical analysis, 6 points) rewards syntactic-variety analysis including coordination versus subordination - upper-range essays integrate syntactic-choice analysis into rhetorical reading rather than merely identifying conjunctions.",
