      "correctText": "Paraphrase",
      "topic": "Evidence Integration",
      "explanation": "Paraphrase restates an author's idea in your own words while preserving meaning, length, and source attribution. Distinct from summary (which compresses) and direct quotation (which preserves exact words). Effective paraphrase demonstrates the writer's comprehension while integrating ideas smoothly into the writer's argument. Always cite paraphrase - unattributed paraphrase is plagiarism even when wording differs from source. NYS W.11-12.8 covers gathering relevant information from multiple sources, assessing usefulness, and integrating into the text while avoiding plagiarism. AP English Lang FRQ Question 1 (synthesis, 6 points) and the AP rubric for source use both reward paraphrase that demonstrates comprehension and integrates with attribution.",
