      "correctText": "Classification definition",
      "topic": "Explanatory Style",
      "explanation": "Classification definition is the expository move of defining a term by placing it within a broader category and then specifying the distinguishing features that separate it from other members of that category. Example: 'A sonnet (genus: lyric poem) is a fourteen-line iambic-pentameter poem with a specific rhyme scheme (differentia).' The technique goes back to Aristotle's Categories and Posterior Analytics (c. 4th c. BCE). NYS W.11-12.2 covers explanatory writing including precise definition. AP English Lang FRQ Question 1 (synthesis, 6 points) and Question 3 (argument) reward writers who define key terms clearly when those terms are contested - rubric awards essays that establish definitional criteria before applying them.",
