      "topic": "Explanatory Style",
      "explanation": "Expository writing explains a process, defines a concept, analyzes a phenomenon, or provides information without arguing a contestable position - the prose mode of textbooks, scientific articles, instruction manuals, encyclopedia entries, and informational journalism. Distinct from argumentative (advances arguable claim), narrative (tells story), and descriptive (renders scene). NYS W.11-12.2 explicitly covers writing 'informative/explanatory texts to examine and convey complex ideas, concepts, and information clearly and accurately through the effective selection, organization, and analysis of content.' AP English Lang FRQ Question 1 (synthesis, 6 points) requires explanatory synthesis of sources - rubric upper-range integrates explanation with argument.",
