      "correctText": "Cause and effect",
      "topic": "Explanatory Style",
      "explanation": "Cause-and-effect organization presents events or phenomena in terms of how causes produce effects - explaining the mechanisms by which one thing produces another. Distinct from chronological (events in time order without causal claim), comparison/contrast (similarities and differences), and problem/solution. NYS W.11-12.2 covers explanatory organizational patterns; RI.11-12.5 covers analyzing structural features of informational text. AP English Lang FRQ Question 1 (synthesis, 6 points) and Question 2 (rhetorical analysis, 6 points) reward cause-effect organization when content warrants - but rubric distinguishes genuine causal analysis from post hoc reasoning (assuming temporal sequence proves causation). Causal claims require supporting evidence beyond sequence.",
