      "correctText": "Anecdote",
      "topic": "Hook Strategies",
      "explanation": "An anecdote hook opens with a brief, vivid story to illustrate a larger point - a single concrete instance that personalizes abstract argument. Example: 'When fourteen-year-old Malala Yousafzai boarded her school bus in Pakistan on Oct 9 2012, she was preparing for an exam; what happened instead would galvanize a global movement for girls' education.' Effective anecdote hooks connect the specific story to the essay's larger claim within the opening paragraph. NYS W.11-12.3 covers narrative writing and engaging openings; W.11-12.2 covers explanatory introductions. AP English Lang FRQ Question 3 (argument, 6 points) and AP Lit FRQ Question 3 (open, 8 points) reward effective hooks - anecdote is a standard upper-range opening strategy.",
