      "correctText": "Rhetorical question",
      "topic": "Hook Strategies",
      "explanation": "A rhetorical question hook opens an essay or speech with a provocative question intended to engage the audience's curiosity rather than to elicit answer - the audience must hold the question while the writer develops the response across the essay. Example: 'What does it cost to be free?' Effective rhetorical questions establish the essay's central tension. Distinct from genuine question (which expects answer) and from rhetorical question used merely for emphasis (which doesn't require sustained engagement). NYS W.11-12.3 covers narrative writing and engaging openings; W.11-12.2 covers explanatory introductions. AP English Lang FRQ Question 3 (argument, 6 points) rewards effective hooks - rhetorical question is one upper-range option.",
