      "correctText": "Statistic hook",
      "topic": "Hook Strategies",
      "explanation": "A statistic hook opens an essay or speech with a startling fact or numerical claim to seize attention. Example: 'Every twenty seconds, a child somewhere dies from a preventable disease.' The hook works by exploiting the audience's surprise response and establishing immediate stakes. Effective statistic hooks pair the number with source attribution and contextual interpretation, lest readers dismiss the figure as unverified. NYS W.11-12.3 covers narrative writing including hooks; W.11-12.2 covers explanatory writing introductions. AP English Lang FRQ Question 3 (argument, 6 points) and Question 2 (rhetorical analysis, 6 points) both reward effective introductions - hook strategy is one component of the upper-range descriptor 'effectively engages the audience.'",
