      "correctText": "Strong verb choice",
      "topic": "Hook Strategies",
      "explanation": "Strong verb choice demonstrates the writing craft of preferring vivid, specific verbs over weak verb-plus-adverb constructions. 'She stormed into the room' replaces 'she walked angrily into the room'; 'He whispered' replaces 'he said quietly'; 'The crowd surged forward' replaces 'the crowd moved forward quickly.' Strong verbs compress sensory and emotional information into the verb itself, eliminating modifier scaffolding. NYS L.11-12.3 covers using knowledge of language to make effective choices; W.11-12.3 covers narrative techniques including vivid words and phrases. AP English Lit FRQ Question 1 (poetry, 6 points) and Question 2 (prose passage, 6 points) reward analysis of authors' verb choices - rubric upper-range explores diction.",
