      "topic": "Latin and Greek Roots",
      "explanation": "The Greek root 'graph' meaning 'write' or 'record' generates an extensive English vocabulary: autograph (self-written signature), biography (life-writing), photograph (light-writing), geography (earth-writing/describing), telegraph (distance-writing), bibliography (book-writing/listing), calligraphy (beautiful-writing), seismograph (earthquake-recording). NYS L.11-12.4 covers using Greek/Latin roots as clues to meaning. AP English Lang and Lit vocabulary, SAT Reading section, and Regents ELA passages all reward Greek-root knowledge. Note related '-graphy' (the field, as in 'photography') versus '-graph' (the instrument or the product, as in 'photograph'). Students with strong root knowledge decode unfamiliar Greek-derived vocabulary on the fly.",
