      "explanation": "Imagery is description using unexpected comparison - figurative language (metaphor, simile, personification) that produces vivid mental pictures by linking concrete imagery to abstract concept or experience. Distinct from sensory detail (which describes directly) and from symbol (which carries thematic weight beyond image). T.S. Eliot's 'evening is spread out against the sky / Like a patient etherized upon a table' (The Love Song of J. Alfred Prufrock 1915) compresses urban evening into a surgical image. NYS RL.11-12.4 covers figurative meaning and word choice. AP English Lit FRQ Question 1 (poetry, 6 points) and Question 2 (prose passage, 6 points) reward imagery analysis - rubric upper-range integrates imagery with tonal and thematic argument.",
