      "correctText": "Accuracy",
      "topic": "Source Credibility",
      "explanation": "The CRAAP test (Currency, Relevance, Authority, Accuracy, Purpose) is the standard university-library source-evaluation framework developed at California State University Chico c. 2004. After Currency (is the source recent enough?), Relevance (does it address my specific question?), Authority (who is the author? credentials? institution?), and Purpose (why was it produced?), the fourth criterion is Accuracy - is the information verifiable in other reliable sources? Are claims documented with citations? NYS RI.11-12.7 requires evaluating source credibility. AP Lang FRQ Question 1 (synthesis) rewards essays that question source reliability rather than treating each given source as equally authoritative.",
