      "correctText": "Periodic style",
      "topic": "Style and Voice",
      "explanation": "Periodic style features long, complex sentences with multiple subordinate clauses that build toward main meaning at sentence-end, creating suspension and grammatical climax. Henry James, Jane Austen, and Cicero are masters of periodic style. Example: 'Although the storm had been forecast for days, although the warnings had been broadcast through every channel, and although prudent families had begun their preparations weeks earlier, still many residents found themselves unprepared.' Distinct from loose style (main meaning early, modifiers added). NYS L.11-12.3 covers using knowledge of language for stylistic effect. AP English Lang FRQ Question 2 (rhetorical analysis, 6 points) rewards periodic-style identification and effect-analysis.",
