      "topic": "Style and Voice",
      "explanation": "Diction is word choice - the deliberate selection of individual words for connotation, register, sound, and precise denotation. Replacing 'said' with 'whispered,' 'shouted,' 'mumbled,' or 'declared' affects diction; choosing 'home' over 'house' or 'dwelling' affects diction; selecting 'verdant' over 'green' affects diction. Distinct from syntax (word arrangement) and from grammar (rules). NYS L.11-12.5 covers vocabulary acquisition; RL.11-12.4 covers determining meaning of words and the impact of word choice on tone. AP English Lit FRQ Question 1 (poetry, 6 points) and Question 2 (prose passage, 6 points) routinely test diction - rubric upper-range awards specific connotation analysis.",
