      "topic": "Style and Voice",
      "explanation": "Voice is the distinctive way a writer expresses ideas - recognizable across works, formed by characteristic diction, syntax, rhythm, point of view, and attitude. Distinct from tone (attitude toward specific subject), style (textual surface choices), and persona (constructed authorial self). Hemingway's voice is paratactic and understated; Henry James's is hypotactic and qualified; Toni Morrison's is allusive and rhythmic. NYS RL.11-12.6 covers analyzing point of view including voice; W.11-12.4 covers producing clear coherent writing in which development organization style are appropriate. AP English Lang FRQ Question 2 (rhetorical analysis, 6 points) and AP English Lit FRQ Question 2 (prose passage, 6 points) reward voice analysis as integrated effect of multiple stylistic choices.",
