      "explanation": "George Orwell's Nineteen Eighty-Four, published June 1949, is the canonical 20th-century dystopian novel - Winston Smith, a 39-year-old Ministry of Truth employee in totalitarian Oceania ruled by the Inner Party and Big Brother, begins a forbidden diary, has a love affair with Julia, is betrayed by O'Brien, and is broken by torture in the Ministry of Love's Room 101. Newspeak, the Thought Police, the Two Minutes Hate, the telescreens, and Room 101's cage of rats organize the world. Orwell wrote it on Jura while dying of tuberculosis. Common Core lists 1984 for Grades 11-12; NYS RL.11-12 standards cover its plot, theme, craft. AP English Lit FRQ Question 3 (open, 8 points) regularly accepts 1984.",
