      "correctText": "Arguable",
      "topic": "Thesis Construction",
      "explanation": "A thesis must be arguable - capable of being supported AND of being contested - to function as the foundation of an argument essay. Distinct from factual claims (verifiable, not arguable: 'the Civil War ended in 1865'), personal preferences (not arguable: 'I prefer Bach to Mozart'), and overly broad claims ('Love is important'). NYS W.11-12.1 requires precise and knowledgeable claims. AP English Lang FRQ Question 3 (argument, 6 points) rubric distinguishes thesis quality at the highest level: 'responds to the prompt with a defensible thesis that establishes a line of reasoning' scores in the upper range; thesis that 'restates the prompt' or 'asserts an obvious truth' scores in the lower range. Specificity AND defensibility together produce arguable thesis.",
