      "topic": "Transitions and Cohesion",
      "explanation": "Contrast transitions ('however,' 'on the contrary,' 'on the other hand,' 'in contrast,' 'nevertheless,' 'yet,' 'although,' 'while') signal a shift in direction, opposing view, or qualifying limitation. In argumentative writing, contrast transitions typically introduce counterclaims, refute opposing views, or limit the writer's own claim. NYS W.11-12.1 requires words and phrases that 'clarify the relationships between claim(s) and counterclaims.' AP English Lang FRQ Question 3 (argument, 6 points) rubric awards essays with discernible counterclaim engagement - contrast transitions explicitly mark that engagement. Compare 'cause-effect' transitions (therefore, consequently, thus) which signal logical entailment.",
