      "prompt": "Author's purpose to amuse or tell a story.",
      "choices": [
        "To persuade",
        "To entertain",
        "Conflict",
        "To inform"
      ],
      "correctText": "To entertain",
      "topic": "Author's Purpose",
      "explanation": "When an author's purpose is to entertain, the text aims to amuse, surprise, or move readers - through humor, suspense, adventure, or emotion. Fiction stories, poems, and humorous essays entertain. NYS Grade 5 ELA State Test literature passages often have an entertain purpose, but informational passages can entertain too if they share fun facts or wild stories. Quote vivid descriptions, surprising details, or humorous lines as evidence of entertainment purpose for 2-point response credit.",
      "domain": "Review",
