      "correctText": "Idiom",
      "topic": "Author's Word Choice",
      "explanation": "An idiom is a common phrase whose meaning differs from the literal words. 'Break a leg' means good luck. 'It's raining cats and dogs' means it's pouring. Idioms are cultural - they make sense only if you know the saying. In Maniac Magee, characters use everyday idioms that signal voice and setting. NYS Grade 5 ELA State Test vocabulary questions sometimes test idioms; students should look for context clues to figure out what an idiom means and avoid taking the words literally.",
