      "prompt": "Numbers that show which paragraph or page a quote came from.",
      "choices": [
        "Synonyms",
        "Paraphrase",
        "Summary citation",
        "Line or paragraph reference"
      ],
      "correctText": "Line or paragraph reference",
      "topic": "Citing Evidence",
      "explanation": "Line or paragraph references are numbers that tell readers exactly where evidence came from in the text - paragraph 3, line 12, page 4. On NYS Grade 5 ELA State Test passages, paragraphs are numbered for easy reference. Students should write 'According to paragraph 4...' or 'In line 15, the author writes...' to anchor their evidence. Top 4-point responses include paragraph or line references with each quotation - the rubric rewards this precision.",
