      "choices": [
        "Summary citation",
        "Multiple causes",
        "Paraphrase",
        "Citation tag"
      ],
      "correctText": "Paraphrase",
      "topic": "Citing Evidence",
      "explanation": "A paraphrase restates an author's idea in your own words without using quotation marks. Paraphrasing shows you understand the text, not just that you can copy it. NYS Grade 5 ELA State Test rubrics accept both direct quotations and paraphrases as text evidence; many graders prefer paraphrases because they show comprehension. Always make sure your paraphrase keeps the original meaning while changing the words - that is the skill graders reward.",
      "domain": "Review",
