      "correctText": "to schedule again",
      "topic": "Language Conventions + Vocabulary (L)",
      "explanation": "The prefix 're-' means 'again' or 'back.' So 'reschedule' means 'to schedule again.' Knowing common prefixes (un-, re-, dis-, pre-) lets you figure out new words without a dictionary.",
