      "id": "ela-5-pe-008",
      "prompt": "Read the fable, then answer the question.\n\n\"The Ant and the Grasshopper\" (a retelling of Aesop)\nAll summer long, a grasshopper hopped through the tall grass, singing and dancing in the warm sun. Nearby, an ant struggled day after day, carrying grains of wheat back to her nest. \"Why work so hard?\" laughed the grasshopper. \"Come sing with me!\" The ant only shook her head and kept walking. When winter came and snow covered the field, the grasshopper had nothing to eat. The ant, warm in her nest, had plenty.\n\nIn the sentence \"Nearby, an ant struggled day after day, carrying grains of wheat back to her nest,\" what does the word \"struggled\" suggest?",
      "choices": [
        "The work was easy for the ant.",
        "The work was difficult, but the ant kept doing it.",
        "The ant lost the grains of wheat.",
        "The ant did not understand what to do."
      ],
      "correctText": "The work was difficult, but the ant kept doing it.",
      "topic": "Reading Literature (RL)",
      "explanation": "To 'struggle' means to work hard against difficulty. The phrase 'day after day' shows the ant kept at it even when it was hard. This word choice helps the author show effort and persistence.",
