      "correctText": "Third person, but the narrator knows Maya's thoughts and feelings",
      "topic": "Reading Literature (RL)",
      "explanation": "The narrator uses 'she' and 'her' (third person) but tells us Maya's inner state — her shaking hands and slow breath. The narrator also knows the grandfather smiled even though Maya does not turn around to see it, which shows a limited-omniscient third-person view.",
