      "prompt": "Read the passage, then answer the question.\n\n\"The Lost Compass\"\nMaya had hiked the same forest trail with her grandfather every summer since she was six. This year, he handed her his old brass compass and said, \"You lead the way.\" Maya's hands shook as she opened it for the first time without him watching. The needle spun, then steadied. She took a slow breath, pointed north, and began to walk. Behind her, her grandfather smiled, but Maya did not turn around to see it.\n\nWhich detail BEST supports the theme that the grandfather trusts Maya?",
      "choices": [
        "Maya has hiked the trail every summer since she was six.",
        "The grandfather hands Maya his old brass compass and tells her to lead.",
        "Maya takes a slow breath before she starts walking.",
        "The needle of the compass spins before it steadies."
      ],
      "correctText": "The grandfather hands Maya his old brass compass and tells her to lead.",
      "topic": "Reading Literature (RL)",
      "explanation": "Citing evidence means pointing to a specific line that proves the idea. The grandfather literally giving Maya his treasured compass and telling her to lead is the clearest action showing trust. The other details describe Maya or the setting, not the grandfather's trust.",
      "domain": "Practice Exam",
      "gradeBand": "Multi",
      "subjectArea": "Review",
      "standardRefs": [],
      "sourceAuthority": "mr-macs-practice-exam",
