      "prompt": "The events that build tension after the introduction but before the climax.",
      "choices": [
        "Cause and effect",
        "Rising action",
        "Context clues",
        "Plot"
      ],
      "correctText": "Rising action",
      "topic": "Story Mountain",
      "explanation": "Rising action is the series of events that build suspense and tension after the exposition and lead up to the climax. In Number the Stars by Lois Lowry, the rising action includes Annemarie hiding her Jewish friend Ellen, the Nazi soldiers searching the apartment, and the dangerous trip to Uncle Henrik's. The Grade 5 ELA State Test asks students to track how problems get worse; identifying rising-action events helps students answer 'cause and effect' and sequencing questions about complications.",
