      "prompt": "A clear statement of the position you will argue.",
      "choices": [
        "Thesis statement",
        "Imagery",
        "Counterclaim",
        "Conclusion"
      ],
      "correctText": "Thesis statement",
      "topic": "Argument Writing",
      "explanation": "A thesis statement is a clear declarative sentence that states the position the writer will argue throughout an essay. Strong Grade 7 thesis statements appear in the introduction, name the topic, and take a defensible position—for example, 'Middle schools should begin no earlier than 8:30 a.m. because adolescents need more sleep, learn better in late mornings, and face health consequences from early starts.' NYS Grade 7 ELA standard W.7.1.a tests thesis development; the state's 4-point essay rubric awards full credit when students place a clear, specific thesis in the introduction.",
      "domain": "Review",
      "gradeBand": "Multi",
      "subjectArea": "Review",
      "standardRefs": [],
