      "correctText": "Counterclaim",
      "topic": "Argument Writing",
      "explanation": "A counterclaim is an opposing argument the writer acknowledges and refutes to demonstrate fairness and strengthen the main argument. In a Grade 7 essay arguing for later start times, the counterclaim might be 'later school starts create child-care problems for working parents.' The writer acknowledges this concern and then refutes it. NYS Grade 7 ELA standard W.7.1.a explicitly requires counterclaim acknowledgment; the state's 4-point rubric distinguishes 2- and 3-point essays (no counterclaim) from full 4-point essays (clear acknowledgment of a real counterclaim with effective refutation).",
      "domain": "Review",
      "gradeBand": "Multi",
