      "explanation": "Evidence is the specific facts, statistics, quotations, examples, or research findings a writer cites to prove that each reason is true. In a Grade 7 essay arguing for later start times, evidence might include American Academy of Pediatrics data showing teen sleep needs, peer-reviewed studies on academic performance, and CDC statistics on teen drowsy-driving accidents. NYS Grade 7 ELA standard W.7.1.b tests evidence use directly; the state's 4-point rubric awards full credit when students cite at least two pieces of specific evidence per reason, attribute the source, and link it explicitly to the reason.",
