      "explanation": "Technical (or domain-specific) vocabulary is the specialized language used within a particular subject or profession—words like 'photosynthesis' in biology, 'tectonic plate' in earth science, or 'tariff' in economics. Grade 7 informational texts in science and social studies are dense with technical vocabulary that readers must decode using context, root words, or glossaries. NYS Grade 7 ELA standard L.7.6 tests technical vocabulary; the state's 2-point rubric awards full credit when students define a technical term using context clues and explain why precise vocabulary matters in the discipline.",
