      "correctText": "Bias",
      "topic": "Bias + Perspective",
      "explanation": "Bias is a one-sided view that favors a particular position or group, often shown through selective evidence, loaded language, or omission of counterarguments. A Grade 7 article that quotes only people who agree with its position shows source bias. NYS Grade 7 ELA standard RI.7.6 tests bias recognition through questions asking students to identify which side an author favors and why; the state's 2-point short-answer rubric awards full credit when students label the bias, cite two pieces of text evidence (loaded language, one-sided quotation, omitted perspective), and explain the effect on readers.",
