      "correctText": "Dynamic character",
      "topic": "Character Types",
      "explanation": "A dynamic character undergoes meaningful internal change in beliefs, values, or self-understanding across the narrative. Crash Coogan in Jerry Spinelli's Crash (1996) is the canonical Grade 7 dynamic character: he transforms from a bullying football star into a friend who chooses kindness over winning. Auggie Pullman in R.J. Palacio's Wonder also shows dynamic growth. NYS Grade 7 ELA standard RL.7.3 explicitly tests dynamic-character analysis; the state rubric awards full credit when students cite a beginning trait, an ending trait, and the catalyst that caused the change.",
