      "correctText": "Static character",
      "topic": "Character Types",
      "explanation": "A static character does not undergo meaningful internal change; their values and behaviors stay consistent from start to finish. Dally Winston in S.E. Hinton's The Outsiders is largely static—his hardness and cynicism never soften—which makes his grief over Johnny's death emotionally devastating. Mrs. Pullman in Wonder remains a steady source of love throughout. NYS Grade 7 ELA standard RL.7.3 tests the contrast between static and dynamic characters through compare-and-contrast items; the rubric rewards specific evidence of consistency for static characters paired with evidence of change for dynamic ones.",
