      "correctText": "Antagonist",
      "topic": "Character Types",
      "explanation": "The antagonist creates the central conflict the protagonist must struggle against; the antagonist may be a person, group, force of nature, or internal struggle. In S.E. Hinton's The Outsiders, Bob Sheldon and the Socs serve as antagonists; in R.J. Palacio's Wonder (2012), Julian Albans antagonizes Auggie at Beecher Prep; in Jerry Spinelli's Crash, Crash himself initially antagonizes Penn Webb. NYS Grade 7 ELA standard RL.7.3 frequently tests antagonist identification; constructed-response items on the state test award points for explaining how the antagonist's motives reveal theme.",
