      "correctText": "Protagonist",
      "topic": "Character Types",
      "explanation": "The protagonist is the central character whose decisions and growth drive the narrative. Ponyboy Curtis is the protagonist of S.E. Hinton's The Outsiders (1967); Salamanca Tree Hiddle is the protagonist of Sharon Creech's Walk Two Moons (1994); Josh Bell is the protagonist of Kwame Alexander's verse novel The Crossover (2014). NYS Grade 7 ELA standard RL.7.3 requires students to trace how a protagonist changes across a text; the state's 2-point rubric for short-answer items awards full credit only when students provide two pieces of textual evidence showing internal or external change in the central figure.",
