      "correctText": "Characterization",
      "topic": "Character Types",
      "explanation": "Characterization is the set of techniques authors use to reveal personality, often summarized by the STEAL acronym (Speech, Thoughts, Effect on others, Actions, Looks). R.J. Palacio characterizes Auggie in Wonder through multiple narrators—Auggie himself, his sister Via, his friend Summer—so readers see him through varied perspectives. Hinton characterizes Ponyboy through his own first-person narration in The Outsiders. NYS Grade 7 ELA standard RL.7.3 requires students to analyze characterization techniques; the state's 4-point essay rubric awards full credit only when students cite at least two STEAL categories with textual evidence.",
