      "correctText": "Argument",
      "topic": "Citing Evidence",
      "explanation": "An argument is the central claim an author makes and supports through reasoning and evidence in an informational or persuasive text. In a Grade 7 op-ed on school start times, the author's argument might be that middle schools should start later because teenagers need more sleep. NYS Grade 7 ELA standard RI.7.8 explicitly tests argument analysis; the state's 4-point extended-response rubric awards full credit when students state the author's argument as a complete sentence and identify at least two pieces of supporting reasoning or evidence cited in the text.",
