      "correctText": "Inference",
      "topic": "Citing Evidence",
      "explanation": "An inference is a logical conclusion a reader draws by combining specific text clues with background knowledge, going beyond what is directly stated. NYS Grade 7 ELA standard RI.7.1 makes inferential reading a central skill: state-test items often ask students to infer an author's attitude, an unstated cause, or a probable consequence based on textual evidence. The state's 2-point rubric awards full credit when students state the inference and cite two specific text clues that justify it—random guesses without textual grounding receive zero points.",
