      "correctText": "Fact",
      "topic": "Citing Evidence",
      "explanation": "A fact is a statement that can be verified through observation, measurement, or trusted sources—distinct from opinion, which expresses a personal belief or judgment. 'The moon orbits Earth approximately every 27.3 days' is a fact; 'the moon is beautiful' is an opinion. NYS Grade 7 ELA standard RI.7.8 tests the fact-versus-opinion distinction directly; the state's 2-point rubric awards full credit when students label two statements correctly (one fact, one opinion) and explain how each could be verified (or why an opinion cannot be).",
