      "correctText": "Citing evidence",
      "topic": "Citing Evidence",
      "explanation": "Citing evidence means quoting or paraphrasing specific text from an informational article to support a claim, then explaining the connection in your own words. The NYS Grade 7 ELA standard RI.7.1 makes this the foundational reading skill: every short-answer and extended-response item demands evidence-based responses. The state's 2-point short-answer rubric awards 1 point for an accurate claim and 1 point for a specific text-based citation—quotation marks, attribution, or paragraph reference—with explicit explanation of how the evidence supports the claim.",
