      "correctText": "Paraphrase",
      "topic": "Citing Evidence",
      "explanation": "Paraphrasing is restating information in one's own words while preserving the original meaning, distinct from quoting (using exact words) and summarizing (a brief overview). Effective paraphrase requires changing both vocabulary and sentence structure. NYS Grade 7 ELA standard W.7.8 tests paraphrasing through evidence-based writing prompts; the state's 4-point essay rubric rewards students who paraphrase sources accurately and clearly, without copying source language, and who give credit through embedded references like 'according to the article' or 'the author explains.'",
