      "explanation": "Character vs character is the most common external conflict, in which the protagonist directly opposes another individual or group. Ponyboy and the greasers versus Bob Sheldon and the Socs drive S.E. Hinton's The Outsiders; Crash Coogan versus Penn Webb drives Jerry Spinelli's Crash before evolving into friendship. NYS Grade 7 ELA standard RL.7.3 tests character-vs-character conflict frequently on multiple-choice and short-answer items; the 2-point rubric requires both a correct conflict label and one piece of evidence showing the direct opposition between named figures.",
