      "topic": "Conflict Types",
      "explanation": "Internal conflict happens inside a character's thoughts, values, or emotions—desire against duty, hope against fear. Salamanca's internal conflict in Sharon Creech's Walk Two Moons is her struggle to accept her mother's death; Josh Bell's internal conflict in Kwame Alexander's The Crossover is his envy of his brother Jordan's new relationship. NYS Grade 7 ELA standard RL.7.3 tests internal conflict through inference questions; the state's 2-point rubric awards full credit when students cite a character's thoughts or self-talk as evidence of inner struggle and connect it to a decision.",
