      "correctText": "Character vs society",
      "topic": "Conflict Types",
      "explanation": "This conflict places the protagonist against the laws, customs, or institutions of their community. In Sharon Flake's The Skin I'm In (1998), Maleeka Madison's conflict is with the racist hierarchy of her middle school's beauty standards. In Alan Gratz's Refugee, all three protagonists face character-vs-society conflicts with hostile nations refusing them shelter. NYS Grade 7 ELA standard RL.7.3 frequently pairs character-vs-society with historical or social context; the rubric requires students to name the social force and explain how the character resists, accommodates, or is defeated by it.",
