      "explanation": "Word choice (diction) is an author's deliberate selection of specific words to create tone, mood, or precise meaning. Karen Hesse's word choice in Out of the Dust—spare nouns, no contractions, repeated 'dust'—mirrors Dust Bowl deprivation. Sharon Flake's word choice in The Skin I'm In (1998) captures Maleeka's seventh-grade voice with slang and rhythm. NYS Grade 7 ELA standards RL.7.4 and RI.7.4 both test word-choice analysis; the state's 2-point rubric rewards students who quote the specific word, name its connotation, and explain its tonal or thematic effect.",
