      "explanation": "Connotation is the emotional or evaluative weight a word carries beyond its dictionary definition—'home' versus 'house,' or 'slender' versus 'skinny' versus 'scrawny' all denote similar things but connote different feelings. NYS Grade 7 ELA standard L.7.5.c explicitly tests connotation; the state's 2-point rubric awards full credit when students explain why two near-synonyms carry different emotional weight, name whether each is positive, neutral, or negative, and apply this distinction to evaluate an author's word choices in a Grade 7 informational or literary passage from the test.",
