      "prompt": "Reasoning that explains why the counterclaim fails.",
      "choices": [
        "Counterclaim",
        "Simile",
        "Counterclaim signal",
        "Refutation reasoning"
      ],
      "correctText": "Refutation reasoning",
      "topic": "Counterclaim",
      "explanation": "Refutation reasoning is the logical explanation of why a counterclaim is incorrect, irrelevant, or weaker than the main argument. After acknowledging a counterclaim, strong Grade 7 writers explain through reasoning and evidence why their original position still stands. NYS Grade 7 ELA standard W.7.1 explicitly requires this reasoning move in argumentative writing; the state's 4-point rubric awards full credit when students provide both the rebuttal claim and clear logical reasoning that explains the flaw in the counterclaim, supported by at least one piece of evidence.",
