      "correctText": "Topic sentence",
      "topic": "Essay Structure",
      "explanation": "A topic sentence is the first sentence of a body paragraph that states the paragraph's main point and previews how it supports the thesis. In a Grade 7 essay arguing for later school starts, a topic sentence might read 'First, adolescent biology demands more sleep than younger children require.' NYS Grade 7 ELA standard W.7.1.c tests topic sentences; the state's 4-point rubric awards full credit when students place a clear topic sentence at the start of each body paragraph and develop it with evidence and explanation in the sentences that follow.",
