      "prompt": "Words and phrases that connect ideas across sentences and paragraphs.",
      "choices": [
        "Transitions",
        "Body paragraph",
        "Introduction",
        "Counterclaim"
      ],
      "correctText": "Transitions",
      "topic": "Essay Structure",
      "explanation": "Transitions are words and phrases that connect ideas across sentences and paragraphs, signaling logical relationships such as addition (also, furthermore), cause and effect (because, therefore), comparison (similarly, in contrast), and sequence (first, finally). NYS Grade 7 ELA standard W.7.1.c explicitly tests transition use; the state's 4-point rubric awards full credit when students use varied, accurate transitions that signal relationships between ideas, avoiding repetition of basic connectors like 'and then' and overuse of simple sequencers like 'firstly, secondly, thirdly.'",
