      "correctText": "Controlling idea",
      "topic": "Informative Writing",
      "explanation": "The controlling idea in informative writing is a clear sentence in the introduction stating what the essay will explain, similar to a thesis in argumentative writing but without taking a position. A Grade 7 informative essay on photosynthesis might have the controlling idea 'Photosynthesis is the process by which plants use sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide to produce energy.' NYS Grade 7 ELA standard W.7.2.a tests controlling-idea development; the 4-point rubric awards full credit when students provide a clear central focus that the body paragraphs systematically develop.",
