      "explanation": "An example is a concrete instance that illustrates a general idea, making abstract concepts accessible to readers. In a Grade 7 informative essay on adaptation, examples might include the polar bear's white fur, the cactus's water-storing stem, and the giraffe's long neck. NYS Grade 7 ELA standard W.7.2.b tests example use; the state's 4-point rubric awards full credit when students integrate at least two specific examples per main point and explain how each example illustrates the general concept being developed.",
