      "id": "ela-7-pe-029",
      "prompt": "Choose the pair that best completes the analogy:\n\nGENEROUS is to STINGY as BRAVE is to ____.",
      "choices": [
        "courageous",
        "fearless",
        "cowardly",
        "kind"
      ],
      "correctText": "cowardly",
      "topic": "Language Conventions + Vocabulary (L)",
      "explanation": "The first pair (generous/stingy) are antonyms — opposites. To follow that relationship, 'brave' must be paired with its opposite, which is 'cowardly.' Courageous and fearless are synonyms of brave, and 'kind' is unrelated.",
