      "explanation": "A summary is a brief, objective restatement of an informational text's main idea and most important supporting details, written in the student's own words and excluding personal opinions. NYS Grade 7 ELA standard RI.7.2 explicitly tests summary writing through 2-point short-answer items and 4-point extended-response prompts. The state rubric awards full credit when summaries state the main idea, include two-to-three key supporting points, exclude minor details, and remain neutral in tone. Plagiarized or opinion-laden summaries receive zero or partial credit per the official rubric.",
