      "explanation": "A supporting detail is a specific fact, example, statistic, quotation, or anecdote that develops or proves the main idea. In a Grade 7 informational text about the moon, supporting details might include the exact distance from Earth (about 238,855 miles), the date of Apollo 11's landing (July 20, 1969), and Neil Armstrong's recorded words. NYS Grade 7 ELA standard RI.7.1 tests supporting-detail identification through 2-point short-answer items; the state rubric awards full credit when students cite two specific details and explain how each supports the central claim.",
