      "explanation": "A narrative essay tells a real or imagined story with characters, setting, conflict, and plot, often to convey a theme or significant insight rather than to argue or inform. Grade 7 narratives include personal essays about formative experiences and fictional short stories. NYS Grade 7 ELA standard W.7.3 tests narrative writing directly; the state's 4-point rubric awards full credit when students engage readers by establishing a context and point of view, develop characters and events using dialogue and sensory description, use transitions to sequence events, and provide a conclusion that reflects on the experience.",
