      "correctText": "Verb",
      "topic": "Parts of Speech",
      "explanation": "A verb expresses action ('Ponyboy runs') or state of being ('Auggie is brave'); verbs are the engine of every sentence and determine tense, voice, and mood. Grade 7 grammar emphasizes consistent verb tense and subject-verb agreement in writing. NYS Grade 7 ELA standard L.7.1 explicitly tests verb forms and consistency; the state's 4-point rubric for writing evaluates verb-tense consistency under conventions, and short-answer items often ask students to identify whether verb shifts within a paragraph are intentional or errors that should be corrected.",
