      "correctText": "Falling action",
      "topic": "Plot Structure",
      "explanation": "Falling action consists of the consequences that follow the climax and steer the story toward resolution. In Karen Hesse's Out of the Dust (1997), the falling action follows the kitchen fire and Billie Jo's mother's death as Billie Jo runs west then returns to her father; in Walk Two Moons, the falling action covers Sal and her father grieving together. NYS Grade 7 ELA standard RL.7.3 tests falling action through questions asking how post-climax events shape theme; the state's 4-point extended-response rubric rewards explicit connections between consequences and the central message.",
