      "correctText": "Climax",
      "topic": "Plot Structure",
      "explanation": "The climax is the highest-tension moment when the protagonist confronts the central conflict and the outcome becomes inevitable. In S.E. Hinton's The Outsiders, the climax occurs when Johnny stabs Bob to save Ponyboy at the fountain; in Sharon Creech's Walk Two Moons (1994), the climax is Salamanca's discovery at the bus crash site. NYS Grade 7 ELA standard RL.7.3 requires students to distinguish climax from rising action; constructed-response items on the state test award full credit only when students cite the specific moment and explain why tension peaks there.",
