      "correctText": "Plot",
      "topic": "Plot Structure",
      "explanation": "Plot is the structured chain of events that drives a narrative, traditionally diagrammed by German novelist Gustav Freytag (1863) as exposition, rising action, climax, falling action, and resolution. In S.E. Hinton's The Outsiders (1967), the plot traces Ponyboy and Johnny from a Tulsa drive-in encounter through the killing of Bob Sheldon, the church fire, and the rumble. NYS Grade 7 ELA standard RL.7.3 tests plot tracking through multi-part questions that ask students to identify cause-and-effect relationships across paragraphs, with the 2-point rubric requiring two pieces of textual evidence.",
