      "correctText": "Refrain",
      "topic": "Poetic Devices",
      "explanation": "A refrain is a phrase or line repeated at regular intervals in a poem or song, often at the end of stanzas, creating emphasis, rhythm, and emotional intensification. Edgar Allan Poe uses 'In her tomb by the side of the sea' as the refrain throughout 'Annabel Lee' (1849) to deepen grief through repetition. Alfred Noyes returns to 'the highwayman came riding' throughout his ballad. NYS Grade 7 ELA standard RL.7.5 tests refrain analysis; the state's 2-point rubric rewards students who identify the repeated line and explain how repetition intensifies emotion or unifies the poem.",
