      "correctText": "First person",
      "topic": "Point of View",
      "explanation": "First-person narration uses I, me, we, us pronouns, giving readers direct access to one character's mind but limited knowledge of others. Ponyboy narrates S.E. Hinton's The Outsiders in first person; Salamanca narrates Walk Two Moons; Billie Jo narrates Out of the Dust in first-person verse. NYS Grade 7 ELA standard RL.7.6 tests how first-person POV shapes interpretation; constructed-response items award full credit when students cite a moment when the first-person narrator's limited knowledge creates suspense, dramatic irony, or sympathy for the speaker.",
