      "prompt": "A mark that ends a statement.",
      "choices": [
        "Period",
        "Comma",
        "Caption",
        "Apostrophe"
      ],
      "correctText": "Period",
      "topic": "Punctuation",
      "explanation": "A period ends a declarative or imperative sentence and signals a full stop in thought. Periods also follow many abbreviations (Mr., Dr., a.m.). Misuse of periods—particularly in sentence fragments and run-on sentences—accounts for many Grade 7 writing errors. NYS Grade 7 ELA standard L.7.2 tests end-punctuation accuracy; the 2-point rubric awards full credit when students place periods at the end of complete sentences and avoid fragments (incomplete sentences ending in periods) and run-ons (multiple complete thoughts joined without periods or appropriate punctuation marks).",
