      "correctText": "Dynamic character",
      "topic": "Reading Lit Concepts",
      "explanation": "A dynamic character undergoes meaningful internal change in beliefs, values, or self-understanding. Crash Coogan in Jerry Spinelli's Crash (1996) is the canonical Grade 7 dynamic character—a bully transformed by friendship into someone who chooses kindness. Charles 'Crash' Coogan transforms across the novel through Penn Webb's persistent gentleness. NYS Grade 7 ELA standard RL.7.3 tests dynamic-character analysis through 2-point short-answer items; the state rubric awards full credit when students cite a specific beginning trait, an ending trait, and the catalyst event that triggered the meaningful internal change.",
