      "explanation": "Foreshadowing is the author's deliberate placement of hints, images, or statements that anticipate later events, building suspense and reader anticipation. In Karen Hesse's Out of the Dust (1997), the early image of dust 'seeping into everything' foreshadows the cumulative damage to Billie Jo's family. In S.E. Hinton's The Outsiders, Johnny carrying a switchblade foreshadows the killing of Bob Sheldon. NYS Grade 7 ELA standard RL.7.5 tests foreshadowing through 2-point short-answer items; the state rubric awards full credit when students cite a specific foreshadowing detail and the later event it anticipates.",
