      "correctText": "Mood",
      "topic": "Setting + Atmosphere",
      "explanation": "Mood is the emotional atmosphere a reader experiences—suspenseful, melancholy, hopeful, foreboding—created through setting details, word choice, and pacing. Karen Hesse's Out of the Dust creates an oppressive, mournful mood through repeated images of dust seeping through windows and into food. Alfred Noyes's poem 'The Highwayman' (1906) creates a dark, foreboding mood through midnight setting and 'ghostly galleon' imagery. NYS Grade 7 ELA standard RL.7.4 distinguishes mood from tone; the 2-point rubric rewards students who name the mood and cite two sensory or descriptive details that produce it.",
