      "explanation": "Compare-and-contrast structure examines similarities and differences between two or more subjects, signaled by transitions like 'similarly,' 'in contrast,' 'unlike,' 'on the other hand,' and 'both.' A Grade 7 article might compare and contrast the school systems of Japan and the United States. NYS Grade 7 ELA standard RI.7.5 tests this structure through both multiple-choice items and 2-point short answers; the state rubric rewards students who identify the two subjects, name a key similarity and a key difference, and cite transition words that signal the structure.",
