      "correctText": "Description",
      "topic": "Text Structures",
      "explanation": "Descriptive (or list) structure presents features, examples, or characteristics of a topic, often in no required order, signaled by transitions like 'for example,' 'in addition,' 'also,' and 'another feature.' A Grade 7 informational article about deep-sea creatures might list features of giant squid, anglerfish, and octopuses without strict sequence. NYS Grade 7 ELA standard RI.7.5 tests descriptive structure; the state's 2-point rubric awards credit when students name the structure, identify two listed features, and explain why an unordered list suits the author's purpose.",
