      "prompt": "How a central message deepens across the course of a text.",
      "choices": [
        "Theme development",
        "Apostrophe",
        "Theme",
        "Moral"
      ],
      "correctText": "Theme development",
      "topic": "Theme Building",
      "explanation": "Theme development is how an author advances a central idea through accumulating events, character changes, and symbolic patterns from beginning through climax to resolution. In Sharon Creech's Walk Two Moons (1994), the theme that grief must be shared develops as Sal's road trip with her grandparents teaches her to speak her mother's death aloud. NYS Grade 7 ELA standard RL.7.2 tests theme development through 4-point essays asking students to trace the central message across three text sections; the state rubric requires textual evidence from beginning, middle, and end for full credit.",
