      "correctText": "Topic",
      "topic": "Theme Building",
      "explanation": "Topic is the broad subject of a text—stated in one or two words like 'family,' 'identity,' 'prejudice'—distinct from theme, which is the complete-sentence claim about that topic. The topic of Sharon Creech's Walk Two Moons is grief; its theme is that grief must be walked through with others, not avoided. The topic of Wonder is appearance; its theme is that what people look like matters less than how they treat others. NYS Grade 7 ELA standard RL.7.2 tests the topic-versus-theme distinction; students who name only the topic on essay rubrics receive partial credit at most.",
