      "correctText": "Verbal irony — the sister says the opposite of what she means, gently teasing Marcus.",
      "topic": "Language Conventions + Vocabulary (L)",
      "explanation": "Verbal irony occurs when a speaker says something whose intended meaning is the opposite of the literal words. A dropped cake is anything but a 'smooth landing,' and the contrast between what is said and what happened produces the gentle teasing effect.",
      "domain": "Practice Exam",
      "gradeBand": "Multi",
      "subjectArea": "Review",
      "standardRefs": [],
