      "correctText": "I finished reading The Call of the Wild before watching the film Hidden Figures.",
      "topic": "Language Conventions + Vocabulary (L)",
      "explanation": "Standard convention places titles of long, stand-alone works — novels and feature films — in italics (or, when italics are unavailable, in plain capitalization as shown here). Quotation marks are reserved for short works (poems, short stories, song titles, episode titles). Only choice D follows the convention for both titles.",
