      "correctText": "Author's purpose",
      "topic": "Purpose + Audience",
      "explanation": "Author's purpose is the reason the author wrote a text—commonly summarized as PIE: to Persuade, Inform, Entertain. Some texts blend purposes—a memoir may inform readers about a period while also entertaining and possibly persuading. NYS Grade 8 ELA standard RI.8.6 explicitly tests how 'an author acknowledges and responds to conflicting evidence or viewpoints' to convey purpose; state-test items ask students to identify purpose and explain how specific text choices (word choice, tone, structure, evidence) reveal it, with the 2-point rubric requiring two pieces of textual evidence.",
