      "explanation": "Audience is the specific group of readers the author writes for—signaled by vocabulary level, examples chosen, tone, formality, and assumed background knowledge. A science article for adults differs from one for middle-schoolers in jargon, sentence length, and visual support. NYS Grade 8 ELA standard W.8.4 explicitly addresses audience awareness; standard RI.8.6 tests recognizing audience from textual cues. State-test items may ask 'who is the most likely intended audience?' with the rubric awarding credit when students cite specific language features (vocabulary, examples, assumed knowledge) that signal audience.",
