      "correctText": "Synecdoche",
      "topic": "Figurative Language",
      "explanation": "Synecdoche substitutes a part for the whole (or vice versa). 'All hands on deck' uses 'hands' for sailors; 'the crown' uses a crown for monarchy. L.9-10.5a covers figurative language. RL.9-10.4 covers figurative meaning. Regents Part 2 multiple-choice may test synecdoche; AP Lang rhetorical analysis essays reward identification. Often confused with metonymy (related but separate concept). Modern: 'the Pentagon decided' (the building for the military leadership).",
