      "explanation": "Connell sets up Rainsford as a celebrated big-game hunter who initially dismisses animals' fear, then Zaroff reveals himself as a refined cannibal-hunter who quotes Marcus Aurelius. The foil collapses Rainsford's confident hierarchy. RL.9-10.3 asks how characters develop a theme. The closing line, 'He had never slept in a better bed,' inverts moral expectations. Regents Part 3 prompts on ethical complexity favor this story.",
