      "correctText": "Foil",
      "topic": "Foil Characters",
      "explanation": "A foil is a character whose traits contrast with another to illuminate that character. Mercutio's cynicism about love ('If love be rough with you, be rough with love') foils Romeo's idealism. RL.9-10.3 asks students to analyze how complex characters develop through interaction. Shakespeare uses Mercutio's Queen Mab speech (1.4) to expose Romeo's lovesickness. Regents Part 3: 'How does the relationship between two characters develop a central idea?'.",
