      "prompt": "A narrative that hints at future events through suggestion uses this technique.",
      "choices": [
        "Classification definition",
        "Relevant",
        "Foreshadowing",
        "Rhetorical question"
      ],
      "correctText": "Foreshadowing",
      "topic": "Hook Strategies",
      "explanation": "Foreshadowing plants hints of future events to build suspense or thematic resonance. Romeo and Juliet's Prologue announces 'star-cross'd lovers' will die, then the entire play foreshadows the deaths. W.9-10.3c covers narrative techniques. Regents Part 4 text-analysis writing benefits from recognizing foreshadowing in source texts. AP Lit narrative writing rewards strategic foreshadowing; analysis essays prize identification of foreshadowing's thematic effect.",
