      "correctText": "Statistic hook",
      "topic": "Hook Strategies",
      "explanation": "Statistic hooks (a.k.a. data openers) begin with a startling number to seize attention: 'Every twelve minutes, an American teen attempts suicide.' Effective in expository and argumentative writing when the data is credible and relevant. W.9-10.2a covers engaging openings for informational/explanatory texts. Regents Part 3 source-based argument essays accept this opening. AP Lang argument essays reward credible statistic openings but penalize fabricated or irrelevant numbers.",
