      "explanation": "Anecdote opens an essay with a brief, vivid story illustrating a larger point. Effective in expository, argumentative, and narrative writing. W.9-10.3a covers narrative openings. Regents Part 3 source-based argument essays sometimes accept anecdotal openings; AP Lang argument and rhetorical analysis essays often praise them when the anecdote sets up the broader argument. Beware: anecdotes must support, not substitute for, broader evidence.",
