      "correctText": "Spectacular",
      "topic": "Latin and Greek Roots",
      "explanation": "Latin root 'spec/spect' (look, see) generates 'inspect' (look into), 'spectator' (one who looks), 'spectacular' (worth looking at), 'speculate' (look from above, theorize), 'perspective' (look through), 'suspect' (look from beneath, doubt). L.9-10.4b requires roots and affixes. Regents Part 2 vocabulary tests root recognition. AP Lang and AP Lit assume root literacy. Note Latin morphology: prefix + root + suffix yields meaning through composition.",
