      "explanation": "Cause-and-effect organization explains how events produce outcomes (or how outcomes follow from events). Can be single cause/multiple effects, multiple causes/single effect, or chains. W.9-10.2a covers organizing complex ideas. Regents Part 4 text-analysis writing often analyzes cause-effect in source texts. AP Lang synthesis essays often hinge on causal reasoning. Avoid post hoc fallacies (mistaking sequence for causation).",
