      "explanation": "Climax is the moment of greatest tension where the protagonist's fate pivots. Romeo's killing of Tybalt and instant banishment by the Prince in 3.1 lock the lovers' tragic trajectory; nothing afterward can restore the original possibility of reconciliation. On Common Core RL.9-10.5, students analyze how an author's choices about plot order create effects; pinpointing climax is the central move. Regents short-response often hinges on this.",
