      "explanation": "Complications are events that intensify the central conflict. In Romeo and Juliet 3.1, Mercutio's 'A plague o' both your houses!' and Romeo's revenge killing of Tybalt push the love story toward tragedy. RL.9-10.3 asks students to analyze how complex characters develop over the course of a text; tracking complications is the mechanism. Common Regents task: 'How does an event in lines X-Y advance the plot?'.",
