      "topic": "Plot Structures in R&J",
      "explanation": "Polyphemus, son of Poseidon, traps Odysseus's crew in his cave in Book 9. Odysseus identifies himself as 'Nobody' (outis), blinds the Cyclops with a heated olive stake, and escapes under sheep. His later boastful revelation of his real name triggers Poseidon's curse, the engine of the wandering. RL.9-10.3 covers cause-effect in plot. Regents tasks on hubris and consequence often draw from this episode.",
