      "correctText": "Resolution",
      "topic": "Plot Structures in R&J",
      "explanation": "Resolution (denouement) ties off loose threads after the climax. The Prince's 'glooming peace' and the gold statue promise reconcile the warring houses, restoring civic order at tragic cost. Aristotle called this catastrophe in tragedy. RL.9-10.5 asks how an author structures a text for effect; analyzing how resolutions deliver meaning is a high-value Regents move. Common Part 2 question: 'How does the ending develop a central idea?'.",
