      "explanation": "Harper Lee uses Atticus Finch's repeated lesson to Scout in Chapter 3 to develop empathy as the novel's moral center. Scout's growth (Boo Radley's porch view in Chapter 31) measures her ability to walk in others' skin. RL.9-10.2 covers theme development across the text. Regents Part 3 source-based argument essays frequently use TKAM to evidence themes of empathy, justice, or moral courage. The Common Core exemplar list includes this text.",
