      "explanation": "Harper Lee uses first-person retrospective narration: adult Scout looks back on her 6-9-year-old experiences, allowing both childlike observation and adult reflection. RL.9-10.6 asks how authors develop point of view to create effects like suspense or sympathy. The double perspective lets Lee dramatize Scout's innocence while moralizing through Atticus. Regents Part 2 multiple-choice frequently tests POV identification; Part 3 essays analyze its effect on theme.",
