      "explanation": "Third-person omniscient narration accesses any character's thoughts and roams freely across time and place. Homer narrates from Olympus's view, knowing Athena's plans and the suitors' fates. Orwell's omniscient narrator in Animal Farm appears neutral but cues readers to see propaganda. RL.9-10.6 asks how POV shapes meaning. Regents tasks often contrast omniscient panorama with first-person limitation.",
