      "correctText": "Chiasmus",
      "topic": "Rhetorical Devices",
      "explanation": "Chiasmus reverses the order of words in parallel clauses (ABBA pattern). JFK's 1961 inaugural address features the famous 'Ask not what your country can do for you—ask what you can do for your country.' Mae West: 'It's not the men in my life, it's the life in my men.' RI.9-10.6 covers advanced rhetorical figures. Regents Part 3 source-based arguments on civic identity sometimes use JFK. AP Lang demands precise device-naming (chiasmus vs antimetabole).",
