      "correctText": "Verbal irony",
      "topic": "Rhetorical Devices",
      "explanation": "Verbal irony means the opposite of what is said. Antony's funeral oration in Julius Caesar 3.2 repeats 'Brutus is an honourable man' with rising sarcasm until the crowd hears it as accusation. RI.9-10.6 and RL.9-10.4 both cover irony. Regents Part 2 multiple-choice tests irony types: verbal (saying opposite), situational (event-outcome mismatch), dramatic (audience knows what character does not). AP Lang rewards precise irony analysis.",
