      "correctText": "Sensory hook",
      "topic": "Sensory Detail",
      "explanation": "Sensory hooks open with immediate sensory immersion: the heat of a Maycomb sidewalk, the salt-spray of Ship-Trap Island. W.9-10.3a explicitly requires 'engaging' narrative openings with 'precise words and phrases, telling details, and sensory language.' Regents Part 4 text-analysis writing rewards engagement. AP Lang narrative openings on the synthesis or argument essays often reward sensory immediacy. Strong sensory openings model the descriptive technique the writer will use throughout.",
