      "explanation": "Effective narrative writing engages all five senses: sight, sound, smell, taste, touch. W.9-10.3d explicitly requires 'precise words and phrases, telling details, and sensory language to convey a vivid picture of the experiences, events, setting, and/or characters.' Beginning writers tend to over-rely on sight; smell and sound are underused and powerful. Regents Part 4 text-analysis writing rewards vivid prose. AP Lang and AP Lit reward sensory range as sophistication.",
