      "explanation": "'Show, don't tell' is the foundational narrative principle: demonstrate emotion, character, and meaning through action, dialogue, and sensory detail rather than stating it directly. Instead of 'Scout was scared,' write 'Scout's hand tightened around Atticus's coat sleeve.' W.9-10.3d explicitly requires sensory language to convey experience. Regents Part 4 text-analysis writing rewards showing. AP Lit narrative scenes reward showing as a sophistication marker.",
