      "explanation": "Harper Lee's 1960 novel uses Depression-era Maycomb as more than backdrop; the town's Jim Crow racial codes, economic stagnation, and gossip networks generate the Tom Robinson trial. RL.9-10.3 expects students to analyze how setting shapes character and theme. Atticus Finch's defense of Robinson is unthinkable outside this specific time-place. Regents Part 3 prompts frequently ask how setting develops a central idea like prejudice or moral courage.",
