      "explanation": "George Orwell's Animal Farm (1945) uses the farm as setting whose name changes signal political transformation: Manor Farm to Animal Farm to Manor Farm again. The setting traces the Russian Revolution from Tsar to Stalin. RL.9-10.5 asks how structural choices create meaning; the farm's spatial changes (windmill, farmhouse occupancy) embody Orwell's argument about corruption of revolution. Regents argument essays often cite this.",
