      "correctText": "Symbolic setting",
      "topic": "Setting as Theme",
      "explanation": "Steinbeck names his town Soledad ('solitude/loneliness') and frames the novella with the Salinas riverbank, the only Eden George and Lennie ever share. The bunkhouse, by contrast, is a transient migrant space. RL.9-10.4 covers analyzing word choice for meaning; Steinbeck's place names enact theme. Regents Part 3 source-based arguments on the American Dream often draw evidence from setting as symbol.",
