      "correctText": "March on Washington",
      "topic": "Speech Analysis",
      "explanation": "The March on Washington for Jobs and Freedom (August 28, 1963) drew 250,000 to the Lincoln Memorial. King's 'I Have a Dream' speech anchored the event and pressured passage of the 1964 Civil Rights Act. RI.9-10.6 covers point of view shaped by context; RI.9-10.9 analyzes documents of historical/literary significance. Regents Part 3 source-based argument essays on civil rights often require historical contextualization.",
