      "correctText": "Gothic atmosphere",
      "topic": "Symbolism in The Raven",
      "explanation": "Gothic atmosphere relies on darkness, mystery, decay, and isolation. Poe layers 'midnight dreary,' 'each separate dying ember,' 'silken sad uncertain rustling' to evoke psychological dread. RL.9-10.4 examines connotative word choice; Poe's diction is calibrated for melancholy. The Gothic mode (Walpole, Shelley, Poe) shapes Regents Part 3 source-based prompts on atmosphere and tone. Frankenstein excerpts often pair with The Raven.",
