      "correctText": "Animal Farm",
      "topic": "Texts and Authors",
      "explanation": "George Orwell's Animal Farm (1945) satirizes the Russian Revolution: Old Major (Marx/Lenin), Napoleon (Stalin), Snowball (Trotsky), Boxer (working class). The seven commandments shrink to one. RL.9-10.2 covers theme; RL.9-10.5 covers structure. Regents Part 3 source-based argument essays on power, propaganda, or revolution often draw on Animal Farm. AP Lang argument essays may pair it with primary documents on Stalin.",
