      "correctText": "Theme",
      "topic": "Theme Statements",
      "explanation": "Theme is not a topic (love, war, freedom) but a complete statement of insight ('Love that defies social rules brings tragedy'). RL.9-10.2 requires students to determine a theme and analyze its development across a text via specific details. Common Core distinguishes theme from summary. Regents Part 2 multiple-choice and Part 3 source-based argument both demand theme identification supported by textual evidence.",
