      "topic": "Theme Statements",
      "explanation": "Mary Shelley subtitled Frankenstein 'The Modern Prometheus.' Victor's pursuit of forbidden knowledge mirrors Prometheus's fire, and the Creature reads Paradise Lost, Plutarch, and Werther, gaining self-awareness that becomes torment. RL.9-10.2 covers theme development; Shelley layers Walton's frame, Victor's narrative, and the Creature's testimony to argue knowledge without responsibility destroys. Regents source-based prompts on technology, ethics, and ambition often draw from Frankenstein excerpts.",
