      "topic": "Theme Statements",
      "explanation": "Animal Farm (1945) traces idealistic revolution descending into Stalinist tyranny: the Seven Commandments shrink to 'All animals are equal, but some are more equal than others.' Orwell's epigraph-like ending shows pigs indistinguishable from humans. RL.9-10.2 asks for theme development through details (changing commandments, the windmill, Boxer's fate). Regents source-based arguments on power, propaganda, or revolution use this text frequently.",
