      "correctText": "Motif",
      "topic": "Theme Statements",
      "explanation": "A motif is a recurring image, idea, or element that develops theme. Steinbeck recycles George and Lennie's 'we'll have a little place' speech to mark moments of hope, despair, and finally tragedy when George recites it as he shoots Lennie. RL.9-10.2 asks how a theme develops through specific details; motifs are the prime vehicle. Regents Part 3 source-based arguments on the American Dream typically cite this motif.",
