      "explanation": "Connell's story opens with Rainsford telling Whitney 'The world is made up of two classes—the hunters and the huntees.' By the end, Rainsford has hunted Zaroff and sleeps in his bed. The theme exposes that moral categories collapse under self-preservation. RL.9-10.2 asks how themes develop through specific details. Regents Part 3 source-based prompts on ethics often pair this story with non-fiction on war or survival.",
