      "topic": "Circles and Coordinates",
      "explanation": "The Inscribed Angle Theorem: an inscribed angle equals half its intercepted arc (G-C.2). Arc = 2 × inscribed angle. All inscribed angles intercepting the same arc are congruent. An inscribed angle intercepting a diameter (semicircle, 180°) = 90° — Thales' Theorem (~600 BCE), proved in Euclid's Elements Book III Prop. 31. On NY Geometry Regents, set up the equation angle=(arc)/2 and solve. Confusing central angle (=arc) with inscribed angle (=half arc) is the top circle-unit error.",
