      "correctText": "corresponding vertices",
      "topic": "Congruence Link",
      "explanation": "Corresponding vertices are matched pairs — one on the pre-image, one on the image — related by the transformation. In △ABC ≅ △DEF, vertex A corresponds to D, B to E, and C to F (G-CO.7). On Regents, the transformation notation establishes correspondence: if T maps A→A', B→B', C→C', the congruence statement is △ABC ≅ △A'B'C'. Misidentifying correspondence is a common error. Corresponding sides and angles are congruent for isometries, proportional for dilations.",
