      "correctText": "angle preservation",
      "topic": "Congruence Link",
      "explanation": "Every rigid motion preserves angle measure — the angle at any image vertex equals the angle at the corresponding pre-image vertex (G-CO.2). Dilations also preserve angle measure (but not distance), making similarity the resulting relationship. Angle preservation is why both congruent and similar triangles have equal corresponding angles. On NY Geometry Regents, students cite angle preservation to justify congruent or equal angle pairs in transformation proofs.",
