      "correctText": "composition of transformations",
      "topic": "Congruence Link",
      "explanation": "A composition of transformations applies two or more transformations in sequence; the image of each becomes the pre-image of the next. Notation T₂∘T₁ means apply T₁ first, then T₂ (G-CO.2). Two reflections across parallel lines produce a translation; across intersecting lines, a rotation. On NY Geometry Regents, composition problems ask students to find the final image or identify the single equivalent transformation. The order matters — in general T₂∘T₁ ≠ T₁∘T₂.",
