      "correctText": "copying an angle",
      "topic": "Constructions",
      "explanation": "To copy an angle at a new location: (1) draw a ray for the first side; (2) draw the same-radius arc at both the original and new vertex; (3) transfer the chord distance between the side-crossings on the original to the new arc; (4) draw the ray through the new intersection (G-CO.12). This construction is the foundation for constructing parallel lines by copying alternate interior angles. On Regents, copying-an-angle steps appear in multi-step constructions requiring angle congruence.",
