      "explanation": "A straightedge is an unmarked ruler used in compass-and-straightedge constructions to draw straight lines through compass-established points (G-CO.12). The straightedge cannot measure — it only connects or extends. Combined with a compass it allows all standard constructions. Euclid's Postulate 1 assumes the straightedge (draw a line between two points) and Postulate 3 assumes the compass (draw a circle with given center and radius). On Regents, construction lines must be visible — do not erase them.",
