      "correctText": "angle bisector",
      "topic": "Constructions",
      "explanation": "An angle bisector is a ray from a vertex dividing the angle into two congruent angles. Compass-and-straightedge construction: (1) arc centered at vertex marks two points on the sides; (2) equal arcs from those points find the intersection inside the angle; (3) draw the ray through intersection from vertex (G-CO.12). The angle bisector is the locus of all points equidistant from the two sides. The three angle bisectors of a triangle meet at the incenter, the center of the inscribed circle.",
