      "correctText": "diagonal property",
      "topic": "Coordinate Proofs",
      "explanation": "Diagonal properties are key classification evidence in coordinate proofs (G-GPE.4). A parallelogram's diagonals bisect each other (same midpoint). A rectangle's diagonals are congruent and bisect each other. A rhombus's diagonals are perpendicular bisectors of each other. A square's diagonals are both congruent AND perpendicular bisectors. On NY Geometry Regents, proving a rectangle uses congruent diagonals (distance formula) combined with bisection (midpoint formula showing both diagonals share the same midpoint).",
