      "explanation": "Slope evidence uses the slope formula to establish parallelism (equal slopes) or perpendicularity (negative-reciprocal slopes) between sides (G-GPE.4, G-GPE.5). To prove a parallelogram: equal slopes for opposite sides. To prove a rectangle: also perpendicular adjacent slopes. On NY Geometry Regents Part III and IV, slope evidence is combined with distance evidence. A rectangle needs perpendicular sides (slope) AND congruent diagonals (distance) for a complete proof.",
