      "explanation": "Standard form (x-h)²+(y-k)²=r² is obtained from general form x²+y²+Dx+Ey+F=0 by completing the square on x and y groups (G-GPE.1). On NY Geometry Regents, completing-the-square problems give general form and ask for center and radius. Steps: group x-terms and y-terms, add (D/2)² and (E/2)² to both sides, factor as perfect squares, read center and radius. This algebraic technique was developed by al-Khwarizmi (~820 CE) for solving quadratics.",
