      "correctText": "coordinate radius",
      "topic": "Equations",
      "explanation": "The coordinate radius r is found from (x-h)²+(y-k)²=r² as the square root of the constant on the right (G-GPE.1). If (x-2)²+(y+3)²=49, then r²=49 so r=7. After completing the square from general form, r² is the combined constant. On NY Geometry Regents, students often find r, then verify by substituting a known point. The radius also determines area (πr²) and circumference (2πr), connecting coordinate geometry to measurement formulas.",
