      "explanation": "The center (h,k) is the fixed interior point equidistant from all boundary points, identified from the standard equation (x-h)²+(y-k)²=r² by reading h and k (negating the signs inside the parentheses) (G-GPE.1). From general form x²+y²+Dx+Ey+F=0, the center is found by completing the square on both x and y terms. On NY Geometry Regents, center-finding from an equation is standard. The center is also found geometrically as the intersection of two perpendicular bisectors of chords.",
