      "correctText": "45-45-90 triangle",
      "topic": "Key Ideas",
      "explanation": "A 45-45-90 isosceles right triangle has legs in ratio 1:1 and hypotenuse √2 (G-SRT.8). If each leg is n, the hypotenuse is n√2. From the Pythagorean theorem: n²+n²=c² gives c=n√2. A square's diagonal creates two 45-45-90 triangles. A square with side s has diagonal s√2. Students find missing sides: if hypotenuse is given, divide by √2 (multiply by √2/2). Exact values sin 45°=cos 45°=√2/2 and tan 45°=1 confirm these ratios.",
