      "correctText": "30-60-90 triangle",
      "topic": "Key Ideas",
      "explanation": "A 30-60-90 triangle has sides in ratio 1:√3:2, opposite the 30°, 60°, and 90° angles respectively (G-SRT.8). If the short leg (opposite 30°) is n, the long leg is n√3 and the hypotenuse is 2n. These ratios come from cutting an equilateral triangle in half along an altitude. On NY Geometry Regents, 30-60-90 triangles appear in problems with exact radical answers: hypotenuse 10 → short leg 5, long leg 5√3. Students recall the ratio from the exact values sin 30°=1/2, cos 30°=√3/2.",
