      "correctText": "exact trig value",
      "topic": "Key Ideas",
      "explanation": "Exact trig values are ratios expressed without a calculator: sin 30°=1/2, cos 45°=√2/2, tan 60°=√3 (G-SRT.6). These values come from the 30-60-90 and 45-45-90 triangles and the unit circle. On NY Geometry Regents, multiple-choice items often require recognizing an exact value. Students who memorize the special-angle values for 30°, 45°, 60° answer these quickly. The complementary identity sin θ=cos(90°-θ) extends the list: sin 60°=cos 30°=√3/2.",
