      "correctText": "linear equation",
      "topic": "Lines and Equations",
      "explanation": "A linear equation graphs as a straight line, most commonly in slope-intercept form y=mx+b (G-GPE.5). In Regents coordinate geometry, students write linear equations for medians, altitudes, perpendicular bisectors, and midsegments. The equation passes through a given point with a given slope using y-y₁=m(x-x₁). Descartes (1637) showed every first-degree equation in x and y represents a line, unifying algebraic and geometric representations.",
