      "explanation": "Points equidistant from two fixed points A and B form the perpendicular bisector of AB (G-GPE.5). Points equidistant from two parallel lines form the midway parallel line. Points equidistant from two intersecting lines form both angle bisectors. On NY Geometry Regents, equidistant locus problems identify these sets and write equations. The circumcenter of a triangle is equidistant from all three vertices, making it the center of the circumscribed circle.",
