      "explanation": "A locus is the set of all points satisfying a given geometric condition (G-GPE). Standard loci: equidistant from two fixed points → perpendicular bisector; equidistant from two parallel lines → midway parallel line; fixed distance from a center → circle. On NY Geometry Regents, locus problems describe one or two conditions and ask students to identify the geometric set and write its equation. Compound locus problems combine two conditions — the solution is the intersection of the individual loci.",
