      "correctText": "scale-factor effect",
      "topic": "Measurement Transfer",
      "explanation": "The scale-factor effect: for two similar figures with ratio k, lengths scale by k, areas by k², volumes by k³ (G-SRT.2, G-GMD.3). A cube with side doubled (k=2) has 4 times the surface area and 8 times the volume. On NY Geometry Regents, problems give k and one measurement and ask for the corresponding one in the other figure. Students must identify which tier (length/area/volume) the question asks about before applying the correct power of k.",
