      "correctText": "volume formula",
      "topic": "Measurement Transfer",
      "explanation": "The NY Geometry Regents reference sheet provides volume formulas (G-GMD.3): Prism/Cylinder V=Bh; Pyramid/Cone V=(1/3)Bh; Sphere V=(4/3)πr³. The 1/3 factor distinguishes apex-pointed solids from enclosing prisms/cylinders. Cavalieri's Principle (1635) justifies these for oblique solids. On Regents, compute B first, then multiply. Forgetting the 1/3 factor for pyramids/cones, or using slant height instead of vertical height, are the most common volume errors.",
