      "explanation": "Unit conversion in measurement problems changes between length, area, or volume units using the correct factor (G-MG.1, G-GMD.3). Linear: 1 ft=12 in, 1 yd=3 ft. Area: 1 ft²=144 in² (12²). Volume: 1 ft³=1728 in³ (12³). On NY Geometry Regents, errors occur when students apply the linear factor to area or volume without squaring or cubing it. Dimensions in feet but volume requested in cubic yards: divide cubic feet by 27, not 3.",
