      "explanation": "A composite figure is a 2D or 3D shape built from two or more simpler geometric shapes (G-MG.1, G-GMD.3). To find area: identify and add/subtract component areas. To find volume: decompose into standard solids and sum. On NY Geometry Regents, careful diagram reading identifies the component shapes and dimensions. A silo (cylinder + hemisphere) has V=πr²h + ½·(4/3)πr³. Students label each part, apply the correct formula, and combine results clearly.",
