      "explanation": "The circumference is the distance around a circle: C=2πr=πd (G-C.5). For r=5, C=10π≈31.4. On NY Geometry Regents, circumference appears in arc length problems (arc = fraction of circumference) and in problems about distance a wheel travels per revolution. Archimedes (~250 BCE) bounded π between 223/71 and 22/7 using inscribed and circumscribed 96-gons. William Jones introduced the symbol π in 1706.",
