      "explanation": "Arc length is the distance along a circle's curved edge: L=(θ/360)·2πr, where θ is the central angle in degrees (G-C.5). For a 120° arc in a circle of radius 9: L=(120/360)·18π=6π. On NY Geometry Regents, arc length problems give the radius and central angle; leave answers in terms of π unless a decimal is specified. In radian measure, arc length simplifies to s=rθ — also tested as part of G-C.5.",
