      "explanation": "The area enclosed by a circle is A=πr² (G-C.5, G-MG.1). For r=4, A=16π≈50.3. On NY Geometry Regents, area problems require identifying r, substituting into A=πr², and expressing the answer in terms of π (exact) or as a decimal. Archimedes (~250 BCE) proved A=πr² in Measurement of a Circle using the method of exhaustion. The sector area formula A_sector=(θ/360)πr² partitions the full circle area.",
