      "topic": "Measures",
      "explanation": "The area of a sector (region bounded by two radii and an arc) is A=(θ/360)·πr², where θ is the central angle in degrees (G-C.5). For a 90° central angle in a circle of radius 6: A=(90/360)·π·36=9π. On NY Geometry Regents, sector area problems give the radius and central angle and ask for exact area (in terms of π) or decimal approximation. Sector area is also related to arc length: A=(1/2)·r·s where s is arc length.",
