      "correctText": "measurement tolerance",
      "topic": "Model Assumptions",
      "explanation": "Measurement tolerance is the allowable range of variation — e.g., diameter 5 cm ±0.1 cm means 4.9 to 5.1 cm is acceptable (G-MG.2, G-MG.3). In manufacturing and engineering, tolerances ensure parts fit despite inevitable small measurement errors. On NY Geometry Regents, tolerance appears in modeling problems where students determine if a measurement falls within an acceptable range. Absolute error = |actual − nominal|; relative error = absolute error / nominal value, expressed as a percent.",
