      "explanation": "A diagram assumption is a property — right angle, parallelism, congruence — accepted as given from a figure's markings without additional proof (G-MG.1, G-CO.9). In NY Geometry Regents diagrams, a small square = right angle, tick marks = congruent sides/angles, arrows = parallel lines. Students may assume only what is explicitly marked; they may not assume a segment is a diameter just because it appears to pass through the center unless labeled or given. Reading every diagram marking accurately is foundational.",
