      "explanation": "The maximum area problem asks for the largest area achievable under a given perimeter constraint (G-MG.3). Result: among all rectangles with fixed perimeter P, the square maximizes area (side=P/4, area=P²/16). Among all figures with a fixed perimeter, the circle encloses maximum area (Isoperimetric Inequality, proved by Jacob Steiner in the 1830s). On NY Geometry Regents, students express area as a function of one variable, find the vertex of the resulting parabola, and state the maximum.",
