      "topic": "Proof Language",
      "explanation": "The given statement opens a two-column proof, listing all information stated in the problem as true. Every subsequent step must trace back to the given statements or previously proved theorems (G-CO.9). On NY Geometry Regents, students lose credit for citing information as given that was not stated in the problem. The given statement establishes the starting point; the logical chain from given to prove is the essence of Euclidean deductive proof, formalized in Euclid's Elements (~300 BCE) as the model for rigorous mathematical argument.",
