      "explanation": "The prove statement names the conclusion that a two-column proof must establish through a logical chain of statements and reasons. It appears at the top of the proof alongside the given statement (G-CO.9, G-CO.10). On NY Geometry Regents, 3- and 6-credit proof questions state 'Prove: [conclusion]' and students must reach that exact statement as the final line. A common error is stopping one step short. The prove statement determines which theorems are relevant — students work backward from it to plan the proof strategy.",
