      "correctText": "theorem match",
      "topic": "Regents Explanation",
      "explanation": "Theorem matching is selecting the correct named theorem to justify a specific proof step (G-CO.9, G-CO.10). On NY Geometry Regents, the reason column requires the exact name: 'Vertical Angles Theorem,' 'Base Angles Theorem,' 'Pythagorean Theorem,' 'Corresponding Angles Postulate.' Writing a description instead of the name may receive credit but is risky. Students should build a reference list of theorem names and precise conditions to cite accurately under exam conditions.",
      "domain": "Review",
