      "correctText": "slope formula",
      "topic": "Slope Reasoning",
      "explanation": "The slope formula m=(y₂-y₁)/(x₂-x₁) gives the rate of vertical change per unit of horizontal change for a non-vertical line (G-GPE.5). Positive slope rises left to right; negative falls; zero is horizontal; undefined is vertical. On NY Geometry Regents, slope is central to coordinate proofs of parallel lines (equal slopes), perpendicular lines (negative-reciprocal slopes), and writing line equations. Descartes's 1637 system implicitly used slope; the modern formula was formalized with the development of calculus (Newton and Leibniz, 1680s).",
