      "explanation": "A regular polygon has all sides congruent and all interior angles congruent. A regular n-gon has n lines of symmetry and rotational symmetry of order n (G-CO.3). Interior angle measure = 180(n-2)/n; each central angle = 360°/n. Area = (1/2)ap where a is the apothem and p is the perimeter (G-MG.1). Euclid's Elements (~300 BCE, Books IV and XIII) showed how to construct regular polygons with compass and straightedge, proving the regular pentagon and linking them to the five Platonic solids.",
