      "correctText": "cross product",
      "topic": "Turning Points",
      "explanation": "The Cross Products Property: if a/b = c/d, then ad = bc (product of means equals product of extremes). This is the primary algebraic tool for solving proportion equations from similar triangles (G-SRT.5). On NY Geometry Regents, students apply cross products to find missing side lengths: e.g., if 6/x = 9/15, then 9x=90, so x=10. The property follows from multiplying both sides of the proportion by bd. Cross products also appear in segment-length problems involving secants and chords.",
