      "explanation": "An endangered species is one at serious risk of extinction throughout all or a significant portion of its range. The U.S. Endangered Species Act (1973) provides legal protection — banning hunting and trade and requiring habitat protection — and has helped recover species like the bald eagle, California condor, and Florida manatee. The IUCN Red List categorizes species globally from Least Concern to Critically Endangered to Extinct. Currently endangered species include the giant panda, mountain gorilla, Sumatran tiger, Amur leopard, vaquita porpoise, and many more. Causes include habitat loss, poaching, climate change, and disease. NY Living Environment Regents Part B uses endangered species in conservation questions.",
