      "explanation": "Habitat loss is the destruction or significant alteration of the natural environment a species needs to survive. Drivers include conversion of forests, wetlands, and grasslands to cropland and pasture; urban and suburban expansion; mining; road construction; and dam-building. Habitat loss is the leading driver of biodiversity loss globally — the IUCN estimates it threatens 85% of species at risk of extinction. Tropical deforestation alone is wiping out countless species, many never even described. Once habitat is gone, species cannot survive there no matter how much we protect them elsewhere. NY Living Environment Regents Part B uses habitat loss in conservation, biodiversity, and human-impact questions.",
