      "explanation": "Biomagnification is the increase in toxin concentration at each successive trophic level of a food chain. Each consumer eats many prey, each carrying some toxin; the toxin accumulates in the consumer at a higher concentration than in any single prey. Top predators end up with the highest concentrations — often millions of times the surrounding water. DDT biomagnification (documented by Rachel Carson in Silent Spring, 1962) caused bald eagle, peregrine falcon, and brown pelican populations to crash from thin eggshells; DDT was banned in the U.S. in 1972 and these species recovered. Mercury still biomagnifies in fish, leading to human exposure. NY Living Environment Regents Part B uses biomagnification.",
