      "explanation": "Osmosis is a special case of diffusion — water moving across a selectively permeable membrane down its concentration gradient. In a hypotonic solution (less solute outside than inside the cell), water flows into the cell; animal cells swell and can burst, while plant cells become turgid. In a hypertonic solution (more solute outside), water flows out; cells shrink (crenate in animals, plasmolyze in plants). In an isotonic solution, water moves in and out equally. NY Living Environment Regents Part B regularly tests osmosis with diagrams of red blood cells or Elodea cells in different solutions and asks students to predict the direction of water movement.",
