      "correctText": "variation source",
      "topic": "Exam Misconceptions",
      "explanation": "Sources of genetic variation: (1) Mutation — random changes in DNA sequence, the ultimate source of new alleles; (2) Sexual reproduction with crossing over in prophase I of meiosis, where homologous chromosomes exchange segments and create new allele combinations; (3) Independent assortment in metaphase I of meiosis, where each homologous pair lines up randomly; (4) Random fertilization, where any of millions of sperm can fertilize any egg. Variation is the raw material on which natural selection acts — without variation, no evolution. NY Living Environment Regents Part B routinely asks students to identify a source of variation in a Punnett-square or pedigree problem.",
