      "explanation": "A receptor is a cell or molecular structure that detects a specific stimulus and converts it into a signal the body can interpret. Sensory receptors include photoreceptors in the retina (light), mechanoreceptors in the skin (touch, pressure), chemoreceptors in taste buds and the nose (chemicals), thermoreceptors in skin and the brain (temperature), and pain receptors (tissue damage). At the molecular level, hormones bind to specific protein receptors on cell membranes, triggering specific responses. Without receptors, organisms could not detect or respond to internal or external changes. NY Living Environment Regents Part B uses receptors in feedback-loop diagrams: the receptor detects the change, sending signal to effector.",
