      "correctText": "biotechnology evidence",
      "topic": "Genes to Traits",
      "explanation": "Biotechnology provides evidence and applications across many fields. DNA fingerprinting (developed by Alec Jeffreys 1984) compares DNA profiles in forensic identification, paternity testing, and finding wrongfully convicted people. Cloning (Dolly the sheep, 1996) demonstrates that adult cells contain all the DNA needed for development. CRISPR-Cas9 (Doudna and Charpentier, Nobel Prize 2020) allows precise gene editing, with applications in treating sickle-cell disease, inherited blindness, and certain cancers. Genetic engineering produces human insulin in bacteria, Bt corn that resists pests, golden rice that produces vitamin A. Each biotechnology has benefits and ethical/safety tradeoffs. NY Living Environment Regents Part B tests biotechnology applications.",
