      "correctText": "probability",
      "topic": "Pedigrees and Probability",
      "explanation": "Probability is the likelihood of an event, expressed from 0 (impossible) to 1 (certain), or as a percentage. In genetics, Punnett squares predict probabilities of offspring genotypes and phenotypes: a Tt x Tt cross gives 3/4 (75%) tall and 1/4 (25%) short. Probabilities are statistical predictions — actual offspring numbers can differ from expectations, especially with small sample sizes (a single Tt x Tt cross might produce 4 tall and 0 short or vice versa). The probability of each independent event in a sequence multiplies (e.g., 1/4 x 1/4 = 1/16 for two affected children). NY Living Environment Regents Part B routinely tests this.",
