      "topic": "Regents Risk Factors",
      "explanation": "The menstrual cycle is roughly 28 days long, regulated by an interaction between the hypothalamus, pituitary, and ovaries. The ovarian cycle has three phases: follicular (FSH causes a follicle to mature), ovulation around day 14 (LH surge releases an egg), and luteal (progesterone from the corpus luteum prepares the uterine lining). The uterine cycle parallels this: the endometrium thickens, then either supports an embryo or sheds (menstruation, days 1-5). If fertilization occurs, hCG from the embryo maintains the corpus luteum and progesterone keeps the lining intact. NY Living Environment Regents Part B uses menstrual-cycle diagrams in human reproduction questions.",
