      "explanation": "Budding is a form of asexual reproduction in which a new organism develops as an outgrowth (a bud) of the parent. The parent's cells mitotically divide to form the bud, which eventually separates as a genetically identical individual. Yeast (Saccharomyces) bud microscopically and rapidly. Hydra (a small freshwater cnidarian) buds visibly under a microscope, a favorite classroom demonstration. Some plants (kalanchoe, ginger) bud at leaf margins or rhizomes. NY Living Environment Regents Part B uses budding diagrams and asks students to identify it as a form of asexual reproduction and to predict the genetic relationship between parent and offspring (identical).",
