      "topic": "Reproductive Strategies",
      "explanation": "Regeneration is the regrowth of lost or damaged body parts. Some animals can regenerate entire limbs or whole bodies (planaria flatworms cut into pieces will each grow into a complete worm; salamanders regrow limbs and tails; starfish regrow arms — and sometimes a single starfish arm with part of the central disc can regrow the whole starfish). In humans, regeneration is more limited: skin heals, liver tissue can regrow substantially, but most other tissues form scar tissue rather than replace lost cells. Stem-cell biology aims to improve human regenerative capacity. NY Living Environment Regents Part B uses regeneration as an example of asexual reproduction in some species and tissue repair in others.",
