      "correctText": "deforestation",
      "topic": "Resource Use",
      "explanation": "Deforestation is the large-scale removal of forest cover. Major drivers include conversion to agriculture (palm-oil plantations in Southeast Asia, cattle ranching and soy production in the Amazon), commercial logging, mining, and urban expansion. Effects include loss of biodiversity (tropical forests hold over half of land-species diversity), increased atmospheric CO2 (forests are major carbon stores; burning them releases that carbon), soil erosion, disrupted water cycles, and displacement of indigenous communities. The Amazon, Congo Basin, and Indonesian rainforests are losing area at alarming rates. NY Living Environment Regents Part B uses deforestation in climate change, biodiversity, and human-impact questions.",
