      "explanation": "An Environmental Impact Statement (EIS) is a detailed document, required under the U.S. National Environmental Policy Act (NEPA, 1970), that assesses the likely environmental effects of major proposed government actions or projects — pipelines, dams, highways, mines, large developments. The EIS describes the project, the existing environment, expected effects (on air, water, wildlife, human communities), alternative approaches, and ways to reduce harm (mitigation). Public comment and review are required. NY also has its own State Environmental Quality Review Act (SEQRA, 1975) covering state and local projects. NY Living Environment Regents Part B uses EISs in environmental policy and human-impact questions.",
