      "correctText": "recycling",
      "topic": "Solutions and Tradeoffs",
      "explanation": "Recycling is the collection, processing, and reuse of waste materials to make new products — paper, aluminum cans, steel, glass, certain plastics, electronics. Aluminum recycling saves about 95% of the energy needed to make new aluminum from bauxite ore. Recycled paper saves trees, water, and landfill space. Glass and steel can be recycled indefinitely without loss of quality. Plastic recycling is more limited — only some types (PET #1, HDPE #2) are widely recycled; many plastics are downcycled or end up as waste. Recycling reduces but does not eliminate environmental impact — the best strategy is reduce first, reuse second, recycle third. NY Living Environment Regents Part B uses recycling in sustainability questions.",
