      "explanation": "An organ system is a group of organs cooperating to carry out a major life function. The human body has 11 organ systems: integumentary (skin), skeletal, muscular, nervous, endocrine, cardiovascular/circulatory, lymphatic/immune, respiratory, digestive, urinary/excretory, reproductive. Organ systems interact to maintain homeostasis — for example, the respiratory and circulatory systems work together to deliver oxygen to every cell. NY Living Environment Regents Part B regularly tests organ-system interactions in homeostasis questions: 'Describe how two organ systems work together to maintain stable internal conditions during exercise' is a classic CRQ-style item.",
