      "explanation": "The circulatory (cardiovascular) system has three main components: the heart (a four-chambered muscular pump), blood vessels (arteries, arterioles, capillaries, venules, veins), and blood. It moves oxygen from the lungs to every cell, nutrients from the digestive tract to every cell, hormones from glands to target cells, immune cells throughout the body, heat to maintain body temperature, and wastes (CO2, urea) to the lungs and kidneys for excretion. Humans have a closed double-loop circulation — one loop to the lungs (pulmonary) and one to the rest of the body (systemic). NY Living Environment Regents Part B uses circulation in homeostasis and gas-exchange questions.",
