      "topic": "Decimal Operations",
      "explanation": "A decimal is a base-10 representation of a rational number with digits to the right of the decimal point. NYS Grade 7 Math standard 7.NS.2.D explicitly tests converting fractions to decimals using long division. Terminating decimals end (0.5, 0.75, 0.125); repeating decimals have a pattern that recurs (0.333... = 1/3; 0.1428571... = 1/7). All rationals are either terminating or repeating decimals; irrationals like π and √2 are non-terminating, non-repeating. State-test items test conversion between fraction and decimal, comparison of decimals (use place value), and operations preserving decimal precision.",
