      "explanation": "Apply the distributive property: 3(2x − 5) = 3 × 2x + 3 × (−5) = 6x − 15. NYS Grade 7 Math standard 7.EE.1 explicitly tests distribution. Worked variations: 4(x + 3) = 4x + 12; −2(x + 4) = −2x − 8 (negative distributes to both terms); 1/2 (4x + 6) = 2x + 3. State-test items test the distributive property with positive and negative multipliers, fractions, and decimals. Common error: forgetting to distribute to the second term, or losing signs on negative distribution. Always multiply outside number by EVERY term inside parentheses with appropriate signs.",
