      "explanation": "To factor: find GCF of all terms, divide each term by GCF, write as GCF × remaining. NYS Grade 7 Math standard 7.EE.1 explicitly tests factoring (reverse of distribution). Worked example: 8x + 12: GCF(8, 12) = 4; divide each term by 4: 8x/4 = 2x; 12/4 = 3; factored: 4(2x + 3). Check by expanding: 4(2x + 3) = 8x + 12 ✓. State-test items test linear factoring with positive coefficients (most common) and mixed signs. Factoring is the inverse of distribution; both operations are essential algebraic skills that appear throughout Grade 7 and prepare students for full algebra in Grade 8.",
