      "correctText": "Sample-based estimate",
      "topic": "Estimation + Prediction",
      "explanation": "A sample-based estimate uses sample data to predict a population characteristic—the sample mean estimates the population mean, sample proportion estimates population proportion. NYS Grade 7 Math standard 7.SP.2 explicitly tests sample-based estimation. Worked example: if 18 of 60 randomly sampled people are left-handed, the sample proportion is 0.30, so we estimate 30% of the population is left-handed. State-test items test sample-based estimation in proportional contexts: 'A random sample of 80 students shows 24 prefer green. How many of the 2,000 students would prefer green?' Setup: 24/80 = x/2000; cross-multiply 80x = 48,000; divide x = 600. Always show the proportional reasoning explicitly.",
