      "topic": "Angles + Parallel Lines",
      "explanation": "The AA (Angle-Angle) similarity criterion: if TWO pairs of corresponding angles in two triangles are EQUAL, the triangles are SIMILAR. NYS Common Core Grade 8 standard 8.G.A.5 + 8.G.A.4 test the AA similarity criterion. The third pair of angles must also be equal (since triangle angles sum to 180°), but only two pairs need to be checked. Worked example: triangle with angles 60°, 70°, 50° and triangle with angles 60°, 70°, ? — the third angle must be 50°, so the triangles are similar by AA. State-test items test AA criterion as the simplest similarity test: given two angle pairs, conclude similarity; or given similarity, deduce that corresponding angles are equal. AA is the most-used similarity criterion in Grade 8 and Algebra/Geometry contexts.",
