      "topic": "Angles + Parallel Lines",
      "explanation": "When a transversal crosses two parallel lines, SAME-SIDE INTERIOR ANGLES (also called co-interior angles) are SUPPLEMENTARY — they sum to 180°. NYS Common Core Grade 8 standard 8.G.A.5 explicitly tests angle relationships from parallel lines and transversals. Worked example: if same-side interior angles are 110° and x, then 110 + x = 180, so x = 70°. Distinguish from alternate interior angles (EQUAL, not supplementary) and corresponding angles (EQUAL). State-test items test angle relationships heavily: identifying which pairs are equal vs supplementary, and computing missing angles. The relationships derive from Euclid's parallel postulate (around 300 BC) and are foundational for proving facts about parallelograms, trapezoids, and other polygons.",
