      "explanation": "The square root of 2 equals 1.41421356... It is the most famous irrational number — the Pythagoreans discovered around 500 BC that the diagonal of a unit square has length sqrt(2), and they proved it cannot be expressed as a fraction. NYS Common Core Grade 8 standard 8.NS.A.2 explicitly tests approximating irrational numbers — comparing the size of irrationals, locating them approximately on a number line, and estimating the value of expressions like pi^2. Worked example: since 1^2 = 1 and 2^2 = 4, sqrt(2) is between 1 and 2; since 1.4^2 = 1.96 and 1.5^2 = 2.25, sqrt(2) is between 1.4 and 1.5; refining further: 1.41^2 = 1.9881, 1.42^2 = 2.0164, so sqrt(2) is approximately 1.41.",
