      "correctText": "Exponential nonlinear",
      "topic": "Real-World Data",
      "explanation": "A graph where y = 2^x (or any exponential expression a^x) is NONLINEAR — specifically, EXPONENTIAL. NYS Common Core Grade 8 standard 8.F.A.3 distinguishes linear vs. nonlinear functions, with exponential being the canonical nonlinear example. Worked example: y = 2^x has values y(0)=1, y(1)=2, y(2)=4, y(3)=8 — doubling each time. This is the characteristic exponential growth: rapid increase, much faster than linear. State-test items test recognition: linear (line/constant rate) vs. nonlinear (curve/changing rate). Real-world examples of exponential association: bacteria growth, compound interest, population growth (in early phases), viral spread. Grade 8 recognizes nonlinear patterns informally; fitting exponential models is for Algebra 1 and beyond.",
