      "explanation": "Different row percentages in a two-way table suggest ASSOCIATION between the variables. If 'plays sports' has 80% pet owners and 'no sports' has 40% pet owners, the difference (80% vs. 40%) suggests pet ownership and sports participation are associated. NYS Common Core Grade 8 standard 8.SP.A.4 tests this. The direction of association (positive: more sports → more pets) requires interpretation in context. State-test items present two-way tables and ask whether association exists by comparing row or column relative frequencies. Importantly, association does NOT prove CAUSATION: maybe pet-owners exercise more by walking dogs (suggesting pets cause sports), or maybe athletic families also adopt pets (suggesting other factors). Grade 8 discusses qualitatively; causal inference is for higher grades.",
