      "explanation": "In a line of best fit for height (x in cm) vs. shoe size (y), slope = 0.4 means 'for each 1 cm increase in height, the predicted shoe size increases by 0.4 (units of shoe size).' NYS Common Core Grade 8 standard 8.SP.A.3 tests slope interpretation in real contexts. Worked example: if a student is 10 cm taller than another, the predicted shoe size is 10 × 0.4 = 4 sizes larger. State-test items test slope interpretation extensively — students must connect the numerical slope to the unit-rate interpretation in the real-world context (e.g., 'per cm,' 'per year,' 'per dollar').",
