      "correctText": "Reflection",
      "topic": "Rigid Transformations",
      "explanation": "A REFLECTION flips a figure over a LINE (the line of reflection), creating a mirror image. NYS Common Core Grade 8 standard 8.G.A.1 + 8.G.A.3 test reflections, especially over the x-axis, y-axis, and lines y = x or y = -x. Notation: reflection over x-axis maps (x, y) → (x, -y); over y-axis maps (x, y) → (-x, y); over y = x maps (x, y) → (y, x). Worked example: reflecting point (3, 4) over x-axis gives (3, -4); over y-axis gives (-3, 4); over y = x gives (4, 3). State-test items test reflections on the coordinate plane, including identifying images, writing rules, and recognizing that reflections preserve distance and angle but REVERSE orientation (clockwise becomes counterclockwise).",
