      "explanation": "A scatter plot with NO CLEAR upward or downward trend shows NO ASSOCIATION — x and y are not linearly related. NYS Common Core Grade 8 standard 8.SP.A.1 tests this case alongside positive and negative association. Worked example: a scatter plot of shoe size (x) vs. test score (y) typically shows no association — the variables are independent. State-test items test recognition of no-association patterns: points scattered randomly with no visible trend. Note: 'no association' usually means no LINEAR association; there could still be a nonlinear pattern (curve, cluster). Grade 8 typically uses 'no association' to mean 'no visible trend.' Important: absence of association in a sample does not prove independence in the population (statistical inference is for higher grades).",
