      "topic": "Statistics Recap",
      "explanation": "A scatter plot where Y DECREASES as X INCREASES shows NEGATIVE association — variables move in OPPOSITE directions. NYS Common Core Grade 8 standard 8.SP.A.1 tests patterns of association: positive (rising), negative (falling), none, linear (line-like), nonlinear. Worked example: age of car (x) vs. resale value (y) typically shows negative association — older cars are worth less. Other negative-association examples: exercise hours vs. body fat percentage; temperature vs. heating bill (when temp goes up, heating bill goes down); time studying vs. error count on a test. State-test items test recognition of negative-association patterns from scatter plots and word descriptions. Distinguish strength: weak (loosely scattered along downward trend) vs. strong (tightly clustered). Critical for understanding bivariate data relationships.",
