      "topic": "Two-Way Tables",
      "explanation": "When ROW PERCENTAGES (or column percentages) are EQUAL across all categories of the other variable, there is NO association — the variables are independent in this dataset. NYS Common Core Grade 8 standard 8.SP.A.4 tests this concept. Worked example: if 50% of pet-owners play sports AND 50% of non-pet-owners play sports, pet ownership does not affect sport participation rates — no association. State-test items test 'is there association?' by checking whether the conditional proportions vary or stay the same. Equal proportions = independence (no association); different proportions = association. The level of difference indicates strength of association: small differences (50% vs 52%) = weak association; large differences (80% vs 30%) = strong association. Foundational for chi-square independence testing in higher grades.",
