      "explanation": "Time interval t = t_f - t_i represents the duration over which displacement, velocity change, or acceleration is being measured. SI unit is the second. In the kinematics equation d = v_i·t + (1/2)at^2, t is the elapsed time from when v_i was the velocity, not the absolute clock time. A common Regents trap is asking for the time to fall from rest through a given distance, requiring d = (1/2)gt^2 solved for t = sqrt(2d/g). For a vertical throw, the up-time equals the down-time to the same height (Galilean symmetry), so total flight time is twice the time to reach peak: t_total = 2·v_i/g. Students must read the problem carefully to identify which segment of motion the requested time refers to.",
