      "explanation": "A mixture is two or more substances physically combined without chemically bonding, so each substance keeps its own properties and the mixture can be separated by physical means like filtering, settling, or magnetism. Examples include trail mix, sand and gravel, and salad. Robert Boyle distinguished mixtures from compounds in his 1661 book The Sceptical Chymist. NYS Grade 5 Standard 5-PS1-4 expects students to conduct investigations to determine whether mixing two or more substances results in new substances.",
