      "correctText": "Motion",
      "topic": "Motion Patterns",
      "explanation": "Motion is the change in an object's position relative to a reference point over time. A walking student, a rolling ball, and a spinning Earth are all in motion. Motion can be measured as distance and time, which lets us calculate speed. Aristotle was the first to write systematically about motion around 350 BCE, though Galileo and Newton corrected his ideas. NYS Grade 5 reviewing Grade 3 NGSS 3-PS2-1 and 3-PS2-2 expects students to describe and predict patterns of an object's motion under the effects of forces.",
