      "correctText": "Friction",
      "topic": "Motion Patterns",
      "explanation": "Friction is a force that resists motion between two surfaces in contact. Rough surfaces produce more friction than smooth ones. Friction slows a bicycle, lets your shoes grip the floor, and warms your hands when you rub them together. Without friction, you could not walk. Leonardo da Vinci sketched the first friction studies in the 1490s, and Charles-Augustin de Coulomb established friction laws in 1781. NYS Grade 5 (reviewing 3-PS2-1) expects students to model friction as a force affecting motion.",
