      "correctText": "Inertia",
      "topic": "Motion Patterns",
      "explanation": "Inertia is the tendency of an object to keep doing what it is already doing: staying still if at rest, or moving in a straight line at constant speed if moving. Objects with more mass have more inertia and are harder to start or stop. A bowling ball is harder to push than a soccer ball. Sir Isaac Newton named inertia in 1687, building on Galileo's earlier work. NYS Grade 5 reviewing 3-PS2-1 expects students to predict motion based on forces, and inertia (and Newton's First Law) is a top extension idea.",
