      "correctText": "Filtration",
      "topic": "Particle Model",
      "explanation": "Filtration is a physical separation method that uses a porous material (paper, screen, or sand) to trap larger particles while letting smaller ones (and liquids) pass through. Long Island's water-treatment plants filter sand and gravel before sending drinking water to homes. Robert Hooke described early laboratory filtration in 1665. NYS Grade 5 Standard 5-PS1-4 expects students to investigate whether mixing substances forms new substances, and separating a mixture by filtration shows that the original substances were not changed, confirming it is a mixture.",
