      "correctText": "Chemical energy",
      "topic": "Plants Make Food",
      "explanation": "Chemical energy is energy stored in the bonds of molecules like sugars, fats, and proteins. Plants store sunlight as chemical energy in glucose, and animals release that energy through respiration to power movement, growth, and heat. Antoine Lavoisier showed in the 1780s that breathing and burning both release the same kind of energy from food and fuel. NYS Grade 5 Standard 5-PS3-1 expects students to describe that the energy in food comes originally from the Sun and was stored as chemical energy by green plants.",
