      "topic": "Water Cycle",
      "explanation": "Runoff is rain or snowmelt that flows downhill across the surface, eventually reaching streams, rivers, and oceans. It carries soil, fertilizer, and pollutants from the land, which is why fertilizer runoff into Long Island's Great South Bay can cause harmful algae blooms. About 30% of all precipitation becomes runoff. Robert Horton developed runoff equations in 1933. NYS Grade 5 Standard 5-ESS2-1 includes runoff as part of the water cycle model and 5-ESS3-1 expects students to think about how communities can protect water resources from runoff pollution.",
