      "topic": "Circulatory System",
      "explanation": "The human heart is a fist-sized four-chambered muscular pump that beats about 100,000 times per day (35 million per year), moving 7,500 liters of blood. William Harvey demonstrated in 1628 that blood circulates in a closed loop rather than being consumed by tissues, overturning 1,400 years of Galen's medicine. The four chambers (two atria, two ventricles) are separated by valves. NYS Grade 6 Science (NGSS MS-LS1-3) requires students to identify the heart as the circulatory pump, name its chambers, and explain how it moves oxygen-rich and oxygen-poor blood separately.",
