      "explanation": "Defining the problem is the first step in any engineering design process: state what the problem is, who has it, and why it matters. NGSS MS-ETS1-1 requires that students 'define the criteria and constraints' clearly before designing anything. Henry Petroski's 1985 book To Engineer Is Human emphasizes that most engineering failures trace back to poorly defined problems. NYS Grade 6 Science requires students to write a one-sentence problem statement, identify stakeholders, and distinguish a real engineering problem (a need) from a wish.",
