      "correctText": "10 percent",
      "topic": "Food Webs",
      "explanation": "The 10% rule, formalized by Raymond Lindeman in his landmark 1942 paper The Trophic-Dynamic Aspect of Ecology, states that only about 10% of the energy stored at one trophic level transfers to the next. The other 90% is lost as heat (cellular respiration) and used for movement, growth, and waste. This is why food chains rarely exceed 4-5 levels and why apex predators (sharks, eagles, big cats) require huge hunting ranges. NYS Grade 6 Science (NGSS MS-LS2-3) requires students to apply the 10% rule and credit Lindeman 1942.",
