      "explanation": "Isaac Newton (1643-1727), English physicist and Lucasian Professor at Cambridge, published Philosophiae Naturalis Principia Mathematica in 1687—the most influential physics book ever written—deriving three laws of motion and the law of universal gravitation F = G m1 m2 / r^2. He showed that the same force pulling an apple down ALSO holds the Moon in orbit. Newton co-invented calculus (with Leibniz) and built the first reflecting telescope. NYS Grade 6 Science (NGSS MS-ESS1-3) requires crediting Newton 1687 with the gravitational law.",
