      "correctText": "Organism",
      "topic": "Levels of Organization",
      "explanation": "An organism is one complete, independent living being. A single-celled bacterium and a 30-meter blue whale are both organisms because each carries out all life processes (homeostasis, metabolism, growth, reproduction, response). The full hierarchy is cell -> tissue -> organ -> organ system -> organism. Above the organism level are population, community, ecosystem, biome, and biosphere. NYS Grade 6 Science (NGSS MS-LS1-3) requires students to order all five levels from cell to organism and recognize that emergent properties (like consciousness or motion) appear at the organism level but not at any single lower level.",
