      "explanation": "Balanced forces are equal in magnitude and opposite in direction, producing zero net force and no change in motion (Newton's First Law). A book resting on a table has gravity (downward) balanced by normal force (upward). Skydivers reaching terminal velocity have gravity balanced by air resistance, falling at constant speed (~53 m/s). The Hoover Dam (built 1931-36) holds back Lake Mead's 35 million acre-feet by balancing water pressure with the dam's massive structure. Statics—the study of bodies in balanced forces—dates to Archimedes (~250 BCE) and underlies all civil engineering. NYS Grade 7 Science exams contrast balanced (no motion change) with unbalanced (acceleration).",
