      "explanation": "Newton's Third Law states that for every action, there is an equal and opposite reaction—forces always occur in pairs acting on different objects. Newton formulated this in 1687. A rocket lifting off exemplifies this: the rocket pushes exhaust gases downward (action), and the gases push the rocket upward (reaction)—the same principle behind Robert Goddard's first liquid-fueled rocket (1926) and the Saturn V (1967-73) lifting astronauts to the Moon. Walking depends on the third law: feet push back on the ground, ground pushes forward on feet. A swimmer pushes water back, water pushes swimmer forward. NYS Grade 7 Science exams test action-reaction with rockets, jumping, swimming.",
