      "explanation": "Civil liberties are constitutional protections shielding individuals from government overreach—freedom of speech, religion, press, assembly, petition (1st), unreasonable searches (4th), self-incrimination and due process (5th), speedy trial and counsel (6th), and cruel punishment (8th). They limit what government may do even with popular majority support. PIG students must distinguish civil liberties (freedom from government action) from civil rights (government-guaranteed equal treatment), and understand that courts calibrate limits on civil liberties using tiers of constitutional scrutiny.",
